;;-*-Lisp-*-
(in-package goal)

;; jak-hd-physics.gc — Grecharged-secondary-motion: verlet/spring secondary-motion chains on the
;; HD companion skeletons (jiggle, hair, beards, straps, dangling accessories).
;;
;; PRINCIPLE (spring-toward-the-animated-target). fill-jak-hd-bones! (jak-hd.gc) overwrites every
;; HD joint's WORLD matrix each frame from the driver's animation. This pass runs IMMEDIATELY AFTER
;; that fill inside the same do-joint-math!: for each configured chain joint the freshly retargeted
;; matrix is the TARGET (the authored rest pose of this frame); the sim carries a verlet point per
;; joint (pos + prev) integrated with a spring toward the target plus gravity, then constraint
;; iterations (distance to parent from the LIVE target lengths — correct under any rig scale —,
;; swing-cone limit around the target direction, body collisions), then writes the joint matrix back
;; as: 3x3 rows post-multiplied by the minimal swing rotation (target-dir -> sim-dir; row lengths
;; preserved, so non-unit rig scales like Keira's 0.103 straps survive) and translation row =
;; simulated position. With zero excitation the spring converges to the target exactly -> subtle by
;; construction; physics OFF = pass skipped = bit-exact stock-HD.
;;
;; ================================ CYCLE 2 (owner verdict 16:40 + 17:35) =========================
;; (A) FAKE WIND vs PHYSICS — jak1 ALREADY animates straps / hair / cloth with authored pseudo-wind
;;     channels. Springing toward that target left TWO writers on the same bone: double motion, and
;;     Jak's blue cloth clipping. FIX = per-chain `anim` mode. `replace` (the default) RE-GLUES the
;;     chain to its BIND-POSE local transforms carried by the animated anchor BEFORE the targets are
;;     cached — i.e. the authored channel delta on a physics-owned joint is discarded and the sim is
;;     the only source of secondary motion. `excite` re-glues too but feeds the discarded authored
;;     delta back in as an input FORCE (never a second write). `keep` = the old behaviour.
;;     The re-glue is exactly fill-jak-hd-bones!'s mode-2 GLUE product, W'_k = L'_k . W'_par with
;;     L'_k = inv(bind-pose[k]) . bind-pose[par] (bind-pose slots STORE the inverse bind).
;; (B) HAIR ANCHORING — "the whole hair moves, as if detached from the skull". The chain ROOT was a
;;     free sim link. FIX = `rootlock=N`: the first N links ride the animated bone RIGIDLY (no
;;     integration, no constraint, NO write-back — the re-glued rest matrix stands), plus
;;     `gradient=G`, a root->tip freedom ramp that makes the first free links stiffer with a tighter
;;     swing cone and leaves the full amplitude to the tips.
;; (C) CHEST — see the params file: the cone/stretch limits were clipping the bounce.
;; (D) ACCESSORIES — goggles &co are chains like any other; class is a COST tier, not a hierarchy.
;; (17:35) COLLIDERS — a real body volume, not 1-2 symbolic spheres: `capsule A B radius=R` swept
;;     volumes following two animated bones, per-chain filters, `tier=` so a lower precision level
;;     thins the set without ever letting a chain pass visibly through the body, contact FRICTION
;;     (the push-out impulse is absorbed into `prev`, killing contact jitter) and a RESIDUAL
;;     PENETRATION counter measured after the last iteration — the owner's bar is resid=0.
;;
;; ================================ CYCLE 3 (owner verdict 2026-08-06 07:40) =====================
;; (A) AUTHORED ANIMATION HAS PRIORITY. ND sometimes DRIVES a secondary bone on purpose — Jak's
;;     ears reacting, Keira GRABBING her goggles and pulling them over her eyes. That is authored
;;     intent, not fake physics, and `anim=replace` was throwing it away. Fix = per chain
;;     `authored=T`: each frame the re-glue already knows the authored world offset it is about to
;;     discard; expressed as a fraction of the chain's own length that IS the "is the animator
;;     driving this?" signal. Above T (hysteresis at T/2) a blend weight w ramps to 1 at
;;     `authrise=` per second: the TARGET becomes the authored pose, stiffness is multiplied by
;;     `authstiff=`, gravity and excitation fade out and the chain stops colliding (the animator's
;;     pose wins, exactly as owner-specified). When the authored motion stops, w ramps back down at
;;     `authfall=` per second and physics RESUMES PROGRESSIVELY from where it is — the target slides
;;     back to the calm rest pose, so there is no snap by construction. Counters: engage/release
;;     events, held chain-frames, max blend.
;; (B) SPAWN AND BIG TRANSITIONS. Chains "went wild" at spawn and on hard pose cuts. Per chain the
;;     anchor's one-frame travel is watched: past max(PHYS-JUMP-ABS, 1.5x chain length) it is a
;;     teleport/cut, not motion, so the chain hard-resets to the authored rest AND takes a
;;     PHYS-SETTLE-frame ramp during which gravity, excitation and the visible deviation are scaled
;;     in from zero. A chain's first simulated frame goes down the same path, so every actor spawns
;;     at its bind pose with zero inherited velocity. `burst=` counts settle frames whose visible
;;     deviation still exceeded PHYS-BURST-REL of the chain length — owner bar: 0.
;; (C) TAPERED COLLIDERS. Constant-radius capsules cannot model Jak's FLARED trouser legs or his
;;     shoulders, so the jacket hem clipped through anyway. `radius2=` gives a capsule a second
;;     radius at its far end and the contact radius is interpolated at the contact point's own
;;     segment parameter — a cone, not a cylinder.
;; (D) THE FREEDOM RAMP MUST FIT THE CHAIN'S LENGTH. Jak's hair is TWO joints with rootlock=1, so
;;     exactly one link could ever move ("only the very tip of the tip"), and Keira's short back
;;     hair had the same shape. The ramp now has a configurable FLOOR (`rootfree=`) so the stiffest
;;     free link keeps a usable fraction of the cone instead of 1/nfree, and the short chains drop
;;     the rigid rootlock for a steep gradient — the root still visibly rides the skull, but the
;;     whole strand bends. Proof: per-LINK window spans (`jdev:`), so "the root is frozen" is a
;;     number, and `frozen=` counts ACTIVE chains that never moved in a window where the actor did.
;; (F) KEIRA'S SHOULDER STRAPS are REVERTED (see physics_chains.txt) — they were a regression.
;; DATA-DRIVEN: chains + params + precision levels live in recharged_assets/physics_chains.txt,
;; parsed C++-side (kmachine.cpp, OG_FEAT_PHYSICS) and queried over the pc-physics-* FFI at
;; companion init (joint NAMES resolved against the live HD jgeo). All FFI numeric returns are
;; MILLI-units (x1000) to avoid the float-return-register trap.
;;
;; SAFETY INVARIANT: after each chain step, any non-finite component or deviation > 2x chain
;; length hard-resets the chain state to the targets (+ nan-resets counter, must stay 0 in proofs).
;; An explosion can never persist more than one frame.
;;
;; PRECISION LADDER (owner-mandated monotone cost<->quality): per-level levers (substeps or fixed
;; 240Hz accumulator, constraint iterations, collider TIER, active chain-class mask) are DATA in the
;; [levels] section, selected by (-> *pc-settings* physics-quality) via pc-physics-enabled.
;;
;; PROOFS: [HD-PHYS] windowed counters (state dump: max deviation / max velocity bounded,
;; nan-resets, rest convergence when calm, rootdev=0 for locked roots, resid=0 penetrations,
;; per-chain deviation list so an INERT chain is visible as a number) — code-level evidence, never
;; capture campaigns.

(#when FLAG_PHYSICS

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; C++ FFI (kmachine.cpp, OG_FEAT_PHYSICS). All value returns are MILLI-units unless noted.
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(define-extern pc-physics-reload (function int))
(define-extern pc-physics-enabled (function int))              ;; 0 = off, else level+1
(define-extern pc-physics-joint-role (function string string int))   ;; (chain<<8)|link, -1 none
(define-extern pc-physics-num-chains (function string int))
;; ids: 0 hz 1 damp 2 grav 3 maxangle-deg 4 inertia 5 stretch 6 radius
;;      7 rootlock 8 gradient 9 animmode 10 excite 11 friction
;;      12 authored 13 authrise 14 authfall 15 authstiff 16 rootfree 17 nodesc 18 colskip (cycle 3)
;;      19 mass 20 hang 21 swing (cycle 4)
;;      22 family 23 side 24 extent 25 compress (cycle 5)
(define-extern pc-physics-chain-param-mi (function string int int int))
(define-extern pc-physics-chain-flags (function string int int))    ;; class bits 1/2/4
(define-extern pc-physics-level-param-mi (function int int int))    ;; 0 substeps 1 iters 2 collide-tier 3 classmask 4 fixedhz
(define-extern pc-physics-joint-collider-mi (function string string int)) ;; milli radius, 0 none
(define-extern pc-physics-num-colliders (function string int))
;; 0 milli radius, 1 RAW chain mask (-1 = all), 2 RAW tier, 3 RAW 1 = capsule,
;; 4 milli FAR-END radius (tapered capsule; = field 0 when radius2= is absent),
;; 5 RAW side (0 none / 1 L / 2 R), 6 RAW chain index this volume RIDES (-1 = a real bone)
(define-extern pc-physics-collider-param-mi (function string int int int))
(define-extern pc-physics-collider-is-joint (function string int string int)) ;; 1 if collider i sits on that joint
(define-extern pc-physics-collider-is-joint2 (function string int string int)) ;; 1 if capsule i ENDS on that joint
(define-extern pc-physics-chain-link-radius-mi (function string int int int)) ;; milli, 0 = absent
;; (C14) mesh-surface audit inputs: per-link EXTREMAL skinned-vertex offsets, bone-local bind
;; space (physics_mesh.txt, derived offline from the real merc/GLB geometry — never hand-tuned).
;; count: samples this link carries (0..5). mi: one coordinate in milli units; arg 2 packs
;; (link << 3) | sample-index, arg 3 is coord 0/1/2 — the FFI here carries at most 4 parameters,
;; same packing convention as pc-physics-joint-role's (chain<<8)|link.
(define-extern pc-physics-chain-msample-count (function string int int int))
(define-extern pc-physics-chain-msample-mi (function string int int int int))
(define-extern pc-physics-chain-xmask (function string int int))    ;; chain-vs-chain partner bits
(define-extern pc-physics-generation (function int))    ;; bumped on every params (re)parse

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; static pools: 24 slots x 48 sim joints x 24 chains x 16 colliders.
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(defconstant PHYS-SLOTS 24)
(defconstant PHYS-COMP-SLOTS 8)  ;; slots 0..7 are claimed by HD companions (bottom-up);
                                 ;; 8..23 by stock-model riders (top-down). One pool, no starvation
                                 ;; of the companions by a crowded village.
(defconstant PHYS-MAXJ 128)      ;; per-slot parent-table / descendant-pass joint ceiling
(defconstant PHYS-JPS 48)      ;; joints per slot
(defconstant PHYS-CPS 24)      ;; chains per slot
;; CYCLE 6. 96, up from 16, and the jump is the owner's blocker made structural rather than a
;; bigger number for its own sake. The volumes are no longer guessed by hand: they are FITTED to
;; the skinned merc geometry, one capsule per bone->child span, so that the union of them contains
;; the mesh (offline audit: fit error 0.000 and hole 0.000 on all 43 sections of the cast). A body
;; described that honestly needs 60-95 capsules, not 16 — Jak is 89 and Keira 55. The 16-collider
;; pool was itself part of the defect: it silently TRUNCATED, so a model that declared more simply
;; lost the rest with no log line.
;; The per-frame cost does NOT scale with this: PHYS-CCMAX below bounds what the solver walks.
(defconstant PHYS-COLS 192)    ;; colliders per slot — mesh-derived volumes, see PHYS-CCMAX for cost
;; What the constraint loop actually iterates, per chain. The old loop walked EVERY collider of the
;; actor and mask-tested each one; at 96 that is 6x the mask tests for no extra contacts. The bind
;; pass now resolves, once, the list of colliders that apply to each chain, and the hot loop walks
;; only that. So raising the POOL is free and this is the only number that costs frame time.
;; CYCLE 13. 96, up from 48, because the list is no longer a hand-authored subset. Until this cycle
;; a volume named the chains it applied to (`chains=`) and the bind pass copied that list verbatim,
;; so 48 was generous. That filter is gone — owner cycle 12: "le filtre chains= est une OPTIMISATION,
;; pas une AUTORISATION" — and the list is now rebuilt every frame from geometry: a chain is tested
;; against every volume of its own character that it can physically REACH. A strand that can reach
;; 60 volumes gets 60 entries, so the ceiling has to sit above the worst real model rather than
;; above the worst authored subset. Overflow is still LOUD (see the rebuild): a truncated list is
;; the exact failure this cycle exists to remove.
(defconstant PHYS-CCMAX 96)    ;; colliders walked per chain per iteration

(define *phys-slot-pid* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-njoints* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-nchains* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-ncols* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-seeded* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-frames* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; window frame counter
(define *phys-slot-resets* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; nan/explosion resets (window)
(define *phys-slot-maxdev* (new 'static 'array float 24))    ;; window max |p - t|
(define *phys-slot-maxvel* (new 'static 'array float 24))    ;; window max per-frame speed
(define *phys-slot-calm* (new 'static 'array int32 24))      ;; consecutive calm frames
(define *phys-slot-anchprev* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 24)) ;; chain0 anchor last pos (debug)
(define *phys-slot-anchmove* (new 'static 'array float 24))  ;; window max anchor move (debug)
;; ONE-LINE window emitter buffer: `format 0` is one logcat line per call on Android, so the whole
;; window must be assembled here and printed once (see the emitter at the bottom of this file).
;; Cycle 2 widened it: the per-chain deviation list rides in the SAME line (24 chains x ~13 chars).
;; Cycle 3 widened it again and added a SECOND line ([HD-PHYS2]: per-chain push-outs and the
;; per-LINK spans). The buffer is reused for both — appending to a string never splits a line, only
;; `format 0` does — so it must hold the LONGER of the two: 24 chains x ~11 + 48 links x ~15 + a
;; header. 2048 leaves better than 2x headroom over the worst case a full slot can produce.
;; CYCLE 16: 2048 -> 4096. [HD-PHYS7] carries FOUR per-chain float lists and TWO int lists, and a
;; full 24-chain slot printing four-decimal floats measures ~1900 characters — 148 short of the old
;; ceiling. `format` to a string APPENDS, so the failure mode of being wrong here is not a truncated
;; line, it is writing past the allocation.
(define *phys-line-buf* (new 'global 'string 4096 (the-as string #f)))
;; (C16) THE FRAME'S COLLISION GEOMETRY, SNAPSHOT ONCE, BEFORE ANY BONE IS WRITTEN.
;; A body volume's spine is read from the skeleton — and some of those spines END on a joint that a
;; chain drives (`neckB Learbase`, `chest RchestDanglerA`: the offline fitter emits body spans that
;; terminate on a chain root). So the write-back of chain 3 MOVED the volume that chain 7 had just
;; been verified clear of, and the pose proven feasible was no longer the pose measured. That
;; non-monotonicity is what the eleven fallback passes of the retired solver were compensating for:
;; a "fallback that cannot fail" is only needed when the guarantee can be invalidated behind you.
;; Snapshotting the spines makes the frame's geometry a FIXED reference, which is what makes the
;; feasibility of the authored pose an actual guarantee and lets one bisection replace all eleven.
;; Volumes that ride another CHAIN (colchain >= 0, the `at=` volumes: Keira's two breasts meeting
;; where they really swung to) are deliberately NOT snapshot — they are read live, because a
;; two-body contact is the strand domain's job and not this one's.
(define *phys-cola* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 4608))
(define *phys-colb* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 4608))
(define *phys-slot-pushouts* (new 'static 'array int32 24))  ;; collision push-out events (window)
(define *phys-slot-maxpen* (new 'static 'array float 24))    ;; max penetration depth resolved (window)
;; ---- cycle-2 counters -------------------------------------------------------------------------
(define *phys-slot-resid* (new 'static 'array int32 24))     ;; penetrations STILL unresolved after the last iteration
(define *phys-slot-maxresid* (new 'static 'array float 24))  ;; deepest residual penetration (window)
(define *phys-slot-rootdev* (new 'static 'array float 24))   ;; max drift of a LOCKED link, read back from the bone (must be 0)
(define *phys-slot-freeroot* (new 'static 'array float 24))  ;; max drift of an UNLOCKED link-0 (contrast: proves the sim is live)
(define *phys-slot-reglue* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; chains whose authored channel was replaced this frame
(define *phys-slot-desc* (new 'static 'array int32 24))      ;; non-simulated descendants re-glued onto moved parents (anti-tear)
(define *phys-slot-nopose* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; chain-frames with a ZERO-LENGTH pose (parked spawn / teleport frame) — not simulatable, not audited
;; ---- cycle-3 counters -------------------------------------------------------------------------
(define *phys-slot-authhold* (new 'static 'array int32 24))  ;; (A) chain-frames the AUTHORED animation owned (blend > 0.5)
(define *phys-slot-autheng* (new 'static 'array int32 24))   ;; (A) suspension ENGAGE events
(define *phys-slot-authrel* (new 'static 'array int32 24))   ;; (A) suspension RELEASE events (physics resumed) — engage without release = stuck
(define *phys-slot-authmax* (new 'static 'array float 24))   ;; (A) max blend weight reached
(define *phys-slot-reseed* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; (B) spawn + teleport chain resets
(define *phys-slot-burst* (new 'static 'array int32 24))     ;; (B) settle frames whose VISIBLE deviation still blew past the bound — owner bar: 0
(define *phys-slot-frozen* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; (D) ACTIVE chains that never moved in a window where the actor did
(define *phys-slot-holdmax* (new 'static 'array int32 24))  ;; (A) longest UNBROKEN suspension of any ONE chain — "never gave it back"
(define *phys-slot-jitter* (new 'static 'array int32 24))   ;; (O) velocity REVERSALS above the noise floor — oscillation, counted
(define *phys-slot-rested* (new 'static 'array int32 24))   ;; (O) chain-frames spent in the calm resting state
(define *phys-slot-clamped* (new 'static 'array int32 24))  ;; (O) corrections that hit the per-frame bound
(define *phys-slot-modelfall* (new 'static 'array int32 24)) ;; (N) links walked home to the model pose
;; (C6/cycle-10) the LARGEST single correction the model-pose ladder ever applied in the window,
;; in units. That pass is the one correction in the frame that is deliberately NOT bounded by
;; maxcorr (it writes `prev` by the same delta, so it cannot read as velocity), and an unbounded
;; correction is a one-frame jump of the BONE. Unbounded is the right trade against the owner's
;; absolute no-penetration rule, but it is a trade, so its size is measured and reported instead
;; of being assumed small.
(define *phys-slot-mfmax* (new 'static 'array float 24))     ;; (C6) worst single model-pose ladder step
(define *phys-slot-escape* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; (C6) last-resort unbounded escapes applied
(define *phys-slot-escmax* (new 'static 'array float 24))    ;; (C6) worst single last-resort escape, units
;; (O) the LONGEST SUSTAINED fight of any one chain in the window. A raw reversal COUNT cannot tell
;; "buzzing" from "sliding along the body": a chain in moving contact reverses now and then no matter
;; how well it behaves (measured: 73 isolated reversals on a perfectly settled Maia). What the owner
;; sees as "jitter comme un fou" is a chain reversing under contact frame AFTER frame — this is that
;; run length, and it is also the counter that arms the rest state.
(define *phys-slot-stickmax* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
;; ---- cycle-4 counters (owner 2026-08-06 14:45) -------------------------------------------------
;; (S) THE OLD JITTER METRIC MEASURED THE WRONG THING and the owner caught it: it only scored a
;; reversal while the link was PRESSED AGAINST A COLLIDER, on the reasoning that a free spring
;; reverses twice per oscillation and counting that would grade the feature as a defect. But
;; "l'hysteresis est HORRIBLE" is about hair and ears in OPEN AIR — the ringing that was explicitly
;; excluded IS the defect. These three replace it, and none of them can be narrowed the same way:
;;   * idle drift  — the actor's anchor did not move this frame, so ANY visible motion is the sim
;;                   feeding itself. A chain that wanders with no input is Maia's floating chest.
;;   * settle time — frames from "the driving motion stopped" to "the chain is at rest". Measures
;;                   DECAY, not the absence of contact, so no amount of re-scoping can hide ringing.
;;   * free ring   — velocity reversals with NO contact at all: precisely the population the old
;;                   metric threw away.
(define *phys-slot-idle* (new 'static 'array float 24))       ;; (S) max visible motion on a no-input frame
(define *phys-slot-idleframes* (new 'static 'array int32 24)) ;; (S) consecutive frames the anchor has been still
(define *phys-slot-settled* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; (S) 1 = already at rest in this idle stretch
(define *phys-slot-settletime* (new 'static 'array int32 24)) ;; (S) worst frames-to-rest seen in the window
(define *phys-slot-unsettled* (new 'static 'array int32 24))  ;; (S) idle stretches STILL ringing after a second
(define *phys-slot-freering* (new 'static 'array int32 24))   ;; (S) reversals in FREE SPACE (no contact)
;; (S) HOW MANY FRAMES THE WINDOW ACTUALLY SAMPLED AS INPUT-FREE. A zero drift reading is worth
;; nothing without it: cycle 3 shipped resid=0 on actors whose colliders never fired once, and an
;; idledrift=0 measured over zero idle frames would be the identical empty zero. Reported next to it.
(define *phys-slot-idleobs* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
;; (S) chain-frames the sleep rule zeroed a link's velocity: the mechanism behind "rien ne se repose
;; vraiment nulle part", visible as a count rather than inferred from the drift being small.
(define *phys-slot-slept* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
;; (W/C6b) link-frames on which ARRIVAL actually moved a body chain toward the model pose. The
;; anti-vacuous-zero counter for restdevA: a small fidelity number next to arrn=0 would mean the
;; chain merely never left, not that the mechanism that brings it home works.
(define *phys-slot-arrn* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
;; (U) "resid=0" is only meaningful if a collision test actually ran. Maia measured push=0 AND
;; resid=0 while her hair visibly went through her: a chain that is tested against nothing scores a
;; perfect penetration audit. These two make that impossible to misread ever again.
(define *phys-slot-noncol* (new 'static 'array int32 24))     ;; (U) ACTIVE chains with collision disabled outright
(define *phys-slot-nomask* (new 'static 'array int32 24))     ;; (U) ACTIVE chains no collider even references
;; ---- cycle-5 per-slot state --------------------------------------------------------------------
(define *phys-slot-fama* (new 'static 'array int32 24))       ;; (FAM) active chains classified BODY
(define *phys-slot-famb* (new 'static 'array int32 24))       ;; (FAM) active chains classified HANGS
(define *phys-slot-unclass* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; (FAM) active chains with NO family — must read 0
;; (W) how far from upright this actor got in the window, 0 = perfectly upright, 1 = fully tilted.
;; The owner's exception to "the model pose is the rest pose": "si tu pends Maia par les pieds,
;; forcement ses seins ne seront pas a la meme position que debout". Gravity's authority over a
;; FAMILY A chain's rest pose is this number, so the field is the proof the exception exists and the
;; proof it is not silently on all the time.
(define *phys-slot-tilt* (new 'static 'array float 24))
;; (W) worst post-settle deviation from the MODEL pose over the window, FAMILY A chains only.
(define *phys-slot-restdeva* (new 'static 'array float 24))
;; ...and the counter that says the measurement RAN. restdevA only scores once the actor has
;; settled, so a leg that never stands still would report a perfect 0.0000 without ever having
;; graded anything — the identical empty zero as resid=0 with push=0 (cycle 3) and idledrift=0
;; with idlewin=0 (cycle 4). Third time the trap is recognised, so it is closed at birth.
(define *phys-slot-restwin* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
;; (Z) residual penetrations of a chain into a volume belonging to the OTHER side of the body.
(define *phys-slot-xleg* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
;; (X) worst simulated/authored chain-length ratio in the window. 1.0 = nothing was crushed.
;; (X) ...on the OUTPUT, i.e. on what is drawn.
(define *phys-slot-lenmin* (new 'static 'array float 24))
;; ...and the same ratio on the SIMULATION state, which is what compress= actually governs. The
;; two answer different questions and the first cycle-5 leg proved they must both be asked:
;; Daxter's chains read 0.757 on the OUTPUT while nothing had been compressed at all. The output
;; is a per-link blend between the model pose and the simulated pose (the influence profile), and
;; when an anim=excite chain drives those two poses far apart — his ears sit over a chain-length
;; from the bind re-glue by design — blending them at a different weight per link shortens the
;; segments. That is the profile doing its job, not a crushed chain. lensim isolates the crush.
(define *phys-slot-lensim* (new 'static 'array float 24))
;; (Z/V) how many collision tests were displaced onto the skinned continuation by `extent=`. Like
;; idlewin= next to idledrift=, it is the counter that stops a clean cross-leg score from being the
;; empty kind: extprobe=0 would mean the pendant geometry was never tested at all.
(define *phys-slot-extprobe* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
;; (R) the gravity vector the integrator ACTUALLY applied, measured as the difference between the
;; acceleration with and without the gravity term — not restated from the constant. `gdir` is that
;; vector in WORLD space (must stay (0,-1,0) however the actor is turned) and `gloc` is the SAME
;; vector re-expressed in the anchor bone's own basis (must rotate, which is what proves the first
;; one is genuinely world and not local).
;; ...and how many frames of the window the probe actually FIRED. It has to exist now: family A
;; gates its gravity term to zero on an upright actor, so an actor whose chains are ALL family A
;; — an ears-only villager, a rider with nothing but hair — legitimately applies no gravity at all
;; while standing up, and gdir then holds its reset (0,0,0). Grading that as "gravity is not world
;; space" is grading the absence of a measurement as a defect, which cost 30 false failures on the
;; first cycle-5 leg. gsamp=0 means NOT MEASURED, and is read as such.
(define *phys-slot-gsamp* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-gdir* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 24))
(define *phys-slot-gloc* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 24))
;; (O/S) pre-constraint snapshot, one substep's worth. Scratch, never read across calls.
(define *phys-psave* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 48))
;; (S/C13d) net contact correction each link took inside THIS substep's collision sweep — the
;; direction the body pushed it. Kept so the velocity-consistency pass can also SPEND the approach
;; velocity the spring pumped into that contact (see the discharge there for the measured case).
;; Scratch like psave, one substep's worth, never read across calls.
(define *phys-lpn* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 48))


;; ---- cycle-4 constants --------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; (S) HOW MUCH OF A CONSTRAINT CORRECTION IS CANCELLED OUT OF THE VELOCITY. This is the single
;; change that answers "l'hysteresis est HORRIBLE" at its source. In a verlet integrator velocity is
;; implied by (p - prev), so ANY projection that moves p without moving prev is read next frame as
;; velocity the chain never had. Cycle 3 already applied that rule to the final collision sweep —
;; the owner's own words, "la correction de contrainte ne doit PAS reinjecter de vitesse" — but the
;; DISTANCE and CONE constraints ran `iters` times per substep and fed every one of their corrections
;; straight back in. That is a pump: gravity stretches the link, the distance constraint pulls it
;; back, the pull-back becomes velocity, and the chain rings forever with no input at all. 1.0 =
;; constraints contribute exactly zero velocity, which is standard position-based dynamics and is
;; what gives a chain a REST POSE it can actually reach.
(defconstant PHYS-PROJFIX 1.0)
;; (S) below this much anchor travel in a frame, the actor is standing still and the chain has no
;; input: anything it does is its own. 2 units = 0.5 mm.
(defconstant PHYS-IDLE-ANCH 2.0)
;; (S) chain speed under which the chain counts as AT REST (units/frame).
(defconstant PHYS-REST-VEL 2.0)
;; (S) an idle stretch still ringing after this many frames is reported as a failure to settle.
(defconstant PHYS-SETTLE-BAR 60)
;; (S) per-link TARGET travel under which the animation is asking this chain for nothing this frame.
;; Same 0.5 mm bar as the anchor: both have to be quiet before a frame is scored as input-free.
(defconstant PHYS-IDLE-TARG 2.0)
;; (S) frames of unbroken no-input before drift is graded: settling out of the motion that just
;; stopped is legitimate and is what settletime measures. Half a second at 60 Hz.
(defconstant PHYS-IDLE-SETTLED 30)
;; (S) SLEEP. Below this link speed on an input-free frame the remaining velocity is not motion, it
;; is the tail of a ring, and carrying it to the next frame is what let hair keep breathing on a
;; character standing still. Zeroed, so the chain converges on its rest pose instead of orbiting it.
;; 1 unit/frame = 0.25 mm/frame; a real swing is two orders of magnitude above this.
(defconstant PHYS-SLEEP-VEL 1.0)
;; (W/cycle-5) ARRIVAL. Sleeping only ever killed the VELOCITY, never asked where the chain was
;; when it did it — and that one omission is the whole of restdevA. A link whose target has gone
;; still and whose own speed has dropped below the floor has its `prev` collapsed onto `pos`, so
;; the verlet residue that was carrying it home is deleted and the spring is left to crawl the
;; remaining distance one acc*dt^2 step at a time. Measured on the phone: Maia's chest chains ended
;; 473 and 948 units (11-23 cm) from the pose Naughty Dog modelled and STAYED there, reading calm
;; the entire time, because at omega_eff = 2.6 rad/s a 473-unit error advances 0.6 units a frame.
;; That is the owner's "ca se balade meme sans mouvement", "rien ne se repose vraiment nulle part"
;; and "la position IDLE devrait etre EXACTEMENT celle du modele de base" — one defect, three
;; descriptions.
;;
;; So sleeping now ARRIVES: the same frames that used to freeze a chain in place relax it onto its
;; target instead. Deliberately NOT a clamp, a freeze or a pin — the three words the owner ruled
;; out ("MAIS SUJETS A LA PHYSIQUE"):
;;   * it is armed only after the chain has been quiet for PHYS-ARRIVE-N consecutive frames AND
;;     the animation has stopped asking the chain for anything (ctmove < PHYS-IDLE-TARG). One
;;     frame of excitation — the anchor moving, the animator keying — disarms it instantly and the
;;     full-amplitude spring is back, with no state to unwind.
;;   * it is a first-order relaxation, not a snap: PHYS-ARRIVE-K of the remaining error per frame.
;;   * it moves the state, never the equilibrium, and it writes `prev` alongside `pos`, so it
;;     injects exactly zero velocity (owner rule O).
;;   * FAMILY A ONLY. Family B's rest pose is gravity's, not the model's; relaxing a hanging strap
;;     onto its authored pose would be the opposite bug and is precisely what the owner rejected.
;;   * links a collider is holding are skipped: the body is allowed to hold a strand off the model
;;     pose, and that is not a fidelity failure (the residual audit takes the same view).
;; PHYS-ARRIVE-N is 3 against PHYS-RESTCALM's 10 and both count the SAME quiet frames, so arrival
;; always has a seven-frame head start on the measurement by construction, on any chain, at any
;; frequency — 0.65^7 of the error is left when the fidelity metric first looks.
;; CYCLE 6b. Two things were wrong with the arming, and both showed up as a body chain reading
;; "calm" while sitting a long way from the model pose:
;;   * arrival demanded that the ANIMATION had also gone quiet (ctmove < PHYS-IDLE-TARG). Samos'
;;     chain 6 measured 217 units off the model with a clearance of +74 — nothing touching it, in
;;     free air — precisely because his idle keeps keying the anchor, so arrival never armed while
;;     the fidelity metric happily sampled the lag. A chain that is not moving is not being driven,
;;     whatever the animator is doing further up; that, and only that, is the right test.
;;   * 0.35 leaves 0.65^7 = 4.9% of the error at the tenth calm frame, which on a 217-unit error is
;;     still 10.6 units. 0.5 leaves 0.39% (0.85 units) with the same seven-frame head start, and it
;;     is applied only to a chain whose fastest link is under 2 units/frame — 0.5 mm/frame, i.e.
;;     motion that is not on screen. It shortens no swing the owner can see.
;;
;; CYCLE 6c — THE 6b ARMING WAS A DIVISION BY THE MEASUREMENT'S OWN THRESHOLD.
;; 6b replaced the quiet-frame counter with a RAMP ON INSTANTANEOUS SPEED,
;; arv = K * (1 - cv / PHYS-REST-VEL), and PHYS-REST-VEL is the same 2.0 units/frame the fidelity
;; metric uses to decide a chain is settled. So the corrective term went to ZERO exactly at the
;; edge of the band the metric grades, and the steady-state lag it leaves behind,
;;      e = r / (K * (1 - r / V)),
;; diverges as the chain's speed r approaches V. That is not a tuning error, it is a pole sitting
;; on the gate. Solved against the shipped 05:24 leg it reproduces the measurements to the digit:
;;   jak-hd     restdevA 8.2321  -> r = 1.35 units/frame
;;   keira-hd   restdevA 79.4384 -> r = 1.90 units/frame
;; both just under the 2.0 the metric calls "at rest", which is why every one of those readings was
;; sampled and none of them was ever corrected. The chain was not stuck; it was crawling home with
;; the brake released only after it had already arrived.
;; A second defect kept the crawl slow enough to be caught: arrival collapsed `prev` ONTO `pos`
;; rather than moving it by the same delta. Collapsing deletes the momentum the chain had, which is
;; strictly more than the "inject no velocity" rule asks for, and it turns a second-order return
;; (time constant 1/omega, ~8 frames) into a first-order crawl at omega^2*dt^2 per step (~130
;; frames for Samos' belly at mass=3.2). Worse, it makes (pos - prev) — the very quantity the
;; fidelity metric reads as "is this chain moving?" — report a chain being dragged across the room
;; as motionless. The solver was lying to the measurement about its own state.
;; So, this cycle:
;;   * arming is the quiet-frame counter again (never the animator's silence, which was the 6a
;;     mistake, and never a divisor that vanishes on the gate, which was the 6b mistake);
;;   * the gain RAMPS from zero over PHYS-ARRIVE-RAMP frames, so a chain that dips under the
;;     threshold at the top of a swing — two frames at most on a real bounce — is never yanked;
;;   * `prev` moves by the SAME DELTA as `pos`: zero velocity injected, zero destroyed;
;;   * and it is applied BEFORE the output blend, so the correction reaches the bone on the frame
;;     it is computed instead of the frame after, and is graded after the length restoration and
;;     the collision sweep have both had their say.
;; Head start at the tenth quiet frame with N=2, RAMP=2, K=0.99: (1-.495)(1-.99)^6 = 5.1e-13.
;; MEASURED, 06:10 leg, K=0.8 and the collapse removed: keira-hd 79.44 -> 11.20, samos-hd 43.67 ->
;; 15.64, the intro 293.23 -> 30.68, the stock riders 28.41 -> 3.25. What was left was not a
;; convergence failure but a FIGHT: the chain-vs-chain pass separates a pair by moving `pos` AND
;; `prev` together, which is invisible to every velocity reading, so a link could be shoved up to
;; 30 units a frame while reading as perfectly calm, and arrival pulled it straight back. The two
;; worst readings of that leg were both that fight (Samos' belly against his own beard at ccdepth
;; 37.2, Maia's hair at 286.3) and it is also what took jak-hd's intro idle drift from 0.0000 to
;; 5.8190 units a frame. See *phys-lxheld*: a link another chain is holding is now held, exactly as
;; a link the body is holding is held. K then rises because what remains is genuine settling lag,
;; and the residual it leaves scales with (1-K).
;; CYCLE 7 — AND (1-K) IS THE WHOLE OF WHAT IS LEFT. The line above is not a figure of speech:
;; arrival is the LAST thing that touches `pos` before the output blend, and every link the
;; fidelity metric grades is a link arrival ran on — the two share their gating clause for clause
;; (family A, upright, not settling, authored below 0.5, i >= rootlock, `lpush` clear), and the
;; only writers that come after — the collision resolve, the cross-side pass — set `lpush` on
;; whatever they move, which takes that link out of the sample. So on a graded frame
;;   restdevA = influence * (1 - K) * |error before arrival|,
;; exactly, and nothing else in the frame can add to it. That is why the number sat at 5-7 units
;; across three cycles of solver work that never touched K: at 0.95 the sim was keeping a
;; twentieth of a displacement the chain-vs-chain pass can legitimately make 100+ units deep, and
;; a twentieth of that is the entire reading. Measured, 09:06 four-leg run: samos-hd `belly`
;; 5.8515 (worst of D-MAX, and 5x every other chain on that actor), evilsis chestL/chestR 7.0029
;; and 6.7711 (worst of D-INTRO) — all three single-joint chains with mass=, i.e. the ones whose
;; partner chains shove them hardest while reading as calm.
;; K 0.95 -> 0.99 divides that residual by five, and it can do nothing else: it changes no force,
;; no limit and no volume. It cannot reach family B at all (arrival is family-A only), so it
;; cannot move `xleg`, which is family B's counter by construction — side= is declared on hanging
;; pendants and on nothing else. It cannot open a penetration either: for family A every volume is
;; capped at the chain's own model pose less PHYS-MODEL-CLR, so the point arrival pulls toward is
;; outside all of them by construction, and pulling harder toward it can only reduce contact.
;; What it does change is what the owner asked for three times in different words — "la position
;; IDLE devrait etre EXACTEMENT celle du modele de base, pas plus haut, pas plus bas". At 0.95 it
;; was 95% of the way there. There is no visible cost: the correction magnitude moves from 0.95 to
;; 0.99 of an error the chain only has while its own Verlet velocity is under 2 units/frame
;; (0.5 mm), so the "pop at the end of the settle" the owner was told to watch for is 4% larger
;; than the one already shipping, not a new one.
(defconstant PHYS-ARRIVE-N 2)
(defconstant PHYS-ARRIVE-RAMP 2.0)
;; CYCLE 9: 0.99 -> 0.995, and the paragraph above is the reason rather than the metric. The
;; residual this leaves is exactly (1-K) of the error a calm chain still carries, so the number it
;; produces is arithmetic, not a judgement call: the worst family A chain on the phone is Daxter's
;; ears at 5.6558 units off the model pose, and they have measured 5.61-5.66 all day, through three
;; solver changes that never touched K, because K is the only term that decides how much of that
;; error survives. Halving (1-K) halves it. Everything the paragraph above says still holds at
;; 0.995 — it reaches no family B chain, it cannot open a penetration on a family A one (their
;; volumes are capped at the model pose, so the point it pulls toward is outside all of them), and
;; it only acts on a chain whose own Verlet velocity is already under 2 units a frame.
(defconstant PHYS-ARRIVE-K 0.995)
;; (W/C6c) how long a chain-vs-chain contact keeps holding the links it separated. The pass runs
;; after the per-chain step, so the flag is always read one frame later; 3 frames of hysteresis
;; means a pair in sustained contact stays exempt instead of flickering in and out of it every
;; other frame, which would rebuild the oscillation the flag exists to remove.
(defconstant PHYS-XHOLD 3)
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; CYCLE 14 — the owner's verdict on the 15:42 build was "massively toned down, nothing fixed", and
;; the arithmetic behind it is measured: the cycle-13 perimeter rebuild puts a grazing contact on
;; every inward half-cycle of a chest or hair chain (their volumes are capped AT the model pose, so
;; the model pose sits ON the surface), and the C13d inelastic discharge then spends the FULL
;; approach velocity on every one of those grazes. Half the oscillation dies per contact — a sim
;; that satisfies every one-sided calm ceiling by being dead. The discharge stays (it is what lets
;; a resting pair go quiet, owner rule O) but it is now SUSTAINED-CONTACT gated: a chain whose
;; stick counter says it is fighting a collider spends everything, a transient graze spends only
;; PHYS-SPEND-SOFT of its approach and keeps the swing. Calm cannot regress: the rest state, the
;; sleep, the ring-down and arrival are all untouched and all idle-gated.
(defconstant PHYS-SPEND-SOFT 0.35)
;; (C14-A) LOCOMOTION motion floors. A frame counts toward `crun` only when the chain's OWN anchor
;; travelled more than this many units in that frame — 60 units/frame ~ 0.9 m/s, which a walk, a
;; run and Keira's Zoomer-work loop (measured 190+ on the phone) all clear and an idle sway does
;; not. Teleport/settle frames are excluded by csettle exactly as every other instrument does.
(defconstant PHYS-RUN-ANCH 60.0)
;; (C14-B/C) mesh samples per link (data ships <=5: four perpendicular-quadrant extremal vertices
;; plus one axial-overhang tip vertex, physics_c14_meshsamples.py).
(defconstant PHYS-MSAM 5)
;; (S) IDLE RING-DOWN. Sleep only ever killed velocity BELOW PHYS-SLEEP-VEL; anything above it rang
;; on indefinitely, and in the intro that is what the owner calls hysteresis — jak-hd was still
;; displacing 27.9 units a frame after half a second with nothing moving on the actor at all. Once
;; the whole actor has been input-free for PHYS-RINGDOWN-N frames the retained velocity is ramped
;; down instead, every family, until the chain stops. Deliberately NOT armed during the first eight
;; idle frames: the free swing right after a motion ends is the feature, and it is left untouched.
(defconstant PHYS-RINGDOWN-N 8)
(defconstant PHYS-RINGDOWN-RATE 0.06)
(defconstant PHYS-RINGDOWN-MIN 0.30)
;; (S/cycle-11) ...and the frame at which the same ramp, applied to the DISPLACEMENT rather than to
;; the stored velocity, reaches zero: from PHYS-RINGDOWN-N to here a chain on a completely
;; motionless actor gives up its remaining creep linearly, and past it, it holds the position it
;; reached. 24 frames, six ahead of PHYS-IDLE-SETTLED, so the hold is complete before anything
;; grades it rather than arriving on the same frame. See the block ahead of ARRIVAL for why the
;; velocity ramp alone could never get there and for the two counters that cross-check the hold.
(defconstant PHYS-HOLD-N 24)
;; (S) FREE-SPACE ANTI-RING. The contact rest state (PHYS-STICK) only ever armed on a chain pressed
;; against a collider, so it could not touch the defect the owner actually reported: hair, ears, a
;; collar and lurker legs ringing in OPEN AIR. A link that reverses direction above the jitter speed
;; floor for this many consecutive frames is not swinging — a real swing reverses at its own period,
;; a few times a second at most — it is oscillating, and its velocity retention collapses until it
;; stops. Same philosophy as the contact rest state, applied where there is nothing to touch.
(defconstant PHYS-RING 4)
(defconstant PHYS-RING-DAMP 0.35)


;; ---- cycle-3 constants ------------------------------------------------------------------------
(defconstant PHYS-SETTLE 20)          ;; frames of physics ramp-in after a spawn / teleport (~1/3 s)
(defconstant PHYS-JUMP-ABS 4096.0)    ;; 1 m of anchor travel in ONE frame is a cut/teleport, never running
(defconstant PHYS-JUMP-REL 1.5)       ;; ...or 1.5x the chain's own length, whichever is larger
(defconstant PHYS-BURST-REL 1.5)      ;; a settling chain deviating past 1.5x its own length = wild.
                                      ;; The first pass used 0.35, which is BELOW what the solver
                                      ;; legitimately produces: a 36-degree cone on a 2-link strap
                                      ;; already allows 0.62x, and Jak's pack strap measured 0.685x
                                      ;; in ordinary motion. A bar under the constraint envelope
                                      ;; does not detect "it went wild", it detects "the chain
                                      ;; worked". 1.5x cannot be reached with the distance and cone
                                      ;; constraints intact, and stays under the explosion reset
                                      ;; bound (100 + 2x), so the two audits do not overlap.
(defconstant PHYS-FROZEN-DEV 2.0)     ;; window deviation under this (0.5 mm) = the chain never moved.
                                      ;; The defect being caught is "declared but NOT SIMULATED",
                                      ;; which reads as exactly 0.0 — so the bar only has to
                                      ;; separate 0 from alive. Set higher and a legitimately stiff
                                      ;; chain (Jak's belt: 5.5 Hz, 7 deg cone) trips it and the
                                      ;; gate starts crying wolf about correct behaviour.
(defconstant PHYS-FROZEN-ANCH 60.0)   ;; ...and only counts in a window where the anchor really did move

;; ---- cycle-3d/3c constants --------------------------------------------------------------------
;; (P) largest jump allowed between two ADJACENT links of the influence profile. A binary rootlock
;; is a step of 1.0 at the boundary, which is a discontinuous derivative and reads as a CREASE —
;; the owner sees it at mid-height on Daxter's ears. The profile below is BUILT so this holds; it
;; is not a check that can be forgotten, and the value is reported per chain at bind time.
(defconstant PHYS-INFL-STEP 0.45)
;; (O) contact dead zone. Re-projecting a sub-tolerance penetration every frame is pure chatter and
;; is exactly the noise floor the residual audit already refuses to score.
(defconstant PHYS-PEN-TOL 1.0)
;; (W/C6b) margin kept between a link's MODEL pose and the surface of any volume it is tested
;; against. See *phys-ccap*. Small on purpose: this is a floor, not a clearance budget.
(defconstant PHYS-MODEL-CLR 2.0)
;; (C13) REACH MARGIN. The perimeter — which volumes a chain is tested against, and which chains are
;; tested against each other — is decided from geometry every frame, not from a data key. The test
;; is "can this chain's bounding sphere touch that volume", and the sphere is measured from THIS
;; frame's poses, so it needs a margin covering how far the two can close on each other before the
;; next frame's test runs. The fastest relative bone travel measured on this cast is 76 units in one
;; frame (samos-hd walking, see *phys-canchmv*); 512 is a bit under seven of those, i.e. an eighth of
;; a metre of slack on a reading refreshed every frame. Being generous costs list length and nothing
;; else — being stingy costs a missed contact, which is the owner's blocker.
(defconstant PHYS-REACH-MARGIN 512.0)
;; (N) how far a family A link the body is holding is biased back toward its model pose each
;; frame. It is a fraction, not a distance, so a link already home does not move and a link
;; driven deep comes back at a rate set by how deep it is. 0.25 = a contact lasting a fifth of
;; a second is essentially home; a glancing one is barely touched.
(defconstant PHYS-MODELPULL 0.25)
;; ...and how much of that authority a link that is still MOVING is allowed to feel.
;; MEASURED DEFECT (cycle 7, owner AB/AG: "plus de jiggle ET un poil plus de fermete", then
;; "beaucoup plus FLASQUE... ne bouge PAS ASSEZ"). Keira's chest link sits at clearance
;; cclr[0] = -0.0149 against its own capped torso volume on EVERY device window — the model-pose
;; cap (PHYS-MODEL-CLR) puts the volume surface 2 units under the breast's modelled position, so
;; the inward half of every jiggle cycle touches it. Contact sets lpush, lpush arms the bias
;; above, and the bias then removed a QUARTER of the chain's deviation per frame while it was
;; swinging: a 2.4-frame half-life, an artificial damping an order of magnitude stronger than any
;; authored damping=. That is why the chest amplitude did not move when stiffness went 2.60 -> 1.55
;; (383.22 -> 380.79 on the phone) — the spring was never what governed its decay — and why the
;; measured amplitude fell from 558.10 (cycle 6) to ~380 the moment volumes gained the model cap.
;; The bias is a REST mechanism: its job is to stop a link the body is holding from LIVING inside
;; it. So it now scales with the link's own quiet, exactly like the arrival term: a chain that has
;; gone still gets the full 0.25 (Maia's hair-through-body case, cycle 6 N, is untouched), a chain
;; in mid-swing keeps PHYS-MPMOVE of it and is left to the collision sweep — which still runs after
;; this and still has the last word, so no penetration guarantee depends on it.
(defconstant PHYS-MPMOVE 0.12)
(defconstant PHYS-MPCALM 4.0)         ;; frames of quiet at which the bias reaches full authority
;; (AH) largest anchor SECOND DIFFERENCE, as a fraction of the chain's own length, that is read as
;; an acceleration rather than as an animation pop. Scale free, so one number covers Daxter's ear
;; and Gol's cape.
(defconstant PHYS-COUPLE-MAX 0.35)
;; (AF) frames of unbroken authored authority the baseline freeze covers. A gesture, not a lifetime:
;; past it the baseline tracks again so a bone the animation merely PARKED is handed back.
(defconstant PHYS-AUTH-GRACE 240)
;; (O) a single frame may not move a joint more than this fraction of the chain's length to satisfy
;; a collider. Deep penetrations (a spawn inside geometry) are walked out over several frames
;; instead of being teleported out, which is the other way an energy loop starts.
(defconstant PHYS-MAXCORR-REL 0.5)
;; (O) frames of PERSISTENT unsatisfied contact after which the chain is treated as resting against
;; the body: damping is raised hard so it settles into the surface instead of vibrating on it.
(defconstant PHYS-STICK 2)            ;; 12 originally, then 4. Four consecutive frames of contact AND
                                      ;; velocity reversal is already a chain buzzing at 7.5 Hz
                                      ;; against the body — waiting 12 frames to calm it means a
                                      ;; fifth of a second of visible vibration first, and the
                                      ;; owner's rule is that it should "rester tranquille",
                                      ;; not eventually. Intervening earlier also means the rest
                                      ;; state is EXERCISED and measurable rather than a mechanism
                                      ;; that only exists when something else is broken: with the
                                      ;; collider bugs fixed the longest fight left is 5-7 frames,
                                      ;; which at 12 would have engaged nothing at all — a mechanism
                                      ;; that only runs when something else is broken is a mechanism
                                      ;; nobody has ever measured. At 2, three consecutive frames of
                                      ;; contact-plus-reversal (20 Hz alternation against the body)
                                      ;; is what arms it, and ONE clean frame disarms it: a nudge
                                      ;; that calms a buzzing chain, never a lock that freezes a
                                      ;; moving one.
(defconstant PHYS-STICK-DAMP 0.15)    ;; velocity retention multiplier once a chain is declared resting
;; (O) a reversal only counts as jitter above this speed (units/frame) — below it, sign flips are
;; float noise on a chain that is standing still.
(defconstant PHYS-JITTER-SPEED 3.0)
;; (Q) how fast the authored-offset BASELINE follows a sustained pose offset, per second. The
;; detector must fire on what the animator DOES, not on where the idle pose happens to sit.
(defconstant PHYS-AUTH-BASE 0.35)

;; (W) how many consecutive CALM frames make an actor "settled" for the model-fidelity metric.
;; The slot-level settled flag turned out never to fire on the shipping legs — restwin read 0 in
;; two consecutive device runs — so the metric was grading nothing while reporting a perfect zero.
;; That is exactly the empty zero its own witness counter was added to expose, and it did.
;; `calm` counts consecutive frames under the rest velocity, is the same signal the rest-converged
;; message has always used, and is observed on the phone every single run.
(defconstant PHYS-RESTCALM 10)

;; (W) THE UPRIGHT WINDOW. Cosine of the angle between the actor's own up axis and world up.
;; Above COS-UP the character is standing/walking/running normally and gravity has NO say in where a
;; FAMILY A chain rests — the model pose is the target, full stop. Below COS-TILT it is genuinely
;; upside down or doubled over and gravity takes the rest pose back. In between it ramps, so there
;; is no frame where the equilibrium jumps.
;; 30 degrees is chosen from the animation, not from taste: jak1's run, roll, jump and landing
;; poses all lean the torso well under it, and the whole point of this cycle is that a running
;; character's hair must NOT be dragged off the modelled silhouette. 75 degrees is where the
;; character is no longer meaningfully upright by any reading.
(defconstant PHYS-COS-UP 0.866)     ;; cos 30 deg
(defconstant PHYS-COS-TILT 0.2588)  ;; cos 75 deg

;; WAVE 2: the sim no longer reads a companion's khd-par — every slot carries its OWN parent table,
;; filled either from the companion's k->e table or, for a stock rider, from the live jgeo
;; (joint.parent). 255 = root / out of range.
(define *phys-par* (new 'static 'array uint8 3072))     ;; PHYS-SLOTS * PHYS-MAXJ
(define *phys-slot-rider* (new 'static 'array int32 24)) ;; 1 = stock-model rider slot
(define *phys-slot-stamp* (new 'static 'array int32 24)) ;; frame this slot last stepped (rider GC +
                                                         ;; once-per-frame guard)
(define *phys-slot-gen* (new 'static 'array int32 24))   ;; params generation the slot was bound with

;; per sim joint (idx = slot*PHYS-JPS + j)
(define *phys-jk* (new 'static 'array int32 1152))          ;; rig joint index k
(define *phys-pos* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
(define *phys-prev* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
(define *phys-targ* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152)) ;; per-frame target cache
;; (A) the target cache is BLENDED toward the authored pose while the animation owns a chain, so it
;; can no longer serve as the write-back's rotation REFERENCE: the bone's 3x3 is the bind-pose-
;; relative basis swung by (reference-direction -> simulated-direction), and if the reference moves
;; with the simulation that swing collapses to identity — the joint would land on the authored
;; POSITION carrying an unrotated basis. This keeps the calm rest pose pristine for exactly that
;; comparison, so at full authored weight the swing is (rest -> authored) and the bone really points
;; where the animator put it.
(define *phys-rest* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
;; (P) the BLENDED output position actually written to the bone: rest + influence*(sim - rest).
;; Kept separate from *phys-pos* because the sim must keep integrating its own full-amplitude state
;; — damping the STATE instead of the OUTPUT would change the chain's dynamics, not its stiffness
;; profile, and the two links either side of a boundary would drift apart again.
(define *phys-out* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
;; (O) last frame's velocity, for the jitter metric: a chain fighting an unsatisfiable collider
;; reverses direction every frame, and that reversal count is the number the owner's "jitter comme
;; un fou" turns into.
(define *phys-vprev* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
;; (S/cycle-4) LAST FRAME'S TARGET, per joint. "No input" cannot be read off the anchor's TRANSLATION
;; alone: a villager who turns on the spot, or a sage whose head rotates about a point a centimetre
;; from his beard root, moves that root by less than the idle threshold while swinging every target
;; below it across half a metre. The chain then follows its target — driven motion, correctly — and
;; the old instrument booked the whole excursion as "drift with no input" (measured: sage-lod0
;; idledrift=2637 units in a window where the actor was, by that definition, standing still). What
;; the animation ASKS FOR is the target, so the target is what has to be still before a frame counts
;; as input-free. This is not a narrower metric — it is a correction of attribution, and it makes the
;; number go UP wherever a chain really does move by itself.
(define *phys-tprev* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
;; (S/cycle-4) LAST FRAME'S OUTPUT POSITION, per joint — the point the BONE received, after the
;; influence blend and after the final collision sweep. Drift has to be measured on this and on
;; nothing else. The verlet pair (pos - prev) is a VELOCITY, and with the constraint corrections
;; mirrored into prev (PHYS-PROJFIX) it is specifically the velocity the chain had BEFORE the cone
;; and distance clamps took it back. A chain hanging on its swing-cone limit — gravity pulling every
;; frame, the cone returning it to the same place every frame — is perfectly still on screen and
;; still reads 8 units of "velocity". Measured on the phone: jak-hd reported exactly 8.0205 in three
;; different builds, byte-identical across a contact-exclusion change that should have moved it, on
;; a Jak standing motionless with no authored activity and no contact. It was not motion. What the
;; owner sees is where the bone is, so that is what is differenced here.
(define *phys-oprev* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
;; (S/cycle-11) the SIM position at the end of the previous frame — the reference the idle hold
;; measures this frame's creep against. `prev` cannot serve: the verlet integrator's `prev` is
;; rewritten by sleep and by the velocity ring-down, so it is a velocity store and not last frame's
;; position, and differencing against it would read the damping as motion.
(define *phys-lastp* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
(define *phys-anim* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152)) ;; per-frame AUTHORED position (pre re-glue), for anim=excite and (A) authored priority
(define *phys-jdev* (new 'static 'array float 1152))         ;; (D) per-LINK window max deviation: "only the tip moves" is a number, not an impression
;; (P) per-LINK influence: the fraction of the simulated displacement this bone actually receives.
;; Built once at bind time, monotone root->tip, with EVERY adjacent step bounded by PHYS-INFL-STEP —
;; the "cran" the owner sees on Daxter's ears is a step of 1.0 in exactly this profile, produced by
;; a binary rootlock, and no amount of amplitude tuning can remove a discontinuous derivative.
(define *phys-infl* (new 'static 'array float 1152))

;; per chain (idx = slot*PHYS-CPS + c); cstart is the joint index base WITHIN the slot.
(define *phys-cstart* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
(define *phys-clen* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
(define *phys-cflags* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
(define *phys-canchor* (new 'static 'array int32 576))      ;; anchor rig joint index (link0's parent)
(define *phys-comega* (new 'static 'array float 576))       ;; 2*pi*hz
(define *phys-cdamp* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-cgrav* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; gravity scale
(define *phys-cmaxrad* (new 'static 'array float 576))      ;; swing cone half-angle, RADIANS (per-link scaled by the gradient)
(define *phys-cinertia* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-cstretch* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-cradius* (new 'static 'array float 576))      ;; per-joint collision radius
(define *phys-crootlock* (new 'static 'array int32 576))    ;; leading links pinned rigidly to the animated bone
(define *phys-cgrad* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; 0 = uniform, 1 = full root->tip freedom ramp
(define *phys-canim* (new 'static 'array int32 576))        ;; 0 keep / 1 replace / 2 excite
(define *phys-cexcite* (new 'static 'array float 576))      ;; anim=excite: authored-delta force scale
(define *phys-cfric* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; contact friction 0..1
(define *phys-cdev* (new 'static 'array float 576))         ;; window max deviation OF THIS CHAIN (per-chain proof)
;; (D/cycle-10) THE SAME QUESTION FROM THE INPUT SIDE: how far did THIS CHAIN'S OWN anchor travel
;; in the window. The frozen audit used to arm on the slot-wide anchmove — "the actor moved" — and
;; that is a different actor from the one the chain is attached to. Measured, intro leg, samos-hd:
;; his `belly` chain reads cdev=0.0000 in six windows where the slot reads anchmove=178-201, and it
;; reads 254-278 in the village leg at the same slot anchmove. Same rig, same parameters. In the
;; cinematic Samos hovers with his hips still and gesticulates from the chest up, so his beard, his
;; ears and the logs on his back are driven while his belly anchor is not — and a chain whose own
;; anchor never moved is not frozen, it is at rest, which is what every other counter in this file
;; (restdevA, idledrift, sleep, arrival) exists to demand of it. Arming the two on contradictory
;; definitions of "input" means one of them has to be wrong on every quiet chain in the game.
;; Accumulated ONLY on frames where the chain is not inside its spawn/teleport ramp: during the
;; ramp it is deliberately held (owner B), and grading a chain for obeying rule B would make the
;; two rules unsatisfiable together.
(define *phys-canchmv* (new 'static 'array float 576))      ;; (D) window max travel of THIS chain's own anchor
;; (S/cycle-10) IDLE DRIFT, BROKEN OUT PER CHAIN. The slot-wide idledrift= is a maximum over every
;; chain on the actor, so a run that fails it says "something on jak-hd moved 4.35 units with no
;; input" and nothing more — which is a whole device cycle spent guessing which of seventeen chains
;; it was. `cself` is this frame's self-displacement for the chain in hand, folded into `cidr` only
;; on the frames the slot scores as input-free (the decision is taken after every chain has been
;; polled, so it cannot be made inside the chain loop). Pure instrumentation: it adds a name to a
;; number that already exists and changes no behaviour.
(define *phys-cself* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; (S) this frame's self-motion, per chain
(define *phys-cidr* (new 'static 'array float 576))         ;; (S) window max idle drift, per chain
;; ---- cycle-3 per-chain state ------------------------------------------------------------------
(define *phys-cauth* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; (A) authored-priority blend weight, 0 = pure physics, 1 = the animator owns the chain
(define *phys-cauththr* (new 'static 'array float 576))     ;; (A) engage threshold (authored offset / chain length); 0 = feature off for this chain
(define *phys-cauthrise* (new 'static 'array float 576))    ;; (A) blend-in rate per second
(define *phys-cauthfall* (new 'static 'array float 576))    ;; (A) blend-out rate per second — this is the "physics resumes progressively" ramp
(define *phys-cauthstiff* (new 'static 'array float 576))   ;; (A) stiffness multiplier at w=1 (how hard the chain tracks the authored pose)
(define *phys-cauthmax* (new 'static 'array float 576))     ;; (A) window max authored ratio seen — proves the DETECTOR is live even when it never engages
(define *phys-crootfree* (new 'static 'array float 576))    ;; (D) floor of the root->tip freedom ramp
(define *phys-cnodesc* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
;; (D-side effect) leading links exempt from BODY COLLISION. Until cycle 3 that exemption was a
;; side effect of rootlock: a rigidly-pinned root was skipped everywhere, collisions included.
;; Freeing short-chain roots so more of the length moves (owner D) would therefore have started
;; colliding every hair root with the very skull it is glued to — a penetration sitting there on
;; frame 1, in the rest pose, that no stiffness could ever clear and that resid= would have read as
;; a real body intersection. The two ideas are now separate: rootlock says "does this link move?",
;; colskip says "is this link inside the body on purpose?". Effective = max(rootlock, colskip).
(define *phys-ccolskip* (new 'static 'array int32 576))      ;; leading links that are INSIDE the body on purpose
;; (A) consecutive frames the authored animation has owned THIS chain. The slot-wide `authhold`
;; counts CHAIN-frames, so on an actor with 5 suspended chains it reaches 300 in 60 frames and says
;; nothing about any one chain — the first cut of this gate read that as "stuck" and was simply
;; wrong. What actually matters is whether ONE chain is never given back, and that is this number.
(define *phys-chold* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
(define *phys-cauthbase* (new 'static 'array float 576))    ;; (Q) slow baseline of the authored offset
(define *phys-cstick* (new 'static 'array int32 576))       ;; (O) consecutive frames of UNSATISFIED contact
(define *phys-cring* (new 'static 'array int32 576))        ;; (S) consecutive frames of FREE-SPACE reversal
;; PER-CHAIN residual frames. The slot-wide resid= says an actor ends frames inside its own body but
;; not WHICH chain, and on a 12-chain character that is a guessing game — it cost a full build cycle
;; on Gol. cres: names the chain, so a bad collider line is read off the log instead of deduced.
(define *phys-cres* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
(define *phys-cmass* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; (K) chain mass: omega_eff = omega / sqrt(mass)
;; ---- cycle-4 per-chain state -------------------------------------------------------------------
(define *phys-chang* (new 'static 'array float 576))        ;; (R) rest direction: 0 = the animator's, 1 = gravity's
(define *phys-cswing* (new 'static 'array float 576))       ;; (T) fraction of the chain's rotation written to the bone
(define *phys-cncol* (new 'static 'array int32 576))        ;; (U) how many bound colliders actually reference this chain
;; (U) MINIMUM CLEARANCE over the window: the smallest signed distance from any of this chain's
;; simulated links to the surface of any collider that applies to it (negative = inside the body).
;; A large POSITIVE number on a chain the owner watches pass through a character is the whole
;; diagnosis in one field — it says the volumes are nowhere near where the chain actually goes,
;; which is why push= and resid= could both read 0 while Maia's hair went straight through her.
(define *phys-cclr* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-csettle* (new 'static 'array int32 576))      ;; (B) frames of physics ramp-in left after a spawn / teleport
(define *phys-canchprev* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 576)) ;; (B) this chain's anchor last frame — a one-frame jump IS the teleport signal
(define *phys-cpush* (new 'static 'array int32 576))        ;; per-chain collision push-outs (window): names the chain a collider is WELDING

;; ---- cycle-5 per-chain state -------------------------------------------------------------------
;; (FAM) THE FAMILY. The owner said it three times and asked for it to be printed: "c'est du CAS PAR
;; CAS". Every chain belongs to exactly one of two families and the family — not a tuning value —
;; decides what its REST POSE is:
;;   1 = FAMILY A, a part of the BODY (hair, breasts, ears, bellies, fur, muzzles). It is simulated
;;       at every instant and gravity drives its DYNAMICS, but the pose it converges back to is the
;;       one Naughty Dog modelled. "Pas plus haut, pas plus bas, pas plus ecrase."
;;   2 = FAMILY B, something that genuinely HANGS (leather straps, hanging cloth, accessories,
;;       capes, pendants). Gravity dictates its rest and it must NEVER be pulled back to the model
;;       pose — a jacket flap that returns to bind is as much a bug as a drooping breast.
;;   0 = UNCLASSIFIED. Treated as A (the safe end: it cannot droop) and COUNTED, so a chain added
;;       without a family shows up as a number in the report instead of quietly inheriting a
;;       behaviour nobody chose.
(define *phys-cfam* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
;; (Z) which side of the body this chain belongs to, 1 = L, 2 = R, 0 = neither/central. Paired with
;; the collider's own side to count CROSS-SIDE penetrations: Jak's left jacket pendant ending up
;; inside his RIGHT leg is not "a penetration", it is the specific defect the owner described, and
;; a counter that cannot tell them apart cannot prove it is gone.
(define *phys-cside* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
;; (Z/V) HOW FAR THE SKINNED GEOMETRY REACHES PAST THE LAST BONE, in units. Jak's jacket pendants
;; are ONE joint each: the bone sits at the hem's top and the cloth hangs a long way below it,
;; rigidly skinned. Colliding the bone POINT therefore proved nothing — the bone stayed politely
;; outside the thigh capsule while the visible cloth swept straight through the opposite leg, which
;; is exactly what the owner saw on two shipped builds. With extent>0 the collision test is moved to
;; the middle of that continuation and inflated to cover it, so the volume being kept out of the leg
;; is the one that is drawn.
(define *phys-cext* (new 'static 'array float 576))
;; (X) how much a link is allowed to SHORTEN, as a fraction of its authored length. DEFAULT 0 —
;; nothing may compress. Until cycle 5 the distance constraint was symmetric (`stretch=` bounded
;; both directions), so a collar pressed between a shoulder and the ground could legally lose 22% of
;; its length and read as "solved". The owner: "attention par exemple au COL DE JAK qui ne doit pas
;; s'ecraser pour autant". A chain that cannot shorten has to BEND instead, which is what cloth does.
(define *phys-ccomp* (new 'static 'array float 576))
;; (W) POST-SETTLE DEVIATION FROM THE MODEL POSE, family A only, links not held by a collider.
;; The measurement the owner's rule actually needs: not "how far is it from the model right now"
;; (that would forbid the bounce he explicitly wants) but "once it has stopped, did it come back".
(define *phys-crestd* (new 'static 'array float 576))
;; (X) worst ratio of simulated chain length to authored chain length seen in the window. 1.0 = the
;; chain is exactly as long as the model says. Below 1 it is being crushed.
(define *phys-clenr* (new 'static 'array float 576))
;; (W) CONSECUTIVE frames this chain has been below the rest velocity. One frame is not enough and
;; the reason is the shape of the thing being measured: a spring is momentarily STILL at each end
;; of its swing, at maximum displacement. Sampling "slow right now" therefore samples the
;; AMPLITUDE and calls it the rest pose — measured on the phone, Keira's chest read 180 units of
;; "failure to return" while doing exactly what it is supposed to do. A chain that has been slow
;; for PHYS-RESTCALM frames in a row has actually stopped.
(define *phys-ccalm* (new 'static 'array int32 576))

;; body collision volumes (idx = slot*PHYS-COLS + i). joint2 < 0 = sphere on joint1, else CAPSULE
;; swept between the two animated bones.
(define *phys-colk* (new 'static 'array int32 4608))         ;; jgeo joint index carrying the volume
(define *phys-colk2* (new 'static 'array int32 4608))        ;; capsule far end, -1 = sphere
(define *phys-colr* (new 'static 'array float 4608))
(define *phys-colr2* (new 'static 'array float 4608))        ;; (C) far-end radius: radius != radius2 = a TAPERED (conical) volume
(define *phys-colmask* (new 'static 'array int64 4608))      ;; chain-applicability bits (bit c)
(define *phys-coltier* (new 'static 'array int32 4608))      ;; 1 = core (every level), 2 = extended
(define *phys-colside* (new 'static 'array int32 4608))      ;; (Z) 0 none / 1 L / 2 R — see *phys-cside*
;; (Y) A COLLIDER THAT RIDES ANOTHER CHAIN'S SIMULATED TIP instead of an animated bone. -1 = a real
;; bone (everything before cycle 5). The owner's description of Keira is that her breasts "s'entre-
;; choquent" — they collide with EACH OTHER, which no bone-mounted volume can express: both bones
;; are animated and neither knows where the other one has actually swung to. Declared as
;; `at=<chain>` on a collider line; the anchor joint is still parsed and must exist, so a rig that
;; lacks it drops the volume through the normal path rather than silently mis-centring it.
(define *phys-colchain* (new 'static 'array int32 4608))

;; ---- cycle 6: what each chain is ACTUALLY tested against, resolved once at bind ----------------
;; The volumes are mesh-derived now and there are up to 96 of them per actor, but a strand only
;; ever meets a handful. Walking all 96 and mask-testing each, every link, every iteration, every
;; substep, would be 6x the work for exactly the same contacts. The applicable list is resolved
;; here instead, so the hot loop is O(links x PHYS-CCMAX) whatever the pool size is.
;; CYCLE 13 — AND THE LIST IS NOW GEOMETRY, NOT DATA. See phys-chain-perimeter! : rebuilt every
;; frame from the volumes this chain can actually reach, so `chains=` cannot license a pass-through.
(define *phys-cclist* (new 'static 'array int32 55296))     ;; slot*PHYS-CPS*PHYS-CCMAX + c*PHYS-CCMAX + n
(define *phys-ccn* (new 'static 'array int32 576))          ;; how many entries of that list are live
;; (C13) per-chain bounding sphere for this frame: centre = the chain's anchor, radius = the
;; furthest any of its links sits from that anchor (model pose OR simulated pose, whichever is
;; further) plus that link's own mesh radius. It is what makes "can this chain reach that volume"
;; and "can these two chains reach each other" answerable from geometry instead of from a data key.
(define *phys-cbsp* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 576)) ;; bounding-sphere centre (anchor)
(define *phys-cbsr* (new 'static 'array float 576))         ;; bounding-sphere radius, 0 = not live
(define *phys-cctrunc* (new 'static 'array int32 24))       ;; per-slot: chain-frames whose list overflowed
(define *phys-slot-ccpairs* (new 'static 'array int32 24))  ;; chain pairs link-tested this window
(define *phys-slot-ccnsum* (new 'static 'array int32 24))   ;; sum of per-chain tested-volume counts
;; (C13) the guaranteed-feasible fallback's own three numbers. mfsnap = links returned toward their
;; MODEL pose because the iterative repair had not cleared them; mfsnapmax = the largest such move,
;; so the size of what the fallback is doing is readable rather than assumed; mfhard = the times not
;; even the model pose was clear, which the closed-form guarantee does not cover (an `at=` volume
;; riding a partner chain that has swung). A fallback that had to give up must never go unreported.
(define *phys-slot-mfsnap* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-mfsnapmax* (new 'static 'array float 24))
(define *phys-slot-mfhard* (new 'static 'array int32 24))

;; ---- cycle 6b: THE MODEL POSE IS THE FLOOR OF EVERY COLLISION VOLUME --------------------------
;; Owner rule W, applied to collision instead of only to the spring: "la position idle devrait etre
;; celle du modele de base". A volume that CONTAINS the pose Naughty Dog modelled for a strand is
;; asserting that the character intersects itself, and the only thing it can do is shove that strand
;; somewhere ND never put it — permanently, because the shove never ends. That is measurable and it
;; was measured: Maia's two chest chains sat 131 and 180 units off their modelled pose with a
;; clearance of -0.99 (inside the surface, but under PHYS-PEN-TOL so no push-out was even recorded),
;; and Keira's chain 5 at -2.79. Both are `at=` volumes, which the offline fitter never clearance-
;; tested at all (it only shrinks bone capsules), and the same hole exists for every xchain pair.
;; So the bound is enforced HERE, at runtime, where it cannot be forgotten by a generator: for each
;; (link, volume) pair the effective radius is capped at the distance from that link's own MODEL
;; pose to that volume's spine, less a hair of margin. Consequences, in order of importance:
;;   * a chain at rest is never held off the pose the model gives it -> restdevA is free to reach 0;
;;   * nothing is allowed any closer to the body than the model itself is, so the anti-clipping
;;     blocker is untouched (the cap can only ever remove a region the character already occupies);
;;   * it tracks the ANIMATION: when Jak folds an arm against his chest the cap opens exactly as far
;;     as the authored pose does, which is the authored-priority rule expressed in geometry.
;; Computed once per (link, volume) per frame, before the substep loop, so the substep sweep, the
;; final resolve and the residual audit all grade the identical radius.
(define *phys-ccap* (new 'static 'array float 4608))        ;; link*PHYS-CCMAX + n, valid for the chain in hand

;; ---- cycle 6 problem 2: the physics elements get a volume of THEIR OWN ------------------------
;; Owner 01:45: "les elements ayant de la physique EUX-MEMES n'ont pas de colliders, donc
;; evidemment si deux entrent en collision ca clip." A chain was a line of dimensionless points: it
;; could be pushed out of the body, but two chains could not see each other at all — hence the
;; metal buckle through Jak's own hanging strap, Keira's goggles into her chest and her front
;; strands through her ears. Each LINK now carries a radius measured from the mesh it drives (the
;; inner-quartile thickness of its own skinned vertices about the strand axis), and chains named by
;; xchain= are resolved against each other link by link.
(define *phys-lrad* (new 'static 'array float 1152))        ;; slot*PHYS-JPS + joint: per-LINK radius
;; (C14) MESH-SURFACE AUDIT STATE. The owner's eyes live on the skinned mesh and every bone-level
;; counter before this produced a zero he could refute by looking (the mayor's bow links sat within
;; tolerance while his ribbon pierced his belly — its mesh extends 3.5-6x beyond its link radii,
;; measured). Each link caches up to PHYS-MSAM extremal skinned-vertex offsets (bone-local bind
;; space, from physics_mesh.txt); every frame they are carried by the link's CURRENT bone rotation
;; and audited — and resolved — against the body volumes, with the authored pose as the floor.
(define *phys-msn* (new 'static 'array int32 1152))         ;; slot*PHYS-JPS + joint: sample count
(define *phys-msam* (new 'static 'array float 17280))       ;; (slot*PHYS-JPS + joint)*15 + si*3 + coord
;; (C14-A) per-chain window max deviation ON LOCOMOTION FRAMES ONLY (own anchor > PHYS-RUN-ANCH).
;; This is the number the hairrun/chestrun floors read: a dead sim maxes every calm ceiling, so
;; calm may never again be bought by killing motion.
(define *phys-crun* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-canchd* (new 'static 'array float 576))       ;; per-chain THIS-FRAME own-anchor travel
;; ---- (C16) THE FLOOR crun WAS NOT ---------------------------------------------------------------
;; Owner 2026-08-10, on a build whose floors read hairrun=619.7 / chestrun=352.5: "les pans de veste
;; NE BOUGENT PAS DU TOUT ; les meches de Keira sont ANCREES ; la poitrine de Keira completement
;; statique." Both statements are true at once, and the arithmetic says why: `crun` above is a MAX of
;; `dev` = |out - targ|, the deviation MAGNITUDE. A chain held at a CONSTANT offset of 352 units
;; scores 352 while welded to the animation — which is precisely what "ancrees" describes. The tell
;; was in the log the whole time and I read past it: chestrun printed 352.4841, the same digits, on
;; every leg for three days. A measurement of a live oscillation does not repeat to four decimals; a
;; deterministic constant does.
;; Consequence, and it is the whole week: the three motion suppressors stacked in this file (calm
;; ceilings, authored-priority suspension, collision clamps) could drive the sim to zero without
;; reddening a single gate, because every calm ceiling is one-sided in the same direction and the
;; only floor was blind to motion by construction.
;; THE QUANTITY BELOW is the one my own memory already prescribes (magnitude-is-not-motion, and
;; drift-metric-attribution rule 5): difference the WRITTEN OUTPUT frame to frame. Not the raw world
;; position — a chain rigidly welded to a running character sweeps metres of world space per second
;; and would score high while visually dead, the same false green wearing the opposite hat — but the
;; PHYSICS OFFSET (out - targ), which divides the body carry out. A constant offset scores exactly 0.
;; An oscillation scores its own per-frame travel. It cannot be maximised by holding still and it
;; cannot be maximised by being carried.
;;   cvsum/cvn = MEAN per-frame |offset(t) - offset(t-1)| over locomotion frames  -> `tvar`
;;   cvmax     = the worst single frame, so a mean flattened by a long window is still readable
;;   cdmax-cdmin = the SPREAD of the deviation over the same frames -> `dspan`, the dispersion the
;;               spec asks for as "variance". The range, not the second moment, deliberately: E[d^2]
;;               and E[d]^2 are both ~3.6e5 here and cancel to a small difference in 32-bit float
;;               over thousands of frames, which is a precision trap on a metric whose entire job is
;;               to distinguish "small" from "zero". The range has no such cancellation and detects a
;;               constant exactly.
(define *phys-cvsum* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-cvn*   (new 'static 'array int32 576))
(define *phys-cvmax* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-cdmin* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-cdmax* (new 'static 'array float 576))
;; (C16) THE EXPLICIT INERTNESS DETECTOR, per chain, which SPEC 16 requires by name.
;;   cish = frames in this window on which THIS chain's own anchor really moved and the chain was
;;          neither settling in from a cut nor owned by the authored animation. It is the sample
;;          count, and it is printed: cish=0 means the chain was never judged, which is reported as
;;          UNJUDGED and never as healthy. Five vacuous zeros shipped before this rule existed.
;;   civ  = the sum of the written joint's frame-to-frame motion over exactly those frames, so
;;          civ/cish is the MEAN motion of the bone the renderer draws while something was driving
;;          it. Below PHYS-INERT-BAR over PHYS-INERT-N samples the chain is INERT and the phase
;;          fails, by chain and by name — that is the owner's "ANCREES" / "COMPLETEMENT STATIQUE"
;;          turned into a number that a welded chain cannot pass.
(define *phys-cish* (new 'static 'array int32 576))
(define *phys-civ*  (new 'static 'array float 576))
;; mean written motion (units/frame) under which a DRIVEN chain is declared inert. 0.25 units is
;; 0.06 mm per frame: this is an inertness test, not a quality bar — anything the eye could call
;; movement is orders of magnitude above it, so a chain that fails it really is welded.
(defconstant PHYS-INERT-BAR 0.25)
;; ...and how many driven frames must be observed before the verdict means anything.
(defconstant PHYS-INERT-N 30)
;; (C14-D) resolution jerk: per-link NET resolution displacement applied this frame — the VECTOR
;; sum of every correction any pass applied to the link (substep sweep, final sweep, cross-side,
;; model fallback, strand pass, mesh sweep), folded to a length at frame end. The window keeps the
;; worst single-frame figure.
;; NET, not path length. The first ledger summed the MAGNITUDE of every correction, and the substep
;; sweep applies opposing corrections iters x substeps times per frame while it and the spring
;; argue over a pinned link: a settled, visually still link read as a 100853-unit "jump" on the
;; same device window whose every calm gate was green (jitter=23, freering=29, rested>0,
;; clamped=18 in the whole leg). What the eye reads as a snap is where the bone ENDED the frame
;; relative to where resolution found it — the net. A real one-frame snap (mfsnap, a deep
;; first-contact push) nets exactly its visible size, so the bound still catches it.
(define *phys-lresv* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
;; (C14) per-chain modelled length, written by the sim loop the frame it is computed, read by the
;; mesh sweep to bound its push exactly as the body pass bounds its own (PHYS-MAXCORR-REL of the
;; chain's own length — never a fixed hand-picked constant that cannot converge).
(define *phys-cchlen* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(define *phys-slot-resjerk* (new 'static 'array float 24))
(define *phys-slot-meshpen* (new 'static 'array float 24))  ;; residual mesh-surface penetration AFTER resolve (window max, authored-floored)
(define *phys-slot-mraw* (new 'static 'array float 24))     ;; BEFORE resolve — the positive control's needle
(define *phys-slot-mfix* (new 'static 'array int32 24))     ;; mesh-sample pushes applied (window)
(define *phys-slot-mtested* (new 'static 'array int32 24))  ;; samples actually tested (window) — 0 = the audit did not run, never a clean zero
;; (C14c) per-link deviation from the AUTHORED pose at the end of the previous frame.
;; The resolution-jerk metric differences against this — see the fold at the end of the sim loop for
;; why the correction-ledger above could not be the answer, and why the character's own motion has
;; to be divided out before a number can be called "a jump the eye sees".
(define *phys-ldev* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
;; (C14c-4) the previous frame's AUTHORED position per link, so a frame on which the ANIMATION
;; itself jumped can be told apart from one on which the resolution did. On a cinematic cut the
;; actor is re-posed wholesale: targ leaps, the verlet chain lags a frame, and the authored-relative
;; offset changes by the size of the cut — which is the animation's doing, not the resolution's.
;; The measured tell that this is what sidekick-human-lod0's intro figure is: it read 2713.4941 on
;; FOUR consecutive builds carrying four different solvers, bit for bit. Nothing the solver does is
;; bit-identical across a rewrite; a scripted cut is. Teleport/settle frames are already excluded
;; from every instrument in this file via csettle (see the note at the top of the window block) —
;; this closes the case the anchor-move detector cannot see, where the actor is re-posed without
;; his anchor travelling.
(define *phys-ltarg* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
(defconstant PHYS-CUT-DELTA 8192.0)   ;; 2 m of authored travel in ONE frame = a cut, not motion
;; (C14c) the OLD ledger's figure, still computed and still printed next to the corrected one. The
;; instrument changed, so both numbers ship: a silent swap is how a metric gets quietly relaxed.
(define *phys-slot-respath* (new 'static 'array float 24))
;; ---- (C14-D/cycle-15) the slew bound's own counters, and resjerk's ATTRIBUTION -----------------
;; resjerk is a magnitude; it never said WHICH WAY. These four say it, so the next reading of that
;; number is diagnosable from the log instead of from a rebuild:
;;   jgcut   times the growth cap actually bit (0 = the bound never had to act)
;;   jtfall  times the mesh clamp had to tighten HARDER than the rate limit because the softened
;;           fraction still penetrated — the blocker overriding smoothness, counted, never hidden
;;   rjup    worst per-frame GROWTH of |out - targ| in the window
;;   rjdn    worst per-frame SHRINK of the same
;;   rjtm    |targ - ltarg| on the very frame that set resjerk: how much of that "jump" was the
;;           AUTHORED pose moving out from under a lagging chain rather than the solver moving it
(define *phys-slot-jgcut* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-jtfall* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
;;   rjpre   the worst per-frame offset change as it stood BEFORE the mesh clamp. resjerk - rjpre
;;           is therefore the clamp's own share of the jerk, separable in the log.
;;   jdcut   times the EXCURSION ceiling (PHYS-DEV-MAX) bit
;;   jdmax   the largest offset it ever had to trim, so "how far out was it really" is a number
(define *phys-slot-rjpre* (new 'static 'array float 24))
(define *phys-slot-jdcut* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-jdmax* (new 'static 'array float 24))
(define *phys-slot-rjup* (new 'static 'array float 24))
(define *phys-slot-rjdn* (new 'static 'array float 24))
(define *phys-slot-rjtm* (new 'static 'array float 24))
;; ---- (C16) THE THREE MOTION SUPPRESSORS, EACH AS A SHARE OF FRAMES ------------------------------
;; The spec's last requirement, and the one that turns "the sim is dead" from a verdict into an
;; address: each mechanism that can stop a chain moving must say how often it actually did. All
;; three already had counters; none had a DENOMINATOR, so none could be read as a rate.
;;   simcf    chain-frames actually simulated in the window — the denominator for all three
;;   clampcf  chain-frames on which the jerk bound or the excursion ceiling actually bit for that
;;            chain (jgcut/jdcut count LINK events, which cannot be turned into a share of frames)
;; The other two divide counters that are already chain-frames: authhold (authored priority owns the
;; chain) and rested (the calm rest state holds it). Bar from the spec: anything above ~20 % of
;; frames is the culprit and gets loosened.
(define *phys-slot-simcf* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-clampcf* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
;; (C14c) bisection steps for the mesh sweep's feasibility clamp. 6 steps = 1/64 of the link's own
;; deviation, i.e. under a unit for anything this sim actually moves.
(defconstant PHYS-MESH-BISECT 6)
;; ---- (C14-D/cycle-15) THE PER-FRAME BOUND THE SPEC ASKS FOR AND THE FILE NEVER HAD -------------
;; SPEC 6: "RESOLUTION LISSE ... Deplacement par frame borne (resjerk), pas d'oscillation, pas de
;; saut visible." Audited 2026-08-09: there was NO per-frame slew limit anywhere on the physics
;; OFFSET (out - targ). `maxcorr` (PHYS-MAXCORR-REL, 0.5 x the chain's own length) bounds ONE
;; collision push; nothing bounded what a whole frame did to a link, and nothing at all bounded the
;; mesh clamp's fraction on the way DOWN — it may bisect from tcap to 0 in a single frame, which
;; collapses the entire deviation onto the authored pose between two frames. Both directions were
;; live in the measurement: across the 130 windows of the 21:45 device run, resjerk tracked
;; maxdev at r=0.877 (resjerk/maxdev = 0.89 babak, 0.94 jak-hd, 0.88 yakow) while maxvel — the
;; integrator's own step — stayed at 72-195. A whole deviation appearing or vanishing in one frame,
;; by something that is not the integrator: that is the owner's "des trucs BIZARRES plus genants
;; qu'un simple clipping".
;; PHYS-JERK-CAP is that bound, in units: how much a link's offset from its authored pose may
;; CHANGE — as a vector, so it covers growth, collapse and reorientation alike — in one frame.
;; 500 units = 12 cm, i.e. ~7 m/s of offset change at 60 Hz. The number is chosen against the
;; measurements it must not touch, not by taste: the worst per-frame offset GROWTH any chain in
;; the cast produced across the 23:0x device run was 466 (rjup, over five legs), and the two
;; ratcheted locomotion peaks are hairrun 627.19 and chestrun 352.48 — both accumulated over
;; several frames, neither reachable in one. So the bound sits above every legitimate frame this
;; sim has ever produced and below every jump the owner has complained about (1011-1161).
(defconstant PHYS-JERK-CAP 500.0)
;; ...and the ceiling on the offset ITSELF, which is the other half of the same problem and was
;; only forced into the open once the jerk bound existed. With the bound in, three legs came in at
;; 528-629 and D-MAYOR read 1307.07 — and its attribution said, in one line, that this was not the
;; bound failing: rjpre 500.06 (the bound held), rjdn 1307.07 == resjerk == maxdev == that chain's
;; own window deviation, all four the SAME number. babak-lod0's chain 1 had left its authored pose
;; by 1307 units (32 cm), the mesh clamp found that pose infeasible, and collapsed the whole of it
;; onto the authored pose in one frame. The clamp had no choice: it may not commit a penetrating
;; pose, so at that point it is COLLAPSE OR PENETRATE, and penetrating is the one thing forbidden.
;; The only remaining lever is therefore the EXCURSION, and it should have been bounded anyway — a
;; background villager's chain sitting a third of a metre off its authored pose is not "subtle
;; secondary motion", it is the thing the owner has described from the start as "l'entierete des
;; cheveux bouge, comme detachee du crane" and "ca part un peu en live".
;; 800 units = 19.5 cm. Chosen against the same measurements as the jerk cap: it is ABOVE both
;; ratcheted locomotion peaks by construction (hairrun 613-630, chestrun 352.48, so neither can be
;; trimmed by it) and BELOW every excursion that produced a collapse (babak 1307, yakow 1123,
;; mayor's tie 2304). Applied by scaling the offset along its own direction, i.e. towards the
;; authored pose, which is the direction that can only reduce penetration; the clamp's
;; length-preserving re-seat runs after it, as with the jerk cap.
(defconstant PHYS-DEV-MAX 800.0)
;; ...and the matching bound on the way down: the mesh clamp may not tighten its per-chain fraction
;; by more than this in one frame WHEN A CLEAR POSE EXISTS at the softened fraction. It is a rate
;; limit, never a licence: if the softened fraction penetrates, the bisection runs on the full
;; range exactly as before and the blocker still wins — that case is counted (jtfall=) rather than
;; hidden, because it is the one path by which a one-frame collapse can still happen.
;; 0.25 = the chain converges onto a needed clamp in 4 frames instead of 1; the release side
;; already had such a limit (PHYS-TMIN-RISE 0.08), only the tightening side did not.
(defconstant PHYS-TMIN-FALL 0.25)
;; (C14c) the bone the mesh sweep is currently moving, so phys-mesh-pen can refuse to test a link
;; against a volume that RIDES THAT SAME BONE. Set by phys-link-mesh-worst, its only caller.
;; Not a parameter because phys-mesh-pen is already at GOAL's 8-argument ceiling.
(define *phys-mesh-selfk* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
;; (C14c-2) one chain's candidate pose at a blend fraction — see phys-chain-blend!.
(define *phys-cblend* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 48))
;; (C14c-2) the frame's PRE-CLAMP simulated pose. The blend fraction is always applied from HERE,
;; never from the running *phys-out*: the sweep makes two passes, and blending pass 2 from a pose
;; pass 1 had already blended applies the fraction twice (targ + t^2*(out-targ)). That compounding
;; over-clamps and, because t moves frame to frame, turns a smooth pull-back into a jumpy one — it
;; took D-INTRO's resolution jerk from 1231 to 3754 while flattering every penetration number.
(define *phys-out0* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 1152))
;; (C14c-2) the blend fraction this chain committed LAST frame. The clamp engages instantly (a
;; penetration is not negotiable) but is released at PHYS-TMIN-RISE per frame, so handing the
;; physics back is a ramp instead of a step — the same shape rule (A) already imposes on authored
;; suspension, and half of what the resolution-jerk bound is measuring.
(define *phys-ctmin* (new 'static 'array float 576))
(defconstant PHYS-TMIN-RISE 0.08)
(define *phys-cxmask* (new 'static 'array int64 576))       ;; chains this chain must be collided with
;; ---- cycle-7 (AH): ANCHOR COUPLING -------------------------------------------------------------
;; The only excitation a chain had was the lag it develops behind its own moving target, and for a
;; damped spring that lag is a/omega^2 — inversely proportional to the SQUARE of the stiffness. So
;; "plus de jiggle ET un poil plus de fermete" could not be delivered by tuning: every notch of
;; firmness was paid for out of the travel. `couple=` adds the pseudo-force of the accelerating
;; anchor FRAME explicitly, so the deviation obeys d'' + 2*zeta*w*d' + w^2*d = -(1+couple)*a_anchor:
;; amplitude is set by couple, firmness by stiffness, and the two stop fighting each other.
;; The anchor's acceleration is measured as the SECOND DIFFERENCE of its own world position, which
;; needs no frame rate and no assumption about how it is animated. Per CHAIN, not per link: the
;; anchor is what the whole chain hangs off.
(define *phys-ccouple* (new 'static 'array float 576))      ;; (AH) anchor-coupling gain, 0 = off
(define *phys-canchp* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 576))  ;; anchor position, previous frame
(define *phys-canchv* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 576))  ;; anchor velocity, previous frame
(define *phys-canchvp* (new 'static 'inline-array vector 576)) ;; (D) anchor velocity, previous frame — frozen arming
(define *phys-canchok* (new 'static 'array int32 576))      ;; 0 = history not usable yet (spawn/cut)
(define *phys-cinject* (new 'static 'array float 576))      ;; POSITIVE CONTROL: deliberate penetration, units
(define *phys-slot-ccc* (new 'static 'array int32 24))      ;; chain-vs-chain contacts resolved (window)
(define *phys-slot-cccmax* (new 'static 'array float 24))   ;; deepest chain-vs-chain overlap (window)
;; (C13b) THE STRAND PASS'S OWN THREE NUMBERS. It runs after the body resolve, after the model-pose
;; fallback and after the residual audit, and it writes the bone transform directly — so until now
;; nothing measured what it left behind. `xveto` counts link-pushes REFUSED because they would have
;; driven that link deeper into its own character (the owner's blocker outranks strand separation);
;; `xunres` counts contacts still overlapping after the clamp and the veto, i.e. the strand-vs-strand
;; residual this phase never had; `xunresmax` is the deepest of them. A strand-vs-strand pass with no
;; residual counter was the same shape of blind spot as a body audit with no perimeter.
;; (C13b) and the verdict for a volume RIDING another chain — a two-body contact that is neither
;; the body's residual nor a strand-vs-strand pair. It gets its own count and its own depth so that
;; taking it out of `resid` can never be a way of not counting it at all.
(define *phys-slot-xbres* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-xbresmax* (new 'static 'array float 24))
(define *phys-slot-xveto* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-xunres* (new 'static 'array int32 24))
(define *phys-slot-xunresmax* (new 'static 'array float 24))
(define *phys-slot-injected* (new 'static 'array int32 24)) ;; links deliberately displaced this window
;; (W/C6c) A LINK ANOTHER CHAIN IS HOLDING IS HELD, exactly as a link the BODY is holding is held.
;; The chain-vs-chain pass runs after the per-chain step — it cannot write that step's `lpush`
;; array — so it leaves a countdown here and the next frame seeds `lpush` from it. Without this the
;; contact and the arrival relaxation form an energy loop: the pair separates (moving `pos` AND
;; `prev` by the same delta, so the motion is invisible to every velocity reading), arrival pulls
;; the link back to the model pose, and the pair separates again, for ever. Measured on the 06:10
;; leg: jak-hd's idle drift went 0.0000 -> 5.8190 units/frame in the intro the moment arrival
;; became strong enough to fight back, and Samos' belly (pushed by his own beard, ccdepth 37.2) and
;; Maia's hair (ccdepth 286.3) carried the two worst fidelity readings of the run. Owner rule O is
;; explicit that an unsatisfiable constraint must settle rather than oscillate; this is that rule
;; applied to a collider class that was added in cycle 6, after the exemption was written.
(define *phys-lxheld* (new 'static 'array int32 1152))      ;; frames left holding this link (chain contact)
(define *phys-slot-xheld* (new 'static 'array int32 24))    ;; link-frames exempted for that reason (window)

;; gravity: 9.8 m/s^2 * 4096 units/m
(defconstant PHYS-GRAV-ACCEL 40140.8)

(defun phys-closest-on-seg! ((out vector) (a vector) (b vector) (p vector))
  "closest point of a collider's SPINE to p. A sphere passes b = a (the degenerate segment falls
  through to `a`), a capsule passes its two animated bone positions — one code path, so the
  constraint pass and the residual audit can never drift apart.
  RETURNS the segment parameter t in [0,1] of that closest point (0 for the degenerate/sphere case)
  so a TAPERED capsule (cycle 3, owner C) can interpolate its radius AT THE CONTACT — a cone. Both
  callers must use the same t or the audit would grade the push-out against a different volume."
  (let ((tt 0.0))
    (let ((ab (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
          (ap (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
      (vector-! ab b a)
      (let ((d2 (vector-dot ab ab)))
        (cond
          ((< d2 0.0001)
           (vector-copy! out a))
          (else
           (vector-! ap p a)
           (set! tt (fmax 0.0 (fmin 1.0 (/ (vector-dot ap ab) d2))))
           (vector-float*! ab ab tt)
           (vector+! out a ab)))))
    tt))

(defun phys-axis-dot ((m matrix) (r int) (v vector))
  "component of the WORLD vector v along row r of the bone matrix m, with the row NORMALIZED. Used
  only by the (R) gravity instrument: bone matrices carry rig scale, and an unnormalized dot would
  report a direction whose length changes with the character rather than one that can be read as a
  unit axis."
  (let* ((a (-> m vector r))
         (l (vector-length a)))
    (if (< l 0.000001) 0.0 (/ (vector-dot a v) l))))

(defun phys-body-pen ((slot int) (cbase int) (jbase int) (c int) (lk int) (tier int)
                      (p vector) (draw draw-control))
  "(C13b) DEEPEST BODY PENETRATION a link would have at world point p, over the SAME per-frame
  reach perimeter the solver and the residual audit use. Returns 0.0 when p is clear of all of them.

  Why this exists, and why it deliberately does NOT apply the model-pose cap: the strand-vs-strand
  pass runs AFTER the per-chain body resolve, after the model-pose fallback and after the residual
  audit, and it writes both *phys-out* and the bone transform. So a link the fallback had parked
  clear of every volume could be shoved straight back into the character by a strand contact, and
  nothing tested or counted it. That is the owner's blocker (\"NE DOIVENT PAS PASSER AU TRAVERS DU
  MESH DE LEUR PERSONNAGE ! QU'IMPORTE LA RAISON !\") surviving as a hole in the very cycle that was
  supposed to close it.
  The caller uses this to compare the SAME link before and after a candidate strand push and to
  refuse any push that goes deeper. Because it is the same link and the same volume on both sides,
  the model-pose cap cancels out of the comparison — which is the point: a strap that RESTS against
  a capsule reads the same depth before and after and is never vetoed, while a push that drives a
  strand further into the body is. Monotonicity, not absolute clearance, is what the strand pass
  owes the body pass, and it is enough: the fallback already made the pre-push point clear."
  (let ((skel (-> draw skeleton))
        (worst 0.0)
        (cpt (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (dv (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
    (dotimes (s2 (-> *phys-ccn* (+ cbase c)))
      (let* ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS)
                    (-> *phys-cclist* (+ (* slot PHYS-CPS PHYS-CCMAX) (* c PHYS-CCMAX) s2))))
             (rc (-> *phys-colchain* cb))
             (k2 (-> *phys-colk2* cb)))
        (when (and (<= (-> *phys-coltier* cb) tier) (!= rc c))
          (let* ((ca (if (>= rc 0)
                         (-> *phys-out* (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* (+ cbase rc))
                                           (+ (-> *phys-clen* (+ cbase rc)) -1)))
                         (-> skel bones (+ (-> *phys-colk* cb) 1) transform vector 3)))
                 (cbv (if (and (< rc 0) (>= k2 0))
                          (-> skel bones (+ k2 1) transform vector 3)
                          ca))
                 (r1 (-> *phys-colr* cb))
                 (tt (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt ca cbv p))
                 (rr (+ (-> *phys-lrad* lk) r1 (* tt (- (-> *phys-colr2* cb) r1)))))
            (vector-! dv p cpt)
            (let ((pen (- rr (vector-length dv))))
              (when (> pen worst) (set! worst pen)))))))
    worst))

(defun phys-chain-settle! ((slot int) (start int) (len int) (sw float) (rl0 int))
  "(C14c-4) the spawn/teleport settle ramp, made LENGTH-PRESERVING.

  It used to lerp each link's position toward the authored pose independently:
      p = targ + sw*(p - targ)
  which shortens every segment by its chord error — the exact defect the mesh clamp had, sitting in
  the one place a chain is guaranteed to be FAR from its authored pose, so the error is at its
  largest. evilsis-lod0 flies into the intro and spends her whole entrance inside this ramp; she was
  the only actor in the cast reading lenmin=0.8902 while everyone else sat at 0.9981-0.9999, and the
  figure survived every fix applied to the clamp because the clamp is not what produced it.

  Same construction as phys-chain-blend!: blend the segment DIRECTION, keep the authored length."
  (dotimes (m 2)
    (let ((da (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
          (ds (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
          (dd (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
      (dotimes (i len)
        (let* ((jj (+ start i))
               (av (if (zero? m) (-> *phys-pos* jj) (-> *phys-prev* jj))))
          (cond
            ((< i rl0)
             (vector-copy! (-> *phys-cblend* i) av))
            ((zero? i)
             (vector-! dd av (-> *phys-targ* jj))
             (vector-float*! dd dd sw)
             (vector+! (-> *phys-cblend* i) (-> *phys-targ* jj) dd))
            (else
             (let ((pv (if (zero? m) (-> *phys-pos* (+ jj -1)) (-> *phys-prev* (+ jj -1)))))
               (vector-! da (-> *phys-targ* jj) (-> *phys-targ* (+ jj -1)))
               (vector-! ds av pv))
             (let ((la (vector-length da)))
               (vector-! dd ds da)
               (vector-float*! dd dd sw)
               (vector+! dd dd da)
               (let ((ln (vector-length dd)))
                 (if (> ln 0.0001)
                     (vector-float*! dd dd (/ la ln))
                     (vector-copy! dd da)))
               (vector+! (-> *phys-cblend* i) (-> *phys-cblend* (+ i -1)) dd))))))
      (dotimes (i len)
        (when (>= i rl0)
          (let ((jj (+ start i)))
            (if (zero? m)
                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-pos* jj) (-> *phys-cblend* i))
                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-prev* jj) (-> *phys-cblend* i))))))))
  (none))

(defun phys-chain-owns-bone? ((slot int) (cbase int) (c int) (kb int) (kb2 int))
  "(C14c-3) 1 if either bone index belongs to this chain's own link set. See the call site in
  phys-mesh-pen for why a chain must not be collided against a volume it carries."
  (let ((ci (+ cbase c))
        (r 0))
    (let ((st (+ (* slot PHYS-JPS) (-> *phys-cstart* ci)))
          (ln (-> *phys-clen* ci)))
      (dotimes (q ln)
        (let ((j (-> *phys-jk* (+ st q))))
          (when (or (= j kb) (and (>= kb2 0) (= j kb2)))
            (set! r 1)))))
    r))

(defun phys-mesh-pen ((slot int) (cbase int) (c int) (tier int)
                      (p vector) (ap vector) (outdir vector) (draw draw-control))
  "(C14) deepest EFFECTIVE penetration of a mesh-surface sample at world point p into the chain's
  BODY volumes, floored by the authored pose: for each volume the sample's penetration at ap — the
  SAME offset carried by the authored bone position — is subtracted first, so a region the
  character's own sculpted/keyed pose already occupies is never reported and never fought (the
  identical rule the per-link ccap encodes, evaluated at the sample instead of the link).
  Body volumes only (colchain < 0): a volume riding another chain is a two-body contact and stays
  in the strand/xbres domain, where one link's push cannot pretend to fix it.
  The sample IS the surface, so no link radius and no sample radius is added — rr is the volume's
  own interpolated cone radius, nothing else. Writes the push-out direction (unit, away from the
  worst volume's spine) into outdir when the return is > 0."
  (let ((worst 0.0)
        (cpt (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (dv (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (av (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (skel (-> draw skeleton)))
    (dotimes (s2 (-> *phys-ccn* (+ cbase c)))
      (let* ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS)
                    (-> *phys-cclist* (+ (* slot PHYS-CPS PHYS-CCMAX) (* c PHYS-CCMAX) s2))))
             (rc (-> *phys-colchain* cb))
             (k2 (-> *phys-colk2* cb)))
        ;; (C14c) A LINK IS NOT TESTED AGAINST A VOLUME THAT RIDES ITS OWN BONE. This is not an
        ;; opt-out of collision (colskip is gone and stays gone) — it is the exclusion of a
        ;; DEGENERATE self-test, and leaving it in was the whole of jak-hd's residual.
        ;; `capsule MhairA MhairB` on jak-hd is literally the hair chain's own two joints: the
        ;; capsule is built AROUND the strand, so the strand's mesh is inside it by construction.
        ;; The authored floor is supposed to cancel exactly that, and it cannot here, because the
        ;; floor point (the authored bone position) is tested against the volume WHERE THE SIM HAS
        ;; ALREADY MOVED IT — the volume travelled with the bone. So pena reads ~0 while pen reads
        ;; the full radius, and the pass manufactures a penetration that no geometry contains.
        ;; Measured: jak-hd carries 28 such capsules of 81 and was the only actor left with a
        ;; residual (207.06 with every other actor at 0.00-9.74) and the worst clamp.
        ;; It also broke the feasibility guarantee outright: the bisection probes with the bone at
        ;; the candidate position, then the commit MOVES the bone, so a self-riding volume is in a
        ;; different place at commit than at probe and the point verified clear no longer is.
        ;; Volumes on every OTHER bone — torso, head, thighs, the rest of the body — are tested
        ;; exactly as before, so nothing the owner can see gains permission to pass through.
        ;; (C14c-3) ...AND "ITS OWN BONE" MEANS THE WHOLE CHAIN, not just this one link.
        ;; The single-bone test above closed `capsule MhairA MhairB` for the link that IS MhairB,
        ;; and left the identical problem one link away. dax-hd is the proof: his ear volumes ride
        ;; his ear chain's own joints (`capsule earBaseR earMidR`, `capsule flapBaseR flapMidR`),
        ;; so testing earTip against them tests a strand against a capsule THE STRAND CARRIES. It
        ;; is degenerate for the same reason, and it also keeps moving during the sweep — a sibling
        ;; link's commit relocates the volume between the feasibility probe and the final audit, so
        ;; the pose verified clear is no longer the pose measured. That is the whole of the residual
        ;; left standing: with every other actor at meshpen=0.0000 across three legs, dax-hd alone
        ;; sat at 3.17-3.19 and would not converge however many corrective passes were added.
        ;; Excluded here: volumes whose spine rides a joint of THIS chain. Still tested: every
        ;; volume on an animated bone — torso, head, hips, thighs, arms — i.e. the entire body the
        ;; owner can watch a strand disappear into.
        (when (and (<= (-> *phys-coltier* cb) tier) (< rc 0)
                   (zero? (phys-chain-owns-bone? slot cbase c (-> *phys-colk* cb) k2)))
          (let* ((ca (-> skel bones (+ (-> *phys-colk* cb) 1) transform vector 3))
                 (cbv (if (>= k2 0) (-> skel bones (+ k2 1) transform vector 3) ca))
                 (r1 (-> *phys-colr* cb))
                 (tt (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt ca cbv p))
                 (rr (+ r1 (* tt (- (-> *phys-colr2* cb) r1)))))
            (vector-! dv p cpt)
            (let* ((dd (vector-length dv))
                   (pen (- rr dd)))
              (when (> pen 0.0)
                ;; the authored floor, at THIS volume: the same offset on the authored bone
                (let* ((tta (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt ca cbv ap))
                       (rra (+ r1 (* tta (- (-> *phys-colr2* cb) r1)))))
                  (vector-! av ap cpt)
                  (let* ((pena (fmax 0.0 (- rra (vector-length av))))
                         (eff (- pen pena)))
                    (when (> eff worst)
                      (set! worst eff)
                      (cond
                        ((> dd 0.0001) (vector-float*! outdir dv (/ 1.0 dd)))
                        (else
                         (set! (-> outdir x) 0.0)
                         (set! (-> outdir y) 1.0)
                         (set! (-> outdir z) 0.0)
                         (set! (-> outdir w) 0.0))))))))))))
    worst))

;; NB: `nms` and `ci` are derived here rather than passed — GOAL caps a real function at 8
;; parameters and this needs exactly the eight below.
(defun phys-link-mesh-worst ((slot int) (cbase int) (c int) (tier int)
                             (jj int) (cand vector) (bm matrix) (draw draw-control))
  "(C14c) worst authored-floored mesh penetration over ALL of this link's samples, with the link
  ORIGIN placed at `cand`. The samples ride the link's current bone ROTATION (the sim writes only a
  translation, so the rotation is the animator's and moving the origin does not change the offsets),
  which is what lets the sweep above ask `what if the link were here?` without touching the skeleton.

  The one property the whole clamp rests on: at cand = *phys-targ* every sample's test point and its
  own authored floor point are THE SAME POINT, so pen == pena and this returns exactly 0.0 — for
  every volume, simultaneously. The authored pose is therefore always feasible, which is why a
  bisection toward it cannot fail to find a feasible t, and why it cannot be defeated by the
  overshoot that made the old per-sample push loop oscillate between two volumes (measured on
  device: meshpen 475.15 out of mraw 502.55 after three FULL-depth pushes — the resolve was moving
  the link out of one volume straight into its neighbour and back)."
  (set! (-> *phys-mesh-selfk* slot) (-> *phys-jk* jj))
  (let ((worst 0.0)
        (ci (+ cbase c))
        (nms (-> *phys-msn* jj))
        (wof (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (tv (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (sp (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (apv (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (mdir (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
    (dotimes (si nms)
      (vector-float*! wof (the-as vector (-> bm vector 0))
                      (-> *phys-msam* (+ (* jj 15) (* si 3))))
      (vector-float*! tv (the-as vector (-> bm vector 1))
                      (-> *phys-msam* (+ (* jj 15) (* si 3) 1)))
      (vector+! wof wof tv)
      (vector-float*! tv (the-as vector (-> bm vector 2))
                      (-> *phys-msam* (+ (* jj 15) (* si 3) 2)))
      (vector+! wof wof tv)
      (set! (-> wof w) 0.0)
      (vector+! sp cand wof)
      (vector+! apv (-> *phys-targ* jj) wof)
      (let ((eff (phys-mesh-pen slot cbase c tier sp apv mdir draw)))
        ;; (AF) THE AUTHORED POSE IS AS LEGITIMATE A FLOOR AS THE MODELLED ONE. Keira pulling her
        ;; goggles over her eyes puts their MESH inside the head volume on purpose; a targ-only
        ;; floor would shove them out of her face while her hand still holds them.
        (when (and (> (-> *phys-cauththr* ci) 0.0)
                   (> eff PHYS-PEN-TOL))
          (let ((ap2 (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
                (md2 (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
            (vector+! ap2 (-> *phys-anim* jj) wof)
            (let ((eff2 (phys-mesh-pen slot cbase c tier sp ap2 md2 draw)))
              (when (< eff2 eff)
                (set! eff eff2)))))
        (when (> eff worst)
          (set! worst eff))))
    worst))

(defun phys-chain-blend! ((slot int) (ci int) (start int) (len int) (tt float) (rl0 int))
  "(C14c-2) write this chain's pose at blend fraction `tt` into *phys-cblend*, LENGTH-PRESERVING.

  Only the DIRECTION of each segment is blended between the authored pose and the simulated one;
  the segment keeps its AUTHORED length exactly. A straight positional lerp — the obvious way to
  write this, and the way it was written first — shortens every segment by its chord error, which
  is how the clamp drove evilsis-lod0 (Maia, the most heavily clamped chain in the cast because
  her hair is what was going through her body) to lenmin=0.8759 while every other actor sat at
  0.9859-0.9999. Owner rule X is that nothing may TASSER, and an anti-clipping fix that crushes
  the strand it rescues has simply moved the defect.

  tt=0 is the authored pose, which is penetration-free by construction (phys-link-mesh-worst), so
  a feasible fraction always exists; tt=1 is the simulated pose with modelled segment lengths."
  (let ((da (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (ds (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
        (dd (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
    (dotimes (i len)
      (let ((jj (+ start i)))
        (cond
          ((< i rl0)
           ;; A ROOT-LOCKED LINK IS NEVER COMMITTED, so the candidate chain must be built on where
           ;; it ACTUALLY IS, not on where a blend would have put it. Building through it was a
           ;; real defect: the free links downstream were positioned from a locked predecessor that
           ;; never moved, so the segment across the lock boundary came out wrong — D-INTRO read
           ;; lenmin=0.8902 (an 11% crush) with every other leg at 0.98-0.9999, and the same
           ;; inconsistency injected spurious displacement into the resolution-jerk figure.
           (vector-copy! (-> *phys-cblend* i) (-> *phys-out0* jj)))
          ((zero? i)
           ;; the root link is positioned relative to its anchor, not to a predecessor
           (vector-! dd (-> *phys-out0* jj) (-> *phys-targ* jj))
           (vector-float*! dd dd tt)
           (vector+! (-> *phys-cblend* i) (-> *phys-targ* jj) dd))
          (else
           (vector-! da (-> *phys-targ* jj) (-> *phys-targ* (+ jj -1)))
           (vector-! ds (-> *phys-out0* jj) (-> *phys-out0* (+ jj -1)))
           (let ((la (vector-length da)))
             (vector-! dd ds da)
             (vector-float*! dd dd tt)
             (vector+! dd dd da)
             (let ((ln (vector-length dd)))
               (if (> ln 0.0001)
                   (vector-float*! dd dd (/ la ln))
                   (vector-copy! dd da)))
             (vector+! (-> *phys-cblend* i) (-> *phys-cblend* (+ i -1)) dd))))))
    (none)))

(defun phys-chain-worst ((slot int) (cbase int) (c int) (tier int)
                         (start int) (len int) (rl0 int) (draw draw-control))
  "(C14c-2) worst authored-floored mesh penetration over the candidate pose currently sitting in
  *phys-cblend* — i.e. `if the chain were here, would anything be inside the body?`. Only the links
  the commit will actually write are asked, because only those are the ones the candidate moves."
  (let ((worst 0.0)
        (nbones (-> (-> draw skeleton) length)))
    (dotimes (i len)
      (when (>= i rl0)
        (let* ((jj (+ start i))
               (k (-> *phys-jk* jj)))
          (when (and (> (-> *phys-msn* jj) 0) (< (+ k 1) nbones))
            (let* ((bm (the-as matrix (-> (-> draw skeleton) bones (+ k 1) transform)))
                   (e (phys-link-mesh-worst slot cbase c tier jj (-> *phys-cblend* i) bm draw)))
              (when (> e worst)
                (set! worst e)))))))
    worst))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; WAVE 2 slot pool. A "slot" is one simulated ACTOR: its parent table, its chains, its verlet
;; state. Nothing in here knows what kind of process owns it — that is the whole point of wave 2.
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defun phys-slot-find ((pid int))
  "the sim slot bound to this process, or -1."
  (let ((r -1))
    (dotimes (s PHYS-SLOTS)
      (when (and (< r 0) (= (-> *phys-slot-pid* s) pid))
        (set! r s)))
    r))

(defun phys-slot-free! ((slot int))
  (set! (-> *phys-slot-pid* slot) 0)
  (set! (-> *phys-slot-rider* slot) 0)
  (set! (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot) 0)
  (set! (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot) 0)
  (none))

(defun phys-slot-claim ((pid int) (rider? int))
  "claim a free slot. Companions take the bottom of the pool ascending, riders the top descending,
  so a crowded village can never starve an HD companion. Rider slots are reclaimed by AGE: a stock
  actor is a plain process-drawable with no deactivate hook of ours, so a slot whose owner stopped
  stepping for a few frames is dead by definition."
  (let ((r -1))
    (cond
      ((zero? rider?)
       (dotimes (s PHYS-COMP-SLOTS)
         (when (and (< r 0) (zero? (-> *phys-slot-pid* s)))
           (set! r s))))
      (else
       (let ((now (the int (current-time))))
         ;; reap stale riders first
         (dotimes (i (- PHYS-SLOTS PHYS-COMP-SLOTS))
           (let ((s (- (- PHYS-SLOTS 1) i)))
             (when (and (nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-pid* s))
                        (nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-rider* s))
                        (> (- now (-> *phys-slot-stamp* s)) 8))
               (phys-slot-free! s)))))
       (dotimes (i (- PHYS-SLOTS PHYS-COMP-SLOTS))
         (let ((s (- (- PHYS-SLOTS 1) i)))
           (when (and (< r 0) (zero? (-> *phys-slot-pid* s)))
             (set! r s))))))
    (when (>= r 0)
      (set! (-> *phys-slot-pid* r) pid)
      (set! (-> *phys-slot-rider* r) rider?)
      (set! (-> *phys-slot-stamp* r) (the int (current-time))))
    r))

(defun phys-fill-par-from-table! ((slot int) (par (pointer uint8)) (n int))
  "companion path: copy the k->e prep table's HD parent column into the slot."
  (let ((pbase (* slot PHYS-MAXJ)))
    (dotimes (k (min PHYS-MAXJ n))
      (set! (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase k)) (-> par k))))
  (none))

(defun phys-fill-par-from-jgeo! ((slot int) (jgeo art-joint-geo) (n int))
  "rider path: the STOCK rig carries its own hierarchy — `joint.parent` is a pointer to the parent
  joint and `joint.number` is that joint's index into jgeo data (this is exactly what
  make-nodes-from-jg uses to wire the cspaces). No offline table, no prep step: any actor in the
  game can be simulated the frame it spawns."
  (let ((pbase (* slot PHYS-MAXJ)))
    (dotimes (k (min PHYS-MAXJ n))
      (let ((j (-> jgeo data k))
            (p 255))
        (when (-> j parent)
          (let ((pn (-> j parent number)))
            (when (and (>= pn 0) (< pn PHYS-MAXJ))
              (set! p pn))))
        (set! (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase k)) (the uint8 p)))))
  (none))

(defun phys-slot-bind! ((slot int) (draw draw-control) (ag string) (rig int))
  "resolve ONE actor's chains from the data file against its live jgeo, into an already-claimed
  slot. Joint names -> (chain,link) via pc-physics-joint-role; the chain ORDER is then derived from
  the rig's own parent table (*phys-par*, filled by the caller from the companion prep table or
  straight from the jgeo), and link0's parent becomes the animated anchor.
  RIG-AGNOSTIC BY CONSTRUCTION: `ag` is just the params key (a companion art-group name for an HD
  companion, the JOINT-GEO name for a stock rider) and `rig` is just the joint count — nothing here
  touches jak-hd. That is what lets the same solver run on every actor in the game."
  (let* ((jgeo (-> draw jgeo))
         (nch (min PHYS-CPS (pc-physics-num-chains ag)))
         (jbase (* slot PHYS-JPS))
         (cbase (* slot PHYS-CPS))
         (pbase (* slot PHYS-MAXJ))
         (nj (min PHYS-MAXJ rig))
         (njoints 0)
         (ncols 0)
         (ndropped 0)
         (nreorder 0)
         ;; temp role tables indexed by rig joint k (k < PHYS-MAXJ by construction)
         (tchain (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 128))
         (tlink (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 128))
         ;; per-chain member SET and the order derived from the rig (both <= PHYS-JPS)
         (mem (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 48))
         (ord (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 48)))
    ;; a rig deeper than the parent-table ceiling is not a crash, but the chains cannot reference
    ;; anything past it — say so once, at bind time, instead of dropping those joints in silence.
    (when (> rig PHYS-MAXJ)
      (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S rig has ~D joints > ~D — joints past the ceiling cannot be chained~%"
              ag rig PHYS-MAXJ))
    ;; resolve every rig joint's role once
    (dotimes (k nj)
      (set! (-> tchain k) -1)
      (set! (-> tlink k) -1)
      (when (< k (-> jgeo length))
        (let ((role (pc-physics-joint-role ag (-> jgeo data k name))))
          (when (>= role 0)
            (set! (-> tchain k) (shr role 8))
            (set! (-> tlink k) (logand role #xff))))))
    ;; ---- chain build: the joint list is a SET, the ORDER comes from the RIG --------------------
    ;; The declared `j` order in physics_chains.txt is the AUTHOR's intent, but for stock NPC rigs
    ;; nobody can verify root->tip order offline: the shipped art files carry the hierarchy, not our
    ;; config. Requiring the declared order to match exactly meant one wrong line silently disabled a
    ;; whole character. So the chain's joint list is treated as a SET and the order is derived from the
    ;; rig itself: the member whose parent is not a member is the root, then each next link is the
    ;; unique member parented to the previous one. A set that is not a single parent-child path is a
    ;; data bug and is dropped LOUDLY. For every chain that already validated (all HD companions) the
    ;; derived order is identical to the declared one, so this is strictly a superset.
    (dotimes (c nch)
      (let ((ci (+ cbase c))
            (start njoints)
            (len 0)
            (bad 0)
            (nmem 0))
        ;; (1) members: every joint of THIS rig the data file assigns to chain c.
        (dotimes (k nj)
          (when (= (-> tchain k) c)
            (cond
              ((>= nmem PHYS-JPS)
               (set! bad 1))
              (else
               (set! (-> mem nmem) k)
               (+! nmem 1)))))
        (when (and (> nmem 0) (zero? bad))
          ;; (2) the root is the single member whose parent lies OUTSIDE the set (255, out of range,
          ;; or simply not a member). Two roots means the config lumped two chains into one entry.
          (let ((root -1)
                (nroots 0))
            (dotimes (i nmem)
              (let ((p (the int (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase (-> mem i)))))
                    (inset 0))
                (when (and (!= p #xff) (< p nj))
                  (dotimes (j nmem)
                    (when (= (-> mem j) p)
                      (set! inset 1))))
                (when (zero? inset)
                  (+! nroots 1)
                  (when (< root 0)
                    (set! root (-> mem i))))))
            (cond
              ((!= nroots 1)
               (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D invalid: ~D roots in the rig — not a single chain~%"
                       ag c nroots)
               (set! bad 1))
              (else
               ;; (3) walk root->tip: at every step EXACTLY one member must hang off the current one.
               (set! (-> ord 0) root)
               (let ((n 1))
                 (while (and (< n nmem) (zero? bad))
                   (let ((cur (-> ord (+ n -1)))
                         (nxt -1)
                         (nkids 0))
                     (dotimes (i nmem)
                       (when (= (the int (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase (-> mem i)))) cur)
                         (+! nkids 1)
                         (when (< nxt 0)
                           (set! nxt (-> mem i)))))
                     (cond
                       ((> nkids 1)
                        (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D invalid: branches at link ~D (declare one chain per branch)~%"
                                ag c (+ n -1))
                        (set! bad 1))
                       ((< nxt 0)
                        (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D invalid: only ~D of ~D joints connect — not a single chain~%"
                                ag c n nmem)
                        (set! bad 1))
                       (else
                        (set! (-> ord n) nxt)
                        (+! n 1))))))
               ;; (4) anchor = the root's parent: an ANIMATED bone the sim reads and never writes.
               (when (zero? bad)
                 (let ((anc (the int (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase root)))))
                   (cond
                     ((or (= anc #xff) (>= anc rig))
                      (set! bad 1))
                     (else
                      (set! (-> *phys-canchor* ci) anc)))))
               ;; (5) slot capacity
               (when (and (zero? bad) (> (+ njoints nmem) PHYS-JPS))
                 (set! bad 1))
               (when (zero? bad)
                 ;; (6) declared-vs-derived: link i of the file must BE the i-th joint of the walk.
                 ;; When it is not, the rig wins and the mismatch is named — a re-order is a config
                 ;; bug the author still wants to hear about, not a silent correction.
                 (let ((diff 0))
                   (dotimes (i nmem)
                     (when (!= (-> tlink (-> ord i)) i)
                       (set! diff 1)))
                   (when (nonzero? diff)
                     (+! nreorder 1)
                     (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D re-ordered from the rig hierarchy (declared order did not match)~%"
                             ag c)))
                 ;; (7) commit, root->tip
                 (dotimes (i nmem)
                   (set! (-> *phys-jk* (+ jbase njoints)) (-> ord i))
                   (+! njoints 1)
                   (+! len 1)))))))
        (when (nonzero? bad)
          (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D invalid (order/anchor/capacity) — disabled~%" ag c)
          (set! njoints start)
          (set! len 0))
        ;; CYCLE 2 (defects C/D): a chain whose joint NAMES resolve to nothing in the live rig
        ;; used to vanish in silence — indistinguishable from "simulated but too subtle". Name
        ;; it, loudly, and count it: a dropped chain is a data bug, never a tuning problem.
        ;; WAVE 2: only the NAMES-not-in-this-rig case prints this line. A chain killed by the
        ;; hierarchy checks above already printed its own specific reason, and stacking a
        ;; "0 of its joints exist" on top of it would send the reader hunting a typo that is not
        ;; there. Both still count as dropped.
        (when (zero? len)
          (+! ndropped 1)
          (when (zero? nmem)
            (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S chain ~D DROPPED: 0 of its joints exist in this rig~%" ag c)))
        (set! (-> *phys-cstart* ci) start)
        (set! (-> *phys-clen* ci) len)
        (set! (-> *phys-cflags* ci) (pc-physics-chain-flags ag c))
        (set! (-> *phys-cdev* ci) 0.0)
        (set! (-> *phys-canchmv* ci) 0.0)
        (vector-reset! (-> *phys-canchvp* ci))
        (set! (-> *phys-cself* ci) 0.0)
        (set! (-> *phys-cidr* ci) 0.0)
        ;; params (milli -> float) + derived
        (let ((hz (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 0))))
              (maxang (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 3)))))
          (set! (-> *phys-comega* ci) (* 6.2831855 hz))
          (set! (-> *phys-cdamp* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 1))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cgrav* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 2))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cmaxrad* ci) (* 0.017453292 maxang))
          (set! (-> *phys-cinertia* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 4))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cstretch* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 5))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cradius* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 6))))
          ;; cycle 2: root lock / freedom gradient / authored-channel mode / contact friction
          (set! (-> *phys-crootlock* ci) (/ (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 7) 1000))
          (set! (-> *phys-cgrad* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 8))))
          (set! (-> *phys-canim* ci) (/ (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 9) 1000))
          (set! (-> *phys-cexcite* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 10))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cfric* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 11))))
          ;; cycle 3: authored-animation priority / freedom floor / descendant policy
          (set! (-> *phys-cauththr* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 12))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cauthrise* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 13))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cauthfall* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 14))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cauthstiff* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 15))))
          (set! (-> *phys-crootfree* ci) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 16))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cnodesc* ci) (/ (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 17) 1000))
          (set! (-> *phys-ccolskip* ci) (/ (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 18) 1000))
          ;; (K) MASS. Owner: "on ne sent pas la masse... trop leger et JELLY". A spring with no mass
          ;; snaps to its target and rattles; mass gives the response a late start and follow-through
          ;; without touching the swing envelope, which is exactly the distinction he drew ("ne PAS
          ;; toucher a l'amplitude, c'est le comportement qui est faux").
          (set! (-> *phys-cmass* ci) (fmax 0.05 (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 19)))))
          ;; (R/T) cycle 4. Both default to the pre-cycle-4 behaviour on the C++ side, so a chain
          ;; that does not declare them is bit-identical to the build the owner already judged.
          (set! (-> *phys-chang* ci) (fmax 0.0 (fmin 1.0 (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 20))))))
          (set! (-> *phys-cswing* ci) (fmax 0.0 (fmin 1.0 (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 21))))))
          ;; ---- cycle 5: the FAMILY and the three keys it governs ---------------------------------
          ;; family/side arrive as 1/2 through the same milli scaling as everything else, so the
          ;; integer divide is the read. 0 = the chain declared nothing.
          (set! (-> *phys-cfam* ci) (/ (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 22) 1000))
          (set! (-> *phys-cside* ci) (/ (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 23) 1000))
          (set! (-> *phys-cext* ci) (fmax 0.0 (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 24)))))
          ;; (X) compression allowance. Absent key = 0 = the link may not shorten at all. This is the
          ;; one cycle-5 default that CHANGES a shipped behaviour on every chain rather than only on
          ;; the ones that opt in, and deliberately so: the symmetric bound was never authored, it
          ;; was `stretch=` being read in both directions.
          (set! (-> *phys-ccomp* ci) (fmax 0.0 (fmin 0.9 (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 25))))))
          ;; ---- cycle 6: per-LINK radius, chain-vs-chain partners, positive control -------------
          ;; (Problem 2) Until now a chain had ONE radius for its whole length, so a strand was as
          ;; thick at the tip as at the root and two strands could not see each other at all. The
          ;; radii= list is measured off the mesh each link actually drives. A link the data does
          ;; not describe falls back to the whole-chain radius=, so a file without the key behaves
          ;; exactly as the build the owner already judged.
          ;; NOTE, deliberately: the list is indexed in DECLARED joint order. A chain the binder had
          ;; to re-order from the rig hierarchy logs that fact above; the fallback below keeps such a
          ;; chain collidable rather than mis-sized, and out-of-range reads return 0 by contract.
          (set! (-> *phys-cxmask* ci) (pc-physics-chain-xmask ag c))
          (set! (-> *phys-cinject* ci)
                (fmax 0.0 (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 26)))))
          ;; (AH) anchor coupling. Clamped rather than trusted: this term is an acceleration the
          ;; data can dial up without bound, and an unbounded one would be an explosion the NaN
          ;; guard reports as a reset instead of as a bad number in a file.
          (set! (-> *phys-ccouple* ci)
                (fmax 0.0 (fmin 8.0 (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-param-mi ag c 27))))))
          (set! (-> *phys-canchok* ci) 0)
          (vector-reset! (-> *phys-canchp* ci))
          (vector-reset! (-> *phys-canchv* ci))
          (dotimes (li len)
            (let ((mi (pc-physics-chain-link-radius-mi ag c li)))
              (set! (-> *phys-lrad* (+ (* slot PHYS-JPS) start li))
                    (if (> mi 0) (* 0.001 (the float mi)) (-> *phys-cradius* ci))))
            ;; (C14) cache the link's mesh samples: extremal skinned-vertex offsets, bone-local
            ;; bind space, from physics_mesh.txt. n=0 (no file, no line, nothing beyond the link
            ;; radius) keeps the link out of meshtested= — an absent file reads as "not measured",
            ;; never as a clean mesh audit.
            (let* ((jj (+ (* slot PHYS-JPS) start li))
                   (n (min PHYS-MSAM (pc-physics-chain-msample-count ag c li))))
              (set! (-> *phys-msn* jj) n)
              (dotimes (si n)
                (dotimes (co 3)
                  (set! (-> *phys-msam* (+ (* jj 15) (* si 3) co))
                        (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-chain-msample-mi
                                             ag c (logior (ash li 3) si) co))))))))
          (set! (-> *phys-crun* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-canchd* ci) 0.0)
          ;; (C16) a re-bind is a fresh window for the temporal-variation floor too
          (set! (-> *phys-cish* ci) 0)
          (set! (-> *phys-civ* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cvsum* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cvn* ci) 0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cvmax* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cdmin* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cdmax* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-crestd* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-ccalm* ci) 0)
          (set! (-> *phys-clenr* ci) 1000000.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cclr* ci) 1000000.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-chold* ci) 0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cauthbase* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cstick* ci) 0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cring* ci) 0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cres* ci) 0)
          ;; (P) build the influence profile. wtip is never lowered — owner D is that too LITTLE of
          ;; the length moves — so continuity is bought by RAISING the root instead.
          (let* ((rl0 (max 0 (min (max 0 (+ len -1)) (-> *phys-crootlock* ci))))
                 (wtip 1.0)
                 (wroot (if (> rl0 0) (* 0.5 (-> *phys-crootfree* ci)) (-> *phys-crootfree* ci))))
            (when (> len 1)
              (let ((mn (- wtip (* PHYS-INFL-STEP (the float (+ len -1))))))
                (when (> mn wroot) (set! wroot mn))))
            (when (> wroot wtip) (set! wroot wtip))
            (dotimes (i len)
              (set! (-> *phys-infl* (+ jbase start i))
                    (if (< len 2)
                        wtip
                        (+ wroot (* (- wtip wroot)
                                    (/ (the float i) (the float (+ len -1)))))))))
          ;; a re-bind (hot params push, look switch) must not inherit a half-engaged suspension or a
          ;; stale anchor: every chain starts calm, at rest, and SETTLES in (owner B).
          (set! (-> *phys-cauth* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cauthmax* ci) 0.0)
          (set! (-> *phys-cpush* ci) 0)
          (set! (-> *phys-csettle* ci) PHYS-SETTLE)
          (vector-reset! (-> *phys-canchprev* ci)))))
    ;; body collision volumes: file order, joints resolved by name, per-chain applicability
    ;; mask + tier. A capsule needs BOTH ends present in the rig or it degrades to a sphere on
    ;; its first joint (never silently: the drop is logged).
    ;; The pool is a hard ceiling and silence about hitting it is not acceptable: before cycle 6
    ;; the excess was dropped with no log at all, so a model could declare a full body and be given
    ;; a fraction of it while every counter still read clean.
    (when (> (pc-physics-num-colliders ag) PHYS-COLS)
      (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S declares ~D colliders > pool ~D — the excess is DROPPED~%"
              ag (pc-physics-num-colliders ag) PHYS-COLS))
    (let ((ncf (min PHYS-COLS (pc-physics-num-colliders ag))))
      (dotimes (i ncf)
        (let ((found -1)
              (found2 -1)
              (cap? (= 1 (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 3))))
          (dotimes (k (-> jgeo length))
            (when (and (< found 0) (> (pc-physics-collider-is-joint ag i (-> jgeo data k name)) 0))
              (set! found k))
            (when (and cap? (< found2 0)
                       (> (pc-physics-collider-is-joint2 ag i (-> jgeo data k name)) 0))
              (set! found2 k)))
          (cond
            ((< found 0)
             (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S collider ~D DROPPED: its joint is not in this rig~%" ag i))
            (else
             (when (and cap? (< found2 0))
               (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S capsule ~D far end missing — degraded to a sphere~%" ag i))
             (let ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS) ncols)))
               (set! (-> *phys-colk* cb) found)
               (set! (-> *phys-colk2* cb) (if cap? found2 -1))
               (set! (-> *phys-colr* cb) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 0))))
               ;; (C) far-end radius. The C++ side returns field 0 verbatim when radius2= is absent,
               ;; so an untouched line stays a cylinder and the interpolation below is a no-op.
               (set! (-> *phys-colr2* cb) (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 4))))
               (set! (-> *phys-colmask* cb) (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 1))
               (set! (-> *phys-coltier* cb) (max 1 (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 2)))
               (set! (-> *phys-colside* cb) (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 5))
               ;; (Y) `at=<chain>` — this volume rides that chain's simulated tip. Validated against
               ;; the chains that actually BOUND in this slot: a reference to a chain the rig
               ;; dropped would otherwise index a stale start/len and collide against whatever the
               ;; previous occupant of that slot left behind.
               (let ((rc (pc-physics-collider-param-mi ag i 6)))
                 (set! (-> *phys-colchain* cb)
                       (cond
                         ((or (< rc 0) (>= rc nch)) -1)
                         ((< (-> *phys-clen* (+ cbase rc)) 1)
                          (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S collider ~D at=chain ~D is not bound — volume disabled~%"
                                  ag i rc)
                          -1)
                         (else rc)))))
             (+! ncols 1))))))
    ;; ---- (C13) THE PERIMETER IS NOT RESOLVED HERE ANY MORE ---------------------------------------
    ;; This is where a chain's collider list used to be copied, once, out of the `chains=` filter the
    ;; data put on each volume. That filter was the second of the three licences the owner threw the
    ;; cycle-12 build out for: all 2384 volumes carried one, so a volume tested only the chains it had
    ;; been introduced to and every other strand went through it uncounted — and, worse, the offline
    ;; generator was emitting a SEPARATE, differently-shrunk copy of each body span per chain (1009
    ;; real spans became 2384 lines, radii spread 20x on the same span), so each chain had its own
    ;; private body and a chain whose copy had been shrunk away had no volume there at all.
    ;; His rule: "le filtre chains= est une OPTIMISATION, pas une AUTORISATION. Par defaut une chaine
    ;; teste TOUT volume qu'elle peut physiquement atteindre. Le filtre ne peut qu'exclure ce qui est
    ;; geometriquement inatteignable, et cette inatteignabilite doit etre PROUVEE."
    ;; So the list is rebuilt from geometry every frame by phys-chain-perimeter! below: the only thing
    ;; that excludes a volume is being out of reach, and the reach is measured, not declared. What is
    ;; left here is the reset — an unbound slot must not inherit the previous occupant's perimeter.
    (dotimes (c nch)
      (set! (-> *phys-ccn* (+ cbase c)) 0)
      ;; (C13b) -1, NOT 0, and this was a live false positive rather than tidiness. cncol changed
      ;; meaning in cycle 13 — from "how many volumes NAMED this chain" (a property of the data, true
      ;; on every frame) to "how many this chain REACHED" (only defined on frames it was simulatable)
      ;; — and the per-window reset below was updated to the -1 "never asked" sentinel while THIS one,
      ;; on the bind path, was left at 0. So on the first window of every fresh binding each chain read
      ;; cncol == 0, and `nomask` counted the WHOLE ACTOR. That is exactly what the device reported:
      ;; jak-hd nomask=17 of 17 chains and dax-hd nomask=5 of 5, in the same window as nopose=5100
      ;; (17 chains x 300 frames un-posed) and ccnsum=0 — a window in which the perimeter rebuild had
      ;; not run once, so there was nothing to have reached. Every other window read nomask=0.
      ;; It is worth being explicit that this is a fix to a FALSE POSITIVE and not a metric being
      ;; narrowed to make a run pass: the un-posed frames of a parked spawn are frames in which the
      ;; chain is not simulated at all, so it can neither reach a volume nor clip through one. What
      ;; the counter is for — a live chain with nothing to collide against — is untouched, and the
      ;; sibling `nopose` still reports the un-posed frames in their own field.
      (set! (-> *phys-cncol* (+ cbase c)) -1)
      ;; (C14c-2) a re-bind starts the chain at full physics authority: carrying another rig's
      ;; clamp fraction over would silently throttle a chain that never needed it.
      (set! (-> *phys-ctmin* (+ cbase c)) 1.0)
      (set! (-> *phys-cbsr* (+ cbase c)) 0.0)
      (vector-reset! (-> *phys-cbsp* (+ cbase c))))
    (set! (-> *phys-cctrunc* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-ccpairs* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-ccnsum* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-mfsnap* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-mfsnapmax* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-mfhard* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-xbres* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-xbresmax* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-xveto* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-xunres* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-xunresmax* slot) 0.0)
    ;; (C14) a re-bind is a fresh window for the mesh audit and the motion floors too
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-jgcut* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-jtfall* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjpre* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-jdcut* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-jdmax* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjup* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjdn* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjtm* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-simcf* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-clampcf* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-resjerk* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-meshpen* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-mraw* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-mfix* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-mtested* slot) 0)
    ;; lresv only: msn was just cached by the chain loop above (this reset runs AFTER it), and the
    ;; mesh sweep only ever reads msn on the CURRENT chains' links, so stale entries on other
    ;; joints are unreachable rather than wiped here.
    (dotimes (k PHYS-JPS)
      (vector-zero! (-> *phys-lresv* (+ (* slot PHYS-JPS) k)))
      ;; (C14c) a re-bind invalidates the previous frame's deviation reference too: differencing
      ;; against another rig's pose would manufacture a one-frame "jump" out of nothing.
      (vector-zero! (-> *phys-ldev* (+ (* slot PHYS-JPS) k)))
      ;; ltarg is zeroed with it: a re-bind must read as a cut on its first frame, not as a
      ;; 200-metre authored jump measured against another rig's pose.
      (vector-zero! (-> *phys-ltarg* (+ (* slot PHYS-JPS) k))))
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-respath* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot) njoints)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot) nch)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-ncols* slot) ncols)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-seeded* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-frames* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-resets* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxdev* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxvel* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-calm* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-pushouts* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxpen* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-resid* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxresid* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-rootdev* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-freeroot* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-reglue* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-desc* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-nopose* slot) 0)
    ;; cycle-3 window counters. A re-bind is a fresh window: carrying an engage event or a burst
    ;; across a params push would attribute the old binding's behaviour to the new one.
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-authhold* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-autheng* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-authrel* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-authmax* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-reseed* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-burst* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-frozen* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-xheld* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-holdmax* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-jitter* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-rested* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-clamped* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-modelfall* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-mfmax* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-escape* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-escmax* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-stickmax* slot) 0)
    ;; ---- cycle-4 window counters ------------------------------------------------------------
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-idle* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-idleframes* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-settled* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-settletime* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-unsettled* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-freering* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-idleobs* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-slept* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-arrn* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-noncol* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-nomask* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-fama* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-famb* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-unclass* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-tilt* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-restdeva* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-restwin* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-xleg* slot) 0)
    ;; a MINIMUM starts at +inf, not at 0 — zeroed here it would print as a fully crushed chain
    ;; on the first window of every binding.
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-lenmin* slot) 1000000.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-lensim* slot) 1000000.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-gsamp* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-extprobe* slot) 0)
    (dotimes (j PHYS-JPS)
      (vector-reset! (-> *phys-tprev* (+ jbase j)))
      (vector-reset! (-> *phys-lastp* (+ jbase j)))
      (vector-reset! (-> *phys-oprev* (+ jbase j))))
    (vector-reset! (-> *phys-slot-gdir* slot))
    (vector-reset! (-> *phys-slot-gloc* slot))
    (dotimes (j PHYS-JPS)
      (set! (-> *phys-jdev* (+ jbase j)) 0.0))
    ;; HOT-RELOAD BOOKKEEPING: the generation this binding was produced from. phys-slot-step!
    ;; compares it every frame and re-binds when the owner pushes a new physics_chains.txt or
    ;; flips the precision level — companions AND riders, without respawning anything.
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-gen* slot) (pc-physics-generation))
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-stamp* slot) (the int (current-time)))
    ;; ONE LINE, always: GOAL caps a call at 8 parameters (format + dest + fmt + 6 args is already
    ;; the ceiling), and every `format 0` is its own logcat line on Android — so the two wave-2
    ;; fields are APPENDED through the shared string buffer instead of splitting the init line and
    ;; disarming every line-based device gate that greps it.
    (format (clear *phys-line-buf*)
            "[HD-PHYS] init ag=~S slot=~D chains=~D dropped=~D sim-joints=~D colliders=~D"
            ag slot nch ndropped njoints ncols)
    (format *phys-line-buf* " reorder=~D rider=~D" nreorder (-> *phys-slot-rider* slot))
    (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*)
    ;; (P) the influence profile is CONFIG, not per-frame state, so it is emitted once per bind
    ;; rather than every window. `profile c<idx>:w0:w1:...` root->tip, one entry per link.
    (format (clear *phys-line-buf*) "[HD-PHYS-INFL] ag=~S profile:" ag)
    (dotimes (c nch)
      (let ((ci (+ cbase c)))
        (when (> (-> *phys-clen* ci) 0)
          (format *phys-line-buf* " c~D" c)
          (dotimes (i (-> *phys-clen* ci))
            (format *phys-line-buf* ":~f" (-> *phys-infl* (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci) i)))))))
    (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*))
  (none))

(defun phys-slot-step! ((slot int) (draw draw-control) (ag string) (rig int))
  "the per-frame verlet/spring chain sim for ONE bound slot. For an HD companion it runs after
  fill-jak-hd-bones! — the freshly retargeted world matrices are the spring targets (or, under
  anim=replace/excite, the re-glued BIND-POSE matrices carried by the animated anchor). For a stock
  actor the same matrices come straight out of do-joint-math!. Either way the bones are FINAL and
  world-space when we get here, and the slot's own parent table (*phys-par*) says who hangs off
  whom — so this body never needs to know which kind of process owns the rig. See the file header
  for the algorithm."
  ;; hot-reload: pc-set-physics! re-parses physics_chains.txt whenever the owner flips the menu
  ;; toggle or the precision level, which bumps the generation. Re-binding here means a pushed
  ;; params file takes effect on companions AND riders without respawning anything.
  (let ((g (pc-physics-generation)))
    (when (!= g (-> *phys-slot-gen* slot))
      (phys-slot-bind! slot draw ag rig)))
  (let ((en (pc-physics-enabled)))
    (when (and (> en 0) (> (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot) 0)
               (nonzero? draw) (nonzero? (-> draw skeleton))
               (nonzero? (-> draw jgeo)))
      (let* ((level (+ en -1))
             (skel (-> draw skeleton))
             (hd-jgeo (-> draw jgeo))
             (nbones (-> skel length))
             (jbase (* slot PHYS-JPS))
             (cbase (* slot PHYS-CPS))
             (pbase (* slot PHYS-MAXJ))
             (substeps (max 1 (min 8 (/ (pc-physics-level-param-mi level 0) 1000))))
             (iters (max 1 (min 16 (/ (pc-physics-level-param-mi level 1) 1000))))
             ;; (C6/N) HOW MANY TIMES THE FINAL RESOLVE SWEEPS THE VOLUMES. Was a hardcoded 6.
             ;; It is Gauss-Seidel, so what is left after n sweeps decays geometrically, and the
             ;; phone gives the rate directly: on the intro leg Maia's `backhairM` was driven
             ;; 967.1 units into her body during her flight (anchmove 628129, maxvel 864 a frame)
             ;; and the six sweeps clawed it back to 13.5 — a factor of 0.53 per sweep. Six more
             ;; take that to a quarter of a unit, i.e. under PHYS-PEN-TOL, which is the difference
             ;; between the leg reporting her clean and reporting her not. Jak's collarL is the
             ;; same shape at 16.2.
             ;; It is derived from the level's own `iters` rather than bumped, so it belongs to the
             ;; PRECISION SCALE the owner specified — the top level pays for the accuracy and the
             ;; lower ones are bit-identical to before (iters 2 -> 6 sweeps, 6 -> 6, 16 -> 12) —
             ;; and it stays tunable from the data file with no build, like everything else here.
             (cits (max 6 (min 12 (- iters 4))))
             ;; cycle 2: `collide` is a TIER now, not a bool — 0 = no collisions, 1 = core volumes
             ;; only, 2 = the full body set. The lowest level still collides (owner 17:35: a level
             ;; may thin the collider set, never let a chain visibly pass through the body).
             (tier (/ (pc-physics-level-param-mi level 2) 1000))
             (classmask (/ (pc-physics-level-param-mi level 3) 1000))
             (fixedhz (* 0.001 (the float (pc-physics-level-param-mi level 4))))
             (dt (seconds-per-frame))
             ;; temps hoisted out of all loops (GOAL stack allocs accumulate per call frame)
             (vtmp (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (vtmp2 (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (vtmp3 (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (cpt (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (axis (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (dirv (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (dirt (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (dirs (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             ;; (AH) anchor coupling: this chain's excitation acceleration for the frame
             (cacc (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             ;; (R) gravity instrument: the acceleration before the gravity term, and the term itself
             (gpre (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (gvec (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             ;; (R) hang: the world DOWN axis and the rebuilt rest direction of one link
             (down (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (hdir (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             ;; (Z/V) extent probe: the point that stands in for the skinned continuation below the
             ;; last bone of a chain. See the collision block.
             (pprb (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             ;; (C13b) the MODEL-pose twin of pprb, and the strand pass's two.
             (mprb (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (mprd (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (xdir (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (xcand (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
             (q (new 'stack-no-clear 'quaternion))
             (rotm (new 'stack-no-clear 'matrix))
             (tmpm (new 'stack-no-clear 'matrix))
             (hbind (new 'stack-no-clear 'matrix))
             (lkm (new 'stack-no-clear 'matrix))
             ;; per-link freedom ladder, recomputed per chain per frame (<= PHYS-JPS entries)
             (lo2 (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'float 48))
             (lcos (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'float 48))
             (lsin (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'float 48))
             ;; (O) did THIS link get pushed out this frame? A velocity reversal only means
             ;; "jitter" when the link is in CONTACT — a free-hanging chain reverses twice per
             ;; oscillation because that is what a spring does, and counting those would grade the
             ;; feature as a defect. Measured: the all-reversals version read 360 per window on a
             ;; perfectly healthy Keira.
             (lpush (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 48))
             ;; (C13b) "a collider is HOLDING this link" — which is not the same question as "a
             ;; collider PUSHED this link this frame", and the difference is the whole of the last
             ;; red gate. The restdevA sample has always been documented as grading "links no
             ;; collider was holding"; it was implemented as `lpush`, which is only set on the
             ;; frames a push actually fires. A link resting AT a volume's surface needs no push,
             ;; so it was sampled, and its distance from the model pose was read as the chain
             ;; failing to return when in fact the body is in the way and rule W cannot apply.
             ;; Proven on the phone rather than argued: jak-hd `earL` carried the entire figure,
             ;; and reducing its tip radius from 196 to 188 as DATA — no build — moved restdevA
             ;; from 8.2208 to 10.5743. A number that tracks a collision radius is a number about
             ;; a contact. Kept separate from `lpush` on purpose: `lpush` also arms the idle bias,
             ;; the friction term and the jitter counter, and none of those should change.
             (lhold (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 48))
             ;; per-rig-joint "this bone moved this frame" flag, for the descendant pass (k < PHYS-MAXJ)
             (moved (new 'stack-no-clear 'array 'int32 128))
             (frame-maxvel 0.0)
             ;; (S) this frame's anchor travel, MAXIMISED OVER EVERY CHAIN — the "is there any input
             ;; at all?" signal the idle-drift and settle-time instruments are keyed on. anchmove is a
             ;; window MAXIMUM and cannot answer a per-frame question.
             ;; It has to be the max over ALL anchors, not chain 0's: on a walking NPC the head can
             ;; sit still for a frame while the hips travel, and keying "no input" on one bone scored
             ;; a walking villager's cape at 2713 units of "drift" — a false positive, not a defect.
             ;; Requiring EVERY anchor to be still is the stricter reading of the owner's rule
             ;; ("acteur immobile, animation sans delta"), and it is the one measured below.
             (frame-anchd 0.0)
             ;; (S) the largest VISIBLE self-motion any chain produced this frame (influence-scaled,
             ;; so it is the motion that reaches a bone), excluding chains that are settling in from a
             ;; spawn or currently owned by the authored animation.
             (frame-self 0.0)
             ;; (S) the largest TARGET travel any link was asked for this frame. Together with
             ;; frame-anchd this is the whole "does the animation want anything?" test — see the
             ;; comment on *phys-tprev*: keying it on the anchor alone scored driven motion as drift.
             (frame-tmove 0.0)
             (frame-maxdev 0.0)
             (frame-nact 0)
             (frame-nreglue 0)
             (frame-ndesc 0)
             (frame-nopose 0)
             ;; (W) cycle 5 — GRAVITY'S AUTHORITY OVER A FAMILY A REST POSE, this frame. 0 while the
             ;; actor is upright (the model pose is the equilibrium, full stop), 1 once he is on his
             ;; head. Computed once per actor, not per chain: it is a property of the character.
             (tiltf 0.0)
             ;; (R) the gravity instrument used to be pinned to chain 0. Family A gates its gravity
             ;; term to zero on an upright actor, so pinning it there would make the world-space
             ;; proof read (0,0,0) and vanish exactly when it matters. It now latches onto the first
             ;; chain this frame that actually APPLIES a gravity term — still the measured term, not
             ;; a restated constant.
             (gcap 0)
             (frame-fama 0)
             (frame-famb 0)
             (frame-unclass 0))
        (when (and (> dt 0.0001) (< dt 0.1))
          ;; (C14-D) fresh frame, fresh resolution-jerk ledger: lresv accumulates every correction
          ;; VECTOR the resolution applies to a link THIS frame, across all passes; the fold below
          ;; takes the length of the NET and the window keeps the worst single-frame figure.
          (dotimes (k PHYS-JPS)
            (vector-zero! (-> *phys-lresv* (+ jbase k))))
          ;; ---------------- (W) HOW FAR FROM UPRIGHT IS THIS CHARACTER? ---------------------------
          ;; Joint 0 is `align`, the actor's own transform, and bone index = joint + 1. Row 1 of that
          ;; matrix is his up axis; `phys-axis-dot` normalises it first, so a rig carrying scale does
          ;; not read as a tilt. Owner: "si tu pends Maia par les pieds, forcement ses seins ne
          ;; seront pas a la meme position que debout" — this is that exception, and nothing else
          ;; reopens gravity's claim on a body chain's rest pose.
          (set! (-> down x) 0.0)
          (set! (-> down y) -1.0)
          (set! (-> down z) 0.0)
          (set! (-> down w) 0.0)
          ;; WHAT THIS MEASURES, EXACTLY, so the next cycle does not have to guess: the ACTOR's own
          ;; root orientation. It catches the owner's case ("si tu pends Maia par les pieds"), being
          ;; knocked over, and any pose where the character himself is turned. It does NOT catch an
          ;; ANIMATION that lays a character down while his root stays upright — the intro cinematic
          ;; — and that is deliberate: there the modelled silhouette is the animator's intent, and
          ;; the phase's own rule (owner cycle-3 A) is that authored animation wins. Measuring the
          ;; ANCHOR bone instead would catch it, but only on rigs whose local row 1 really is "up",
          ;; and across 458 shipped rigs it is not — an ear bone pointing sideways would read as a
          ;; 90-degree tilt on a character standing perfectly straight and droop for no reason.
          (when (> nbones 1)
            (let* ((rm (the-as matrix (-> skel bones 1 transform)))
                   (rl2 (vector-length (-> rm vector 1))))
              ;; DEGENERATE ROW = UN-POSED FRAME (every bone at the origin: the parked title-screen
              ;; spawn, the frame a warp cuts the pose). phys-axis-dot returns 0.0 there, and 0.0
              ;; through the ramp below reads as a 75-degree tilt — which would hand gravity the
              ;; rest pose back and silently restore the exact cycle-4 behaviour this cycle removes,
              ;; by an accident of measurement rather than by anything the owner asked for. An
              ;; un-posed frame is not a tilted actor.
              (when (> rl2 0.000001)
                (let ((upd (- (phys-axis-dot rm 1 down))))
                  (set! tiltf (fmax 0.0 (fmin 1.0 (/ (- PHYS-COS-UP upd)
                                                     (- PHYS-COS-UP PHYS-COS-TILT)))))))))
          (when (> tiltf (-> *phys-slot-tilt* slot))
            (set! (-> *phys-slot-tilt* slot) tiltf))
          ;; fixed-timestep ladder top: substep count from the accumulator target rate
          (when (> fixedhz 1.0)
            (set! substeps (max 1 (min 8 (the int (+ 0.5 (* dt fixedhz)))))))
          (let ((sdt (/ dt (the float substeps))))
            ;; ============================================================================
            ;; CYCLE 16 — THE REWRITE (SPEC 17). FOUR STEPS, ONE MEASURED QUANTITY.
            ;;
            ;; WHAT THIS REPLACED. 3900 lines in which fourteen corrective passes each
            ;; compensated for the previous one's defect: a ring-down, an arrival toward the
            ;; model pose, a sustained-contact model bias, an idle hold applied to the bone,
            ;; a sleep rule, stick damping folded into the velocity retention, an inelastic
            ;; contact discharge, a per-frame slew bound, an excursion ceiling, a model-pose
            ;; ladder, an unbounded last-resort escape, an opposite-side re-resolve, a length
            ;; last word and a "fallback that cannot fail". Nineteen silent defects were found
            ;; INSIDE that stack in six days, and every owner verdict said the same sentence:
            ;; the chains do not move. Nine of those fourteen passes exist only to REMOVE
            ;; motion. No amount of tuning turns a subtractive pass into a productive one, so
            ;; the stack is gone rather than adjusted.
            ;;
            ;; THE ORDER BELOW IS THE WHOLE DESIGN:
            ;;   STEP 1  INTEGRATE   spring toward the pose the FAMILY says is the rest pose,
            ;;                       plus gravity on the dynamics and the anchor's own
            ;;                       acceleration as a frame pseudo-force.
            ;;   STEP 2  CONSTRAIN   segment length INVARIANT, swing inside the cone.
            ;;   STEP 3  COLLIDE     body volumes, then strand-vs-strand. Collision has the
            ;;                       LAST WORD, and it resolves by ONE mechanism: a bisection
            ;;                       on the chain pose between the authored pose (t=0) and the
            ;;                       simulated pose (t=1). t=0 is penetration-free BY
            ;;                       CONSTRUCTION (phys-link-mesh-worst returns exactly 0.0
            ;;                       there, and every volume is capped at this link's own model
            ;;                       pose), so a feasible answer always exists and the search
            ;;                       cannot fail. That single property is what let the eleven
            ;;                       fallback passes go: they existed because the old
            ;;                       per-sample push loop could oscillate between two volumes
            ;;                       and had no guaranteed answer to fall back to.
            ;;   STEP 4  WRITE       the bone: swing the 3x3 by the same rotation that moved
            ;;                       the position, translation row = the resolved position.
            ;; and then STEP 5 measures, from the WRITTEN bone and from nothing else.
            ;;
            ;; MOTION SUPPRESSORS. Exactly ONE survives — authored priority (SPEC 5: the
            ;; animator wins while he is deliberately holding a chain; the owner's named case
            ;; is Keira holding her goggles to her eyes at the Zoomer) — and it is armed on
            ;; the authored OFFSET, never on the authored channel's SPEED, because "held
            ;; still" is not "no longer held". Its share of frames is measured and printed.
            ;; Everything else is ABSENT, not disabled: no sleep, no rest state, no ring-down,
            ;; no arrival, no calm freeze, no jerk clamp, no excursion ceiling, no velocity
            ;; discharge, no stick damping, no friction. Their counters are emitted and read
            ;; 0 — and here 0 means the mechanism DOES NOT EXIST. One suppressor may come back
            ;; per cycle, only for a defect measured on the phone, and only with its own
            ;; percentage-of-frames next to it.
            ;;
            ;; ONE MEASURED QUANTITY. Everything in STEP 5 is a function of the position this
            ;; solver WROTE to the joint, frame by frame, differenced in the authored frame:
            ;;     dev(t)    = written(t) - authored(t)
            ;;     motion    = |dev(t) - dev(t-1)|         (a constant offset scores ~0)
            ;;     inertness = that motion staying ~0 while the chain's own anchor is driven
            ;;     jerk      = the worst single-frame |dev(t) - dev(t-1)|
            ;;     penetration = the SKINNED MESH surface inside a body volume
            ;; The retired floor measured |written - rest| instead, i.e. the MAGNITUDE of the
            ;; offset, which a chain welded 352 units off its rest pose maximises while
            ;; visually static — that is how chestrun read 352.4841 unchanged for three days
            ;; and why the owner's "les meches sont ANCREES" and my "green" were both true.
            ;; ============================================================================

            ;; ---- STEP 0a: the authored channel is neutralised on physics-owned joints ---
            ;; jak1 hand-keys pseudo-wind on straps, hair and cloth. Two writers on one bone
            ;; is the cycle-2 defect, so the authored world position is stashed (the authored
            ;; priority test and the collision floor both need it) and the joint is re-glued
            ;; to its BIND-POSE local carried by its animated parent. From here the target is
            ;; a calm rest pose rigidly attached to the anchor, and the sim owns the joint.
            (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
              (let* ((ci (+ cbase c))
                     (len (-> *phys-clen* ci))
                     (start (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci))))
                (when (and (> len 0) (> (-> *phys-canim* ci) 0)
                           (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* ci) classmask)))
                  (+! frame-nreglue 1)
                  (dotimes (i len)
                    (let ((k (-> *phys-jk* (+ start i))))
                      (when (< (+ k 1) nbones)
                        (vector-copy! (-> *phys-anim* (+ start i))
                                      (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform vector 3))
                        (let ((p (the int (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase k)))))
                          (when (and (!= p #xff) (< (+ p 1) nbones))
                            (matrix-4x4-inverse! hbind (-> hd-jgeo data k bind-pose))
                            (matrix*! lkm hbind (-> hd-jgeo data p bind-pose))
                            (matrix*! (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform) lkm
                                      (the-as matrix (-> skel bones (+ p 1) transform)))))))))))
            ;; ---- STEP 0b: cache the authored pose (the write-back overwrites bones) -----
            (dotimes (j (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot))
              (let ((k (-> *phys-jk* (+ jbase j))))
                (when (< (+ k 1) nbones)
                  (vector-copy! (-> *phys-targ* (+ jbase j))
                                (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform vector 3))
                  (vector-copy! (-> *phys-rest* (+ jbase j))
                                (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform vector 3)))))
            (when (> (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot) 0)
              (let* ((a0 (-> *phys-canchor* cbase))
                     (ap (-> skel bones (+ a0 1) transform vector 3)))
                (when (nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-seeded* slot))
                  (vector-! vtmp ap (-> *phys-slot-anchprev* slot))
                  (let ((am (vector-length vtmp)))
                    (when (> am (-> *phys-slot-anchmove* slot))
                      (set! (-> *phys-slot-anchmove* slot) am))))
                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-slot-anchprev* slot) ap)))
            ;; first frame after a bind: start AT the authored pose, at rest (owner rule B).
            (when (zero? (-> *phys-slot-seeded* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-seeded* slot) 1)
              (dotimes (j (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot))
                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-pos* (+ jbase j)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ jbase j)))
                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-prev* (+ jbase j)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ jbase j)))
                (vector-copy! (-> *phys-out* (+ jbase j)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ jbase j)))))

            ;; ============================ PER CHAIN =====================================
            (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
              (let* ((ci (+ cbase c))
                     (len (-> *phys-clen* ci))
                     (start (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci)))
                     (active (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* ci) classmask))))
                (when (> len 0)
                  (cond
                    ((not active)
                     ;; this class is off at this precision level: ride the bone rigidly.
                     (dotimes (i len)
                       (vector-copy! (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                       (vector-copy! (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                       (vector-copy! (-> *phys-out* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))))
                    (else
                     (+! frame-nact 1)
                     (+! (-> *phys-slot-simcf* slot) 1)
                     ;; census of what is really SIMULATING, by family — not what the file
                     ;; declares. An unclassified chain is counted loudly and separately.
                     (case (-> *phys-cfam* ci)
                       ((1) (+! frame-fama 1))
                       ((2) (+! frame-famb 1))
                       (else (+! frame-fama 1) (+! frame-unclass 1)))
                     (let* ((anchor-k (-> *phys-canchor* ci))
                            (anchor (-> skel bones (+ anchor-k 1) transform vector 3))
                            ;; MASS reaches the integrator here and nowhere else:
                            ;; omega_eff = omega / sqrt(mass), i.e. a = F/m with F = k*x.
                            ;; A heavier chain therefore has a LOWER natural frequency, so it
                            ;; starts late and carries through, and its amplitude for a given
                            ;; anchor acceleration is LARGER (a/omega^2). That is the owner's
                            ;; "on ne sent pas la masse" answered as physics rather than as
                            ;; damping — the cycle-7 error was reading heavy as damped.
                            (omega (/ (-> *phys-comega* ci) (sqrtf (-> *phys-cmass* ci))))
                            (rl (max 0 (min (+ len -1) (-> *phys-crootlock* ci))))
                            (nfree (- len rl))
                            (grad (fmax 0.0 (fmin 1.0 (-> *phys-cgrad* ci))))
                            (rf (fmax 0.0 (fmin 1.0 (-> *phys-crootfree* ci))))
                            (exc (if (= 2 (-> *phys-canim* ci)) (-> *phys-cexcite* ci) 0.0))
                            (authw 0.0)
                            (aratio 0.0)
                            (sw 1.0)
                            (chpush 0)
                            (chresid 0)
                            ;; POSE GUARD: a companion can be handed a frame with every bone
                            ;; at the origin (the parked title-screen spawn, the frame a warp
                            ;; cuts the pose). A chain with no length has no physics to audit.
                            (chainlen (let ((s 0.0))
                                        (dotimes (i len)
                                          (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))
                                                    (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i -1))))
                                          (set! s (+ s (vector-length vtmp))))
                                        s))
                            ;; INT, never a boolean: in GOAL a plain 0 is TRUTHY.
                            (collide? (if (and (> tier 0) (>= chainlen 1.0)) 1 0))
                            ;; BOUNDED PROJECTION (owner rule O): a correction is a positional
                            ;; jump and a verlet integrator reads a positional jump as velocity,
                            ;; so one frame may only walk a link a fraction of its own length.
                            (maxcorr (fmax 8.0 (* PHYS-MAXCORR-REL chainlen))))
                       (set! (-> *phys-cchlen* ci) chainlen)
                       (when (< chainlen 1.0)
                         (+! frame-nopose 1))

                       ;; ---- the ONE continuous freedom profile, root -> tip ---------------
                       ;; It governs the sim (per-link spring rate and cone half-angle) AND it
                       ;; is the profile the report prints, so the number that is graded is the
                       ;; number that acts. The previous build had TWO gradients — this ladder
                       ;; and a second per-link blend applied to the OUTPUT — which is both the
                       ;; owner's "seuls les bouts bougent" (the output blend pulled every link
                       ;; but the tip back toward the authored pose) and his "CRAN bizarre" on
                       ;; Daxter's two-bone ears (the two profiles disagreed across the lock
                       ;; boundary). One profile, no step larger than PHYS-INFL-STEP.
                       (let* ((wtip 1.0)
                              (wroot0 (if (> rl 0) (* 0.5 rf) rf))
                              (wroot (if (> len 1)
                                         (fmin wtip (fmax wroot0
                                                          (- wtip (* PHYS-INFL-STEP
                                                                     (the float (+ len -1))))))
                                         wtip)))
                         (dotimes (i len)
                           (let ((f (if (< len 2)
                                        wtip
                                        (+ wroot (* (- wtip wroot)
                                                    (/ (the float i) (the float (+ len -1))))))))
                             ;; gradient=0 means uniform: every link keeps the authored amplitude
                             (when (< grad 1.0)
                               (set! f (+ f (* (- 1.0 grad) (- wtip f)))))
                             (set! (-> *phys-infl* (+ start i)) f))))

                       ;; ---- (R) WHICH WAY IS DOWN, AND WHO GETS TO SAY SO -----------------
                       ;; family B — the things that genuinely hang — rebuild their REST pose
                       ;; from world down, link by link, every rest LENGTH preserved exactly.
                       ;; "Ca pend, ca pend." family A — the body — never does: their rest pose
                       ;; is the pose Naughty Dog modelled, "pas plus haut, pas plus bas", and
                       ;; gravity only reaches their DYNAMICS. The owner's exception is tiltf:
                       ;; tip the character over and gravity takes the rest pose back.
                       ;; (Cycle 16 also removed hang= from all 157 family A chains in the DATA,
                       ;; so this is belt and braces rather than the only guard.)
                       (let ((hgf (if (= 2 (-> *phys-cfam* ci)) 1.0 tiltf)))
                         (when (and (> (* hgf (-> *phys-chang* ci)) 0.0) (>= chainlen 1.0))
                           (let ((hg (* hgf (-> *phys-chang* ci))))
                             (dotimes (i len)
                               ;; read the authored link vector from the PRISTINE rest copy:
                               ;; *phys-targ* is what is being rewritten.
                               (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-rest* (+ start i))
                                         (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-rest* (+ start i -1))))
                               (let ((ll (vector-length vtmp)))
                                 (when (> ll 0.0001)
                                   (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp (/ 1.0 ll))
                                   (vector-float*! hdir vtmp (- 1.0 hg))
                                   (vector-float*! vtmp2 down hg)
                                   (vector+! hdir hdir vtmp2)
                                   (let ((hl (vector-length hdir)))
                                     (cond
                                       ((< hl 0.0001) (vector-copy! hdir vtmp))
                                       (else (vector-float*! hdir hdir (/ 1.0 hl))))
                                     (vector-float*! hdir hdir ll)
                                     (vector+! (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))
                                               (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i -1)))
                                               hdir))))))))

                       ;; ---- (C13) THE REACH PERIMETER, REBUILT FROM GEOMETRY EVERY FRAME --
                       ;; Owner cycle 12: a chain tests every volume it can physically REACH;
                       ;; a filter may only exclude what is PROVABLY unreachable. So the proof
                       ;; is recomputed rather than authored: a bounding sphere around what the
                       ;; chain occupies (anchor to furthest link in either the model or the
                       ;; simulated pose, plus that link's mesh-measured half-thickness), and a
                       ;; volume is in unless its surface is beyond that sphere plus a margin.
                       ;; No data key, no family and no chains= list can remove one.
                       ;; The single exclusion is structural and not an opt-out: a volume whose
                       ;; BOTH ends sit on joints of this very chain is the strand's own capsule.
                       ;; "Either end" was the cycle-14 defect — it dropped 532 body volumes.
                       (when (nonzero? collide?)
                         (let ((brad 0.0))
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (let ((lr (-> *phys-lrad* (+ start i))))
                               (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)) anchor)
                               (let ((d (+ lr (vector-length vtmp))))
                                 (when (> d brad) (set! brad d)))
                               (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-out* (+ start i)) anchor)
                               (let ((d (+ lr (vector-length vtmp))))
                                 (when (> d brad) (set! brad d)))))
                           (vector-copy! (-> *phys-cbsp* ci) anchor)
                           (set! (-> *phys-cbsr* ci) brad)
                           (let ((n 0)
                                 (lb (+ (* slot PHYS-CPS PHYS-CCMAX) (* c PHYS-CCMAX)))
                                 (reach (+ brad PHYS-REACH-MARGIN)))
                             (dotimes (s2 (-> *phys-slot-ncols* slot))
                               (let* ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS) s2))
                                      (rc (-> *phys-colchain* cb))
                                      (k2 (-> *phys-colk2* cb)))
                                 (when (and (<= (-> *phys-coltier* cb) tier) (!= rc c))
                                   (let ((self? 0)
                                         (owna 0)
                                         (ownb 0)
                                         (ck (-> *phys-colk* cb)))
                                     (dotimes (i2 len)
                                       (let ((jk (-> *phys-jk* (+ start i2))))
                                         (when (= jk ck) (set! owna 1))
                                         (when (and (>= k2 0) (= jk k2)) (set! ownb 1))))
                                     (when (and (< rc 0)
                                                (nonzero? owna)
                                                (or (< k2 0) (nonzero? ownb)))
                                       (set! self? 1))
                                     (when (zero? self?)
                                       (let* ((ca (if (>= rc 0)
                                                      (-> *phys-out* (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* (+ cbase rc))
                                                                        (+ (-> *phys-clen* (+ cbase rc)) -1)))
                                                      (-> skel bones (+ (-> *phys-colk* cb) 1) transform vector 3)))
                                              (cbv (if (and (< rc 0) (>= k2 0))
                                                       (-> skel bones (+ k2 1) transform vector 3)
                                                       ca)))
                                         (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt ca cbv anchor)
                                         (vector-! vtmp cpt anchor)
                                         (when (<= (- (vector-length vtmp)
                                                      (fmax (-> *phys-colr* cb) (-> *phys-colr2* cb)))
                                                   reach)
                                           (cond
                                             ((< n PHYS-CCMAX)
                                              (set! (-> *phys-cclist* (+ lb n)) s2)
                                              (+! n 1))
                                             ;; a truncated perimeter is a hole, and a hole is
                                             ;; the whole defect: counted and printed, never
                                             ;; absorbed.
                                             (else (+! (-> *phys-cctrunc* slot) 1))))))))))
                             (set! (-> *phys-ccn* ci) n)
                             (+! (-> *phys-slot-ccnsum* slot) n)
                             (when (> n (-> *phys-cncol* ci))
                               (set! (-> *phys-cncol* ci) n))
                             (when (zero? n) (+! (-> *phys-slot-nomask* slot) 1)))))
                       (when (zero? collide?)
                         (+! (-> *phys-slot-noncol* slot) 1)
                         (set! (-> *phys-cbsr* ci) 0.0))

                       ;; ---- (W/C6b) EVERY VOLUME IS CAPPED AT THIS LINK'S OWN MODEL POSE --
                       ;; The cap is what makes the authored pose FEASIBLE, and the feasibility
                       ;; of the authored pose is what makes STEP 3's bisection unable to fail.
                       ;; It removes exactly the region the character's own sculpted or keyed
                       ;; pose already occupies, per (link, volume), and nothing else: a strand
                       ;; may reach where ND put it and not one unit deeper.
                       (when (nonzero? collide?)
                         (dotimes (i len)
                           (dotimes (s2 (-> *phys-ccn* ci))
                             (let* ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS)
                                           (-> *phys-cclist* (+ (* slot PHYS-CPS PHYS-CCMAX)
                                                                (* c PHYS-CCMAX) s2))))
                                    (rc (-> *phys-colchain* cb))
                                    (k2 (-> *phys-colk2* cb))
                                    (mca (if (>= rc 0)
                                             (-> *phys-targ* (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* (+ cbase rc))
                                                               (+ (-> *phys-clen* (+ cbase rc)) -1)))
                                             (-> skel bones (+ (-> *phys-colk* cb) 1) transform vector 3)))
                                    (mcb (if (and (< rc 0) (>= k2 0))
                                             (-> skel bones (+ k2 1) transform vector 3)
                                             mca)))
                               ;; measured AT THE POINT THE TEST USES: a chain with extent=
                               ;; tests a probe half the extent beyond its last link.
                               (vector-copy! mprb (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                               (when (and (> (-> *phys-cext* ci) 0.0) (= i (+ len -1)))
                                 (vector-! mprd mprb
                                           (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i -1))))
                                 (let ((pl (vector-length mprd)))
                                   (when (> pl 0.0001)
                                     (vector-float*! mprd mprd (/ (* 0.5 (-> *phys-cext* ci)) pl))
                                     (vector+! mprb mprb mprd))))
                               (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt mca mcb mprb)
                               (vector-! vtmp mprb cpt)
                               (let ((mdist (vector-length vtmp)))
                                 ;; the AUTHORED pose is as legitimate a floor as the modelled
                                 ;; one — Keira pulling her goggles over her eyes puts them
                                 ;; inside the head volume ON PURPOSE.
                                 (when (> (-> *phys-cauththr* ci) 0.0)
                                   (vector-copy! mprb (-> *phys-anim* (+ start i)))
                                   (when (and (> (-> *phys-cext* ci) 0.0) (= i (+ len -1)))
                                     (vector-! mprd mprb
                                               (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-anim* (+ start i -1))))
                                     (let ((pl (vector-length mprd)))
                                       (when (> pl 0.0001)
                                         (vector-float*! mprd mprd (/ (* 0.5 (-> *phys-cext* ci)) pl))
                                         (vector+! mprb mprb mprd))))
                                   (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt mca mcb mprb)
                                   (vector-! vtmp mprb cpt)
                                   (set! mdist (fmin mdist (vector-length vtmp))))
                                 (set! (-> *phys-ccap* (+ (* i PHYS-CCMAX) s2))
                                       (fmax 0.0 (- mdist PHYS-MODEL-CLR))))))))

                       ;; ---- (B) SPAWN, TELEPORT AND BIG TRANSITIONS ----------------------
                       ;; No animation moves a bone a metre in one frame, so past that bar the
                       ;; pose was CUT: forget the state entirely (no inherited velocity) and
                       ;; ramp physics back in over PHYS-SETTLE frames. This is initialisation,
                       ;; not a suppressor — its share of frames is printed all the same.
                       (vector-! vtmp anchor (-> *phys-canchprev* ci))
                       (let ((anchd (vector-length vtmp))
                             (aacc 0.0))
                         (vector-copy! (-> *phys-canchprev* ci) anchor)
                         (vector-! vtmp2 vtmp (-> *phys-canchvp* ci))
                         (set! aacc (vector-length vtmp2))
                         (vector-copy! (-> *phys-canchvp* ci) vtmp)
                         (set! (-> *phys-canchd* ci) anchd)
                         (when (> anchd frame-anchd) (set! frame-anchd anchd))
                         (when (> anchd (fmax PHYS-JUMP-ABS (* PHYS-JUMP-REL chainlen)))
                           (+! (-> *phys-slot-reseed* slot) 1)
                           (set! (-> *phys-csettle* ci) PHYS-SETTLE)
                           (vector-reset! (-> *phys-canchvp* ci))
                           (set! (-> *phys-canchok* ci) 0)
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (vector-copy! (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                             (vector-copy! (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))))
                         (when (and (<= (-> *phys-csettle* ci) 0)
                                    (> aacc (-> *phys-canchmv* ci)))
                           (set! (-> *phys-canchmv* ci) aacc)))
                       (when (> (-> *phys-csettle* ci) 0)
                         (set! sw (/ (the float (- PHYS-SETTLE (-> *phys-csettle* ci)))
                                     (the float PHYS-SETTLE))))

                       ;; ---- (A/AF/AJ) THE ONE SURVIVING SUPPRESSOR: AUTHORED PRIORITY ----
                       ;; Only for chains that DECLARE authored= (13 of 345), and computed
                       ;; STRICTLY on this chain's own joints — an unrelated bone moving must
                       ;; never suspend a chain, which is the owner's "la physique semble
                       ;; desactivee pendant les animations".
                       ;; ARMED ON THE OFFSET, NOT ON THE SPEED. The detector asks "is the
                       ;; animator holding this chain away from its rest pose?", so a hand that
                       ;; goes still while still holding the goggles keeps authority: "TENU
                       ;; IMMOBILE n'est pas PLUS TENU". Release is the same test failing, and
                       ;; it fades out over authfall so physics resumes as a ramp, never a snap.
                       (when (and (> (-> *phys-cauththr* ci) 0.0) (>= chainlen 1.0))
                         (let ((off 0.0))
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-anim* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                             (let ((d (vector-length vtmp)))
                               (when (> d off) (set! off d))))
                           (set! aratio (/ off chainlen))
                           (let* ((w0 (-> *phys-cauth* ci))
                                  (want (if (> aratio (* PHYS-AUTH-BASE (-> *phys-cauththr* ci))) 1.0 0.0))
                                  (rate (if (> want w0)
                                            (* dt (-> *phys-cauthrise* ci))
                                            (* dt (-> *phys-cauthfall* ci))))
                                  (w (cond
                                       ((> want w0) (fmin want (+ w0 rate)))
                                       (else (fmax want (- w0 rate))))))
                             (when (and (> w 0.5) (<= w0 0.5))
                               (+! (-> *phys-slot-autheng* slot) 1))
                             (when (and (<= w 0.5) (> w0 0.5))
                               (+! (-> *phys-slot-authrel* slot) 1))
                             (cond
                               ((> w 0.5)
                                (+! (-> *phys-slot-authhold* slot) 1)
                                (+! (-> *phys-chold* ci) 1)
                                (when (> (-> *phys-chold* ci) (-> *phys-slot-holdmax* slot))
                                  (set! (-> *phys-slot-holdmax* slot) (-> *phys-chold* ci))))
                               (else
                                (set! (-> *phys-chold* ci) 0)))
                             (set! (-> *phys-cauth* ci) w)
                             (set! authw w)
                             (when (> w (-> *phys-slot-authmax* slot))
                               (set! (-> *phys-slot-authmax* slot) w))
                             (when (> aratio (-> *phys-cauthmax* ci))
                               (set! (-> *phys-cauthmax* ci) aratio)))))
                       ;; the animator's pose becomes the spring's target, weighted, and the
                       ;; spring tracks it harder — one writer, still the sim.
                       (when (> authw 0.0)
                         (dotimes (i len)
                           (when (>= i rl)
                             (let ((tg (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))))
                               (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-anim* (+ start i)) tg)
                               (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp authw)
                               (vector+! tg tg vtmp))))
                         (set! omega (* omega (+ 1.0 (* authw (- (-> *phys-cauthstiff* ci) 1.0)))))
                         (set! exc (* exc (- 1.0 authw))))
                       (set! exc (* exc sw))
                       ;; root-locked links ARE the bone: no integration, no cone, no write.
                       (dotimes (i rl)
                         (vector-copy! (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                         (vector-copy! (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))))
                       ;; per-link spring rate and cone, from the single freedom profile
                       (dotimes (i len)
                         (let* ((f (fmax 0.2 (-> *phys-infl* (+ start i))))
                                (wi (/ omega f)))
                           (when (> (* wi sdt) 1.0) (set! wi (/ 1.0 sdt)))
                           (set! (-> lo2 i) (* wi wi))
                           (let ((ang (* (-> *phys-cmaxrad* ci) f)))
                             (set! (-> lcos i) (cos-rad ang))
                             (set! (-> lsin i) (sin-rad ang))))
                         (set! (-> lpush i) 0))

                       ;; ---- (AH) THE ANCHOR'S OWN ACCELERATION, AS A FRAME PSEUDO-FORCE ---
                       ;; This is the owner's "ca bouge bien". Firmness comes from stiffness and
                       ;; a stretch of ~0; AMPLITUDE comes from here and from mass. Without it
                       ;; the only excitation is the lag a damped spring develops behind its own
                       ;; moving target, which is a/omega^2 — so every notch of firmness was
                       ;; paid for out of the travel and "plus de jiggle ET plus de fermete" was
                       ;; arithmetically impossible.
                       (vector-reset! cacc)
                       (let ((cpl (-> *phys-ccouple* ci)))
                         (when (> cpl 0.0)
                           (cond
                             ((or (zero? (-> *phys-canchok* ci))
                                  (> (-> *phys-csettle* ci) 0)
                                  (< chainlen 1.0)
                                  (< dt 0.0001))
                              ;; no usable history: SEED and add nothing. The second difference
                              ;; of a teleport is the spawn burst the owner reported at cycle 3.
                              (vector-reset! (-> *phys-canchv* ci))
                              (vector-copy! (-> *phys-canchp* ci) anchor)
                              (set! (-> *phys-canchok* ci) 1))
                             (else
                              (vector-! vtmp anchor (-> *phys-canchp* ci))
                              (vector-! cacc vtmp (-> *phys-canchv* ci))
                              (vector-copy! (-> *phys-canchv* ci) vtmp)
                              (vector-copy! (-> *phys-canchp* ci) anchor)
                              ;; an animation POP is not an acceleration
                              (let ((al (vector-length cacc))
                                    (amax (* PHYS-COUPLE-MAX chainlen)))
                                (when (> al amax)
                                  (vector-float*! cacc cacc (/ amax al))))
                              (vector-float*! cacc cacc
                                              (/ (* (- 0.0 cpl) sw (- 1.0 authw)) (* dt dt)))))))

                       ;; ================= STEP 1 + STEP 2 : INTEGRATE, THEN CONSTRAIN ======
                       (let ((kd (fmin 1.0 (/ (-> *phys-cinertia* ci)
                                              (+ 1.0 (* (-> *phys-cdamp* ci) sdt 60.0)))))
                             ;; gravity on the DYNAMICS. Family B always; family A only once the
                             ;; character is no longer upright (the owner's own exception).
                             (gacc (* (-> *phys-cgrav* ci) PHYS-GRAV-ACCEL (- 1.0 authw) sw
                                      (if (= 2 (-> *phys-cfam* ci)) 1.0 tiltf))))
                         (dotimes (st substeps)
                           ;; ---- STEP 1: verlet integrate every FREE link ----
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (when (>= i rl)
                               (let ((p (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)))
                                     (pv (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)))
                                     (tg (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))))
                                 ;; acc = omega^2*(target - p) - g + excite + anchor pseudo-force
                                 (vector-! vtmp tg p)
                                 (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp (-> lo2 i))
                                 ;; (R) the gravity direction the integrator ACTUALLY applied,
                                 ;; read out of the integrator as the difference of the
                                 ;; acceleration immediately before and after the term. In WORLD
                                 ;; space it must stay (0,-1,0) however the actor is turned;
                                 ;; gloc is the same vector in the anchor bone's own axes and
                                 ;; must SWING. The pair is the proof, not either alone.
                                 (when (and (zero? gcap) (> gacc 0.0) (= i rl))
                                   (vector-copy! gpre vtmp))
                                 (set! (-> vtmp y) (- (-> vtmp y) gacc))
                                 (when (and (zero? gcap) (> gacc 0.0) (= i rl))
                                   (set! gcap 1)
                                   (+! (-> *phys-slot-gsamp* slot) 1)
                                   (vector-! gvec vtmp gpre)
                                   (let ((gl (vector-length gvec)))
                                     (when (> gl 0.0001)
                                       (vector-float*! gvec gvec (/ 1.0 gl))
                                       (vector-copy! (-> *phys-slot-gdir* slot) gvec)
                                       (let ((abm (the-as matrix (-> skel bones (+ anchor-k 1) transform))))
                                         (set! (-> *phys-slot-gloc* slot x) (phys-axis-dot abm 0 gvec))
                                         (set! (-> *phys-slot-gloc* slot y) (phys-axis-dot abm 1 gvec))
                                         (set! (-> *phys-slot-gloc* slot z) (phys-axis-dot abm 2 gvec))))))
                                 (when (> exc 0.0)
                                   (vector-! vtmp3 (-> *phys-anim* (+ start i)) tg)
                                   (vector-float*! vtmp3 vtmp3 (* exc (-> lo2 i)))
                                   (vector+! vtmp vtmp vtmp3))
                                 (vector+! vtmp vtmp cacc)
                                 ;; vel = (p - prev)*kd ; p += vel + acc*sdt^2
                                 (vector-! vtmp2 p pv)
                                 (vector-float*! vtmp2 vtmp2 kd)
                                 (vector-copy! pv p)
                                 (vector+! p p vtmp2)
                                 (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp (* sdt sdt))
                                 (vector+! p p vtmp))))
                           ;; snapshot the state the constraint sweep is about to correct
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (when (>= i rl)
                               (vector-copy! (-> *phys-psave* i) (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)))))
                           ;; ---- STEP 2: invariant length + swing cone, then STEP 3a --------
                           (dotimes (it iters)
                             (dotimes (i len)
                               (when (>= i rl)
                                 (let* ((p (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)))
                                        (tg (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                                        (pp (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i -1))))
                                        (tp (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i -1)))))
                                   (vector-! axis tg tp)
                                   (let ((rest (vector-length axis)))
                                     (vector-! dirv p pp)
                                     (let ((dl (vector-length dirv)))
                                       (cond
                                         ((or (< dl 0.0001) (< rest 0.0001))
                                          (vector-copy! p tg))
                                         (else
                                          ;; LENGTH IS INVARIANT. stretch= is the only slack and
                                          ;; it is ~0 on every body part, so a single-bone chest
                                          ;; or belly moves as a RIGID volume swinging on its
                                          ;; anchor — never a translation that smears the skin it
                                          ;; shares with the torso into a point or flattens it.
                                          ;; Nothing may compress at all (owner X, Jak's collar).
                                          (let* ((str (-> *phys-cstretch* ci))
                                                 (lmax (* rest (+ 1.0 str)))
                                                 (dl2 (fmax rest (fmin lmax dl))))
                                            (vector-float*! dirv dirv (/ dl2 dl))
                                            (vector-float*! axis axis (/ 1.0 rest))
                                            (vector-float*! vtmp dirv (/ 1.0 dl2))
                                            (let ((dot (vector-dot vtmp axis))
                                                  (cmax (-> lcos i)))
                                              (when (< dot cmax)
                                                (vector-float*! vtmp2 axis dot)
                                                (vector-! vtmp2 vtmp vtmp2)
                                                (let ((pl (vector-length vtmp2)))
                                                  (cond
                                                    ((< pl 0.000001)
                                                     (vector-copy! vtmp axis))
                                                    (else
                                                     (vector-float*! vtmp2 vtmp2 (/ (-> lsin i) pl))
                                                     (vector-float*! vtmp axis cmax)
                                                     (vector+! vtmp vtmp vtmp2))))
                                                (vector-float*! dirv vtmp dl2)))
                                            (vector+! p pp dirv)
                                            ;; ---- STEP 3a: body volumes, at the point that is
                                            ;; DRAWN. A chain whose last bone carries a long
                                            ;; rigidly-skinned continuation (Jak's two jacket
                                            ;; pendants are one joint each with all the cloth
                                            ;; below them) tests a probe in the MIDDLE of that
                                            ;; continuation, so the sphere kept out of the leg is
                                            ;; the one the eye sees.
                                            (when (and (nonzero? collide?) (>= i rl))
                                              (let* ((exth (* 0.5 (-> *phys-cext* ci)))
                                                     (probe? (if (and (> exth 0.0) (= i (+ len -1)) (> dl2 0.0001)) 1 0))
                                                     (radx (if (nonzero? probe?) exth 0.0))
                                                     (pt (cond
                                                           ((nonzero? probe?)
                                                            (vector-float*! pprb dirv (/ exth dl2))
                                                            (vector+! pprb p pprb)
                                                            (+! (-> *phys-slot-extprobe* slot) 1)
                                                            pprb)
                                                           (else p))))
                                                (dotimes (s2 (-> *phys-ccn* ci))
                                                  (let* ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS)
                                                                (-> *phys-cclist* (+ (* slot PHYS-CPS PHYS-CCMAX)
                                                                                     (* c PHYS-CCMAX) s2))))
                                                         (rc (-> *phys-colchain* cb))
                                                         (k2 (-> *phys-colk2* cb))
                                                         ;; an at= volume rides the referenced
                                                         ;; chain's SIMULATED tip, so Keira's two
                                                         ;; breasts meet where they actually swung
                                                         ;; to — the owner's "elles s'entre-choquent".
                                                         (ca (if (>= rc 0)
                                                                 (-> *phys-pos* (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* (+ cbase rc))
                                                                                   (+ (-> *phys-clen* (+ cbase rc)) -1)))
                                                                 (-> skel bones (+ (-> *phys-colk* cb) 1) transform vector 3)))
                                                         (cbv (if (and (< rc 0) (>= k2 0))
                                                                  (-> skel bones (+ k2 1) transform vector 3)
                                                                  ca))
                                                         (r1 (-> *phys-colr* cb))
                                                         ;; TAPERED: the radius is read AT the
                                                         ;; contact, so a flared trouser leg and a
                                                         ;; shoulder are cones, not cylinders.
                                                         (tt (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt ca cbv pt))
                                                         (rr (fmin (+ (-> *phys-lrad* (+ start i)) radx r1
                                                                      (* tt (- (-> *phys-colr2* cb) r1)))
                                                                   (-> *phys-ccap* (+ (* i PHYS-CCMAX) s2)))))
                                                    (vector-! vtmp pt cpt)
                                                    (let ((dd (vector-length vtmp)))
                                                      ;; DEAD ZONE: a sub-tolerance overlap is the
                                                      ;; float noise the audit refuses to score.
                                                      ;; Re-projecting it every frame is chatter,
                                                      ;; and chatter under contact is what the
                                                      ;; owner called "jitter comme un fou".
                                                      (when (< dd (- rr PHYS-PEN-TOL))
                                                        (+! (-> *phys-slot-pushouts* slot) 1)
                                                        (+! chpush 1)
                                                        (set! (-> lpush i) 1)
                                                        (let ((pen (- rr dd)))
                                                          (when (> pen (-> *phys-slot-maxpen* slot))
                                                            (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxpen* slot) pen)))
                                                        (vector-copy! vtmp2 p)
                                                        ;; degenerate: the joint is exactly on the
                                                        ;; spine and there is no direction to
                                                        ;; normalise. Aim at its own target, then
                                                        ;; straight up.
                                                        (when (< dd 0.0001)
                                                          (vector-! vtmp tg cpt)
                                                          (set! dd (vector-length vtmp))
                                                          (when (< dd 0.0001)
                                                            (set! (-> vtmp x) 0.0)
                                                            (set! (-> vtmp y) 1.0)
                                                            (set! (-> vtmp z) 0.0)
                                                            (set! (-> vtmp w) 0.0)
                                                            (set! dd 1.0)))
                                                        (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp (/ rr dd))
                                                        (vector+! vtmp3 cpt vtmp)
                                                        (vector-! vtmp vtmp3 pt)
                                                        (let ((cl (vector-length vtmp)))
                                                          (when (> cl maxcorr)
                                                            (+! (-> *phys-slot-clamped* slot) 1)
                                                            (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp (/ maxcorr cl))))
                                                        (when (nonzero? probe?)
                                                          (vector+! pprb pprb vtmp))
                                                        (vector+! p p vtmp)))))))))))))))
                           ;; ---- VELOCITY-NEUTRAL CORRECTIONS (owner rule O, both directions)
                           ;; In a verlet integrator velocity is IMPLIED by (p - prev), so a
                           ;; projection that moves p and leaves prev behind is read next
                           ;; substep as velocity the chain never had. Run `iters` times that is
                           ;; a PUMP: gravity stretches the link, the distance constraint pulls
                           ;; it back, the pull-back becomes velocity, and the chain rings on
                           ;; with no input at all. Moving prev by the same delta cancels
                           ;; exactly that and nothing else — the correction stays, the
                           ;; spurious velocity goes, and no velocity is INJECTED either way.
                           ;; This is the whole of the hysteresis fix. It is not a suppressor:
                           ;; it removes energy the solver invented, never energy the chain had.
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (when (>= i rl)
                               (let ((p (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)))
                                     (pv (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i))))
                                 (vector-! vtmp p (-> *phys-psave* i))
                                 (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp PHYS-PROJFIX)
                                 (vector+! pv pv vtmp)))))
                         ;; ---- (B) the settle ramp, length-preserving, plus its burst audit --
                         (when (> (-> *phys-csettle* ci) 0)
                           (phys-chain-settle! slot start len sw rl)
                           (when (>= chainlen 1.0)
                             (let ((mx 0.0))
                               (dotimes (i len)
                                 (when (>= i rl)
                                   (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                                   (let ((d (vector-length vtmp)))
                                     (when (> d mx) (set! mx d)))))
                               (when (> mx (* PHYS-BURST-REL chainlen))
                                 (+! (-> *phys-slot-burst* slot) 1))))
                           (+! (-> *phys-csettle* ci) -1))
                         ;; ---- SANITY: a nan or an explosion resets to the authored pose -----
                         (let ((broken 0))
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (let ((p (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i))))
                               (vector-! vtmp p (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                               (let ((dev (vector-length vtmp)))
                                 (when (not (and (< dev (+ 100.0 (* 2.0 chainlen)))
                                                 (< (fabs (-> p x)) 100000000.0)
                                                 (< (fabs (-> p y)) 100000000.0)
                                                 (< (fabs (-> p z)) 100000000.0)))
                                   (set! broken 1)))))
                           (when (nonzero? broken)
                             (+! (-> *phys-slot-resets* slot) 1)
                             (dotimes (i len)
                               (vector-copy! (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                               (vector-copy! (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))))))
                         ;; ---- POSITIVE CONTROL: a DELIBERATE penetration, on demand ---------
                         ;; inject= is absent from the shipped data and is added by
                         ;; physics_c14_poscontrol.sh to the external override only. It walks
                         ;; every free link toward the nearest body volume's spine, so the audit
                         ;; below has something real to find. A zero from an audit that has
                         ;; never been shown to fire is worth nothing — five of them shipped.
                         (when (and (> (-> *phys-cinject* ci) 0.0) (nonzero? collide?))
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (when (>= i rl)
                               (let ((p (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)))
                                     (bestd 1000000.0))
                                 (vector-reset! xdir)
                                 (dotimes (s2 (-> *phys-ccn* ci))
                                   (let* ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS)
                                                 (-> *phys-cclist* (+ (* slot PHYS-CPS PHYS-CCMAX)
                                                                      (* c PHYS-CCMAX) s2))))
                                          (rc (-> *phys-colchain* cb))
                                          (k2 (-> *phys-colk2* cb)))
                                     (when (< rc 0)
                                       (let* ((ca (-> skel bones (+ (-> *phys-colk* cb) 1) transform vector 3))
                                              (cbv (if (>= k2 0)
                                                       (-> skel bones (+ k2 1) transform vector 3)
                                                       ca)))
                                         (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt ca cbv p)
                                         (vector-! vtmp cpt p)
                                         (let ((d (vector-length vtmp)))
                                           (when (< d bestd)
                                             (set! bestd d)
                                             (vector-copy! xdir vtmp)))))))
                                 (when (< bestd 999999.0)
                                   (let ((l (vector-length xdir)))
                                     (when (> l 0.0001)
                                       (vector-float*! xdir xdir
                                                       (/ (fmin (-> *phys-cinject* ci) l) l))
                                       (vector+! p p xdir)
                                       (vector+! (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i))
                                                 (-> *phys-prev* (+ start i)) xdir)
                                       (+! (-> *phys-slot-injected* slot) 1)))))))))

                       ;; ================= STEP 3b : COLLISION HAS THE LAST WORD =============
                       ;; The candidate the bone would receive is the SIMULATED pose. If any of
                       ;; the skinned mesh it carries is inside a body volume, walk the whole
                       ;; chain pose back toward the AUTHORED pose until it is not — by
                       ;; bisection, on the pose parameter, with the segment lengths preserved
                       ;; exactly at every t (phys-chain-blend!). Two properties make this the
                       ;; only resolve the solver needs:
                       ;;   * t=0 is feasible BY CONSTRUCTION, so the search always terminates
                       ;;     on a clear pose. That is why the eleven fallback passes are gone.
                       ;;   * the pose is continuous in t, so the correction cannot be a jump.
                       ;;     The owner's "des trucs bizarres plus genants qu'un simple
                       ;;     clipping" was a per-sample push loop overshooting between two
                       ;;     volumes; a bisection has no overshoot to have.
                       ;; The audit that drives it lives on the MESH, not on the bones: the
                       ;; skinned surface extends 2.8x-6x beyond the link radii, which is where
                       ;; the owner's eyes were and the old bone-level counters were not.
                       (dotimes (i len)
                         (vector-copy! (-> *phys-out0* (+ start i))
                                       (if (>= i rl) (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))))
                       (let ((tsel 1.0))
                         (when (nonzero? collide?)
                           (phys-chain-blend! slot ci start len 1.0 rl)
                           (let ((w1 (phys-chain-worst slot cbase c tier start len rl draw)))
                             (when (> w1 (-> *phys-slot-mraw* slot))
                               (set! (-> *phys-slot-mraw* slot) w1))
                             (when (> w1 PHYS-PEN-TOL)
                               (set! tsel 0.0)
                               (let ((thi 1.0))
                                 (dotimes (b PHYS-MESH-BISECT)
                                   (let ((tm (* 0.5 (+ tsel thi))))
                                     (phys-chain-blend! slot ci start len tm rl)
                                     (cond
                                       ((<= (phys-chain-worst slot cbase c tier start len rl draw)
                                            PHYS-PEN-TOL)
                                        (set! tsel tm))
                                       (else (set! thi tm))))))
                               (+! (-> *phys-slot-mfix* slot) 1)
                               (set! (-> *phys-ctmin* ci) tsel))))
                         (cond
                           ((and (nonzero? collide?) (< tsel 0.9999))
                            (phys-chain-blend! slot ci start len tsel rl)
                            (dotimes (i len)
                              (vector-copy! (-> *phys-out* (+ start i))
                                            (if (>= i rl) (-> *phys-cblend* i) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))))))
                           (else
                            (dotimes (i len)
                              (vector-copy! (-> *phys-out* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-out0* (+ start i)))))))

                       ;; ================= STEP 4 : WRITE THE BONE ===========================
                       ;; The 3x3 is swung by the SAME rotation that moved the position, so the
                       ;; basis stays orthonormal and stays consistent with the translation —
                       ;; the previous build wrote a rotation in one pass and translations in
                       ;; six more, so the bone's basis stopped matching its own position.
                       (dotimes (i len)
                         (cond
                           ((< i rl)
                            ;; locked: the bone is not touched, and it is read BACK to prove
                            ;; nothing else moved it.
                            (let ((k (-> *phys-jk* (+ start i))))
                              (when (< (+ k 1) nbones)
                                (vector-! vtmp (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform vector 3)
                                          (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                                (let ((d (vector-length vtmp)))
                                  (when (> d (-> *phys-slot-rootdev* slot))
                                    (set! (-> *phys-slot-rootdev* slot) d))))))
                           (else
                            (let* ((p (-> *phys-out* (+ start i)))
                                   (tg (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                                   (k (-> *phys-jk* (+ start i)))
                                   (pp (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-out* (+ start i -1))))
                                   (tp (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i -1)))))
                              (vector-! vtmp p tg)
                              (let ((dev (vector-length vtmp)))
                                (when (> dev frame-maxdev) (set! frame-maxdev dev))
                                (when (> dev (-> *phys-cdev* ci)) (set! (-> *phys-cdev* ci) dev))
                                (when (> dev (-> *phys-jdev* (+ start i)))
                                  (set! (-> *phys-jdev* (+ start i)) dev))
                                (when (and (zero? i) (zero? rl)
                                           (> dev (-> *phys-slot-freeroot* slot)))
                                  (set! (-> *phys-slot-freeroot* slot) dev)))
                              (when (< (+ k 1) nbones)
                                (let ((dst (the-as matrix (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform))))
                                  (vector-! dirt tg tp)
                                  (vector-! dirs p pp)
                                  (let ((lt (vector-length dirt))
                                        (ls (vector-length dirs)))
                                    (cond
                                      ((or (< lt 0.0001) (< ls 0.0001))
                                       (vector-copy! (-> dst vector 3) p)
                                       (set! (-> dst vector 3 w) 1.0))
                                      (else
                                       (vector-float*! dirt dirt (/ 1.0 lt))
                                       (vector-float*! dirs dirs (/ 1.0 ls))
                                       ;; swing= writes only a fraction of the rotation, for
                                       ;; rigs whose local axes are not the strand direction.
                                       (let ((swf (fmax 0.0 (fmin 1.0 (-> *phys-cswing* ci)))))
                                         (when (< swf 0.999)
                                           (vector-! vtmp dirs dirt)
                                           (vector-float*! vtmp vtmp swf)
                                           (vector+! dirs dirt vtmp)
                                           (let ((l2 (vector-length dirs)))
                                             (cond
                                               ((> l2 0.0001) (vector-float*! dirs dirs (/ 1.0 l2)))
                                               (else (vector-copy! dirs dirt))))))
                                       (let ((dot (vector-dot dirt dirs)))
                                         (cond
                                           ((or (> dot 0.99999) (< dot -0.999))
                                            (vector-copy! (-> dst vector 3) p)
                                            (set! (-> dst vector 3 w) 1.0))
                                           (else
                                            (quaternion-from-two-vectors! q dirt dirs)
                                            (quaternion->matrix rotm q)
                                            (matrix*! tmpm dst rotm)
                                            (dotimes (r 3)
                                              (vector-copy! (-> dst vector r) (-> tmpm vector r))
                                              (set! (-> dst vector r w) 0.0))
                                            (vector-copy! (-> dst vector 3) p)
                                            (set! (-> dst vector 3 w) 1.0)))))))))))))

                       ;; ================= STEP 5a : per-chain audits, from the WRITTEN pose ==
                       ;; RESIDUAL PENETRATION, at link level, against EVERY volume in the
                       ;; perimeter — with `tested` printed next to it, because a zero from a
                       ;; perimeter that excluded half the chains is exact and false (that was
                       ;; colskip on 202 chains and chains= on 2384 volumes).
                       (when (nonzero? collide?)
                         (let ((tested 0))
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (when (>= i rl)
                               (let* ((exth (* 0.5 (-> *phys-cext* ci)))
                                      (probe? (if (and (> exth 0.0) (= i (+ len -1))) 1 0))
                                      (radx (if (nonzero? probe?) exth 0.0)))
                                 (vector-copy! mprb (-> *phys-out* (+ start i)))
                                 (when (nonzero? probe?)
                                   (vector-! mprd mprb
                                             (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-out* (+ start i -1))))
                                   (let ((pl (vector-length mprd)))
                                     (when (> pl 0.0001)
                                       (vector-float*! mprd mprd (/ exth pl))
                                       (vector+! mprb mprb mprd))))
                                 (dotimes (s2 (-> *phys-ccn* ci))
                                   (let* ((cb (+ (* slot PHYS-COLS)
                                                 (-> *phys-cclist* (+ (* slot PHYS-CPS PHYS-CCMAX)
                                                                      (* c PHYS-CCMAX) s2))))
                                          (rc (-> *phys-colchain* cb))
                                          (k2 (-> *phys-colk2* cb))
                                          (ca (if (>= rc 0)
                                                  (-> *phys-out* (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* (+ cbase rc))
                                                                    (+ (-> *phys-clen* (+ cbase rc)) -1)))
                                                  (-> skel bones (+ (-> *phys-colk* cb) 1) transform vector 3)))
                                          (cbv (if (and (< rc 0) (>= k2 0))
                                                   (-> skel bones (+ k2 1) transform vector 3)
                                                   ca))
                                          (r1 (-> *phys-colr* cb))
                                          (tt (phys-closest-on-seg! cpt ca cbv mprb))
                                          (rr (fmin (+ (-> *phys-lrad* (+ start i)) radx r1
                                                       (* tt (- (-> *phys-colr2* cb) r1)))
                                                    (-> *phys-ccap* (+ (* i PHYS-CCMAX) s2)))))
                                     (+! tested 1)
                                     (vector-! vtmp mprb cpt)
                                     (let* ((dd (vector-length vtmp))
                                            (clr (- dd rr)))
                                       (when (< clr (-> *phys-cclr* ci))
                                         (set! (-> *phys-cclr* ci) clr))
                                       (when (< dd (- rr PHYS-PEN-TOL))
                                         (+! chresid 1)
                                         (+! (-> *phys-slot-resid* slot) 1)
                                         (let ((pen (- rr dd)))
                                           (when (> pen (-> *phys-slot-maxresid* slot))
                                             (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxresid* slot) pen)))
                                         ;; a residual in a volume belonging to the OTHER side of
                                         ;; the body is the crossed jacket pendant the owner named
                                         (let ((cs2 (-> *phys-colside* cb))
                                               (ms (-> *phys-cside* ci)))
                                           (when (and (> cs2 0) (> ms 0) (!= cs2 ms))
                                             (+! (-> *phys-slot-xleg* slot) 1))))))))))
                           (set! (-> *phys-cres* ci) chresid)
                           (+! (-> *phys-cpush* ci) chpush)))
                       ;; MESH-SURFACE RESIDUAL, on the pose that was actually written.
                       (when (nonzero? collide?)
                         (let ((mw 0.0)
                               (mt 0))
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (when (>= i rl)
                               (let* ((jj (+ start i))
                                      (k (-> *phys-jk* jj)))
                                 (when (and (> (-> *phys-msn* jj) 0) (< (+ k 1) nbones))
                                   (+! mt (-> *phys-msn* jj))
                                   (let* ((bm (the-as matrix (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform)))
                                          (e (phys-link-mesh-worst slot cbase c tier jj
                                                                   (-> *phys-out* jj) bm draw)))
                                     (when (> e mw) (set! mw e)))))))
                           (+! (-> *phys-slot-mtested* slot) mt)
                           (when (> mw (-> *phys-slot-meshpen* slot))
                             (set! (-> *phys-slot-meshpen* slot) mw))))
                       ;; (X) NOTHING MAY BE CRUSHED. Both ratios: the OUTPUT (what is drawn)
                       ;; and the SIMULATION state. Jak's collar is the owner's named case.
                       (when (>= chainlen 1.0)
                         (let ((lo 0.0)
                               (ls 0.0)
                               (la 0.0))
                           (dotimes (i len)
                             (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i))
                                       (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i -1))))
                             (set! la (+ la (vector-length vtmp)))
                             (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-out* (+ start i))
                                       (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-out* (+ start i -1))))
                             (set! lo (+ lo (vector-length vtmp)))
                             (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i))
                                       (if (zero? i) anchor (-> *phys-pos* (+ start i -1))))
                             (set! ls (+ ls (vector-length vtmp))))
                           (when (> la 0.0001)
                             (let ((ro (/ lo la))
                                   (rs (/ ls la)))
                               (when (< ro (-> *phys-slot-lenmin* slot))
                                 (set! (-> *phys-slot-lenmin* slot) ro))
                               (when (< rs (-> *phys-slot-lensim* slot))
                                 (set! (-> *phys-slot-lensim* slot) rs))
                               (when (< ro (-> *phys-clenr* ci))
                                 (set! (-> *phys-clenr* ci) ro))))))
                       ;; (W) MODEL-POSE FIDELITY, FAMILY A ONLY, POST-SETTLE.
                       ;; A body chain has to come back to the shape ND sculpted once it is
                       ;; calm — and the instantaneous deviation is NOT the criterion, because
                       ;; that would forbid the bounce the owner explicitly wants. So this is
                       ;; sampled only after the chain has been quiet for PHYS-RESTCALM frames,
                       ;; and restwin counts the samples so the figure can never be an empty
                       ;; zero. Nothing clamps the chain onto that pose: with hang=0 on family A
                       ;; the spring's own equilibrium IS the model pose, so it arrives there by
                       ;; being a spring. (The pass that used to WALK it there — arrival — is
                       ;; what welded the chains and produced a week of false greens.)
                       (let ((quiet (if (and (< (-> *phys-canchd* ci) PHYS-IDLE-ANCH)
                                             (<= (-> *phys-csettle* ci) 0))
                                        1 0)))
                         (cond
                           ((nonzero? quiet) (+! (-> *phys-ccalm* ci) 1))
                           (else (set! (-> *phys-ccalm* ci) 0)))
                         (when (and (= 1 (-> *phys-cfam* ci))
                                    (>= (-> *phys-ccalm* ci) PHYS-RESTCALM)
                                    (>= chainlen 1.0))
                           (let ((worst 0.0))
                             (dotimes (i len)
                               (when (>= i rl)
                                 (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-out* (+ start i)) (-> *phys-targ* (+ start i)))
                                 (let ((d (vector-length vtmp)))
                                   (when (> d worst) (set! worst d)))))
                             (+! (-> *phys-slot-restwin* slot) 1)
                             (when (> worst (-> *phys-slot-restdeva* slot))
                               (set! (-> *phys-slot-restdeva* slot) worst))
                             (when (> worst (-> *phys-crestd* ci))
                               (set! (-> *phys-crestd* ci) worst)))))
                       ;; (O/S) OSCILLATION, counted on the WRITTEN bone and nowhere else: a
                       ;; sign change of the per-frame displacement above a noise floor. The
                       ;; retired metric only scored a reversal while a link was PRESSED against
                       ;; a collider, which threw away exactly the population the owner calls
                       ;; hysteresis — hair, ears, a collar and lurker legs in OPEN AIR.
                       (let ((chspeed 0.0))
                         (dotimes (i len)
                           (when (>= i rl)
                             (let ((jj (+ start i)))
                               ;; dev = the WRITTEN position in the AUTHORED frame. Differencing
                               ;; here and not on the raw world position is what divides out the
                               ;; body carry: an actor crossing 4032 units in a frame takes his
                               ;; hair with him, and that is not chain motion.
                               (vector-! vtmp2 (-> *phys-out* jj) (-> *phys-targ* jj))
                               (vector-! vtmp vtmp2 (-> *phys-oprev* jj))
                               (let ((sp (vector-length vtmp)))
                                 (when (> sp chspeed) (set! chspeed sp))
                                 (when (> sp frame-maxvel) (set! frame-maxvel sp))
                                 (when (and (> sp PHYS-JITTER-SPEED)
                                            (> (vector-length (-> *phys-vprev* jj)) PHYS-JITTER-SPEED)
                                            (< (vector-dot vtmp (-> *phys-vprev* jj)) 0.0))
                                   (+! (-> *phys-slot-jitter* slot) 1)
                                   ;; free-space ringing: a reversal with NO contact at all. That
                                   ;; is the population the retired contact-only metric threw
                                   ;; away, and it is exactly what the owner calls hysteresis.
                                   (when (zero? (-> lpush i))
                                     (+! (-> *phys-slot-freering* slot) 1))))
                               (vector-copy! (-> *phys-vprev* jj) vtmp)
                               (vector-copy! (-> *phys-oprev* jj) vtmp2))))
                         ;; rested is a MEASUREMENT, not a mechanism: chain-frames whose written
                         ;; motion is below the rest bar. Nothing is frozen to produce it.
                         (when (< chspeed PHYS-REST-VEL)
                           (+! (-> *phys-slot-rested* slot) 1))
                         (set! (-> *phys-cself* ci) chspeed)
                         ;; the actor-wide self-motion, for the IDLE DRIFT gate. Chains that are
                         ;; settling in from a cut or held by the animator are excluded: they are
                         ;; supposed to be moving toward a pose that is not their own equilibrium,
                         ;; so grading them as drift would fail the one mechanism that is correct.
                         (when (and (<= (-> *phys-csettle* ci) 0)
                                    (< authw 0.5)
                                    (> chspeed frame-self))
                           (set! frame-self chspeed)))
                       ))))))) ;; close let(kd/gacc) / let* / else / cond / when / let* / dotimes

            ;; ================= STEP 3c : STRAND vs STRAND ================================
            ;; Two elements that both carry physics could not see each other at all: a chain
            ;; was a line of points. That is Jak's back buckle through his own hanging strap,
            ;; Keira's goggles into her chest and her bangs through her ears — the owner's
            ;; "encore plus les elements a physique avec d'autres elements a physique".
            ;; Each link now carries its own mesh-derived radius, partners come from xchain=,
            ;; and a push is VETOED if it would drive either link deeper into the body: the
            ;; strand pass may not undo the body pass, which had the last word before it.
            (dotimes (a (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
              (let* ((cia (+ cbase a))
                     (la (-> *phys-clen* cia))
                     (sa (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* cia)))
                     (rla (max 0 (min (+ la -1) (-> *phys-crootlock* cia)))))
                (when (and (> la 0) (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* cia) classmask)))
                  (dotimes (b (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                    (when (> b a)
                      (let* ((cib (+ cbase b))
                             (lb (-> *phys-clen* cib))
                             (sb (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* cib)))
                             (rlb (max 0 (min (+ lb -1) (-> *phys-crootlock* cib)))))
                        (when (and (> lb 0)
                                   (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* cib) classmask))
                                   (> (-> *phys-cbsr* cia) 0.0)
                                   (> (-> *phys-cbsr* cib) 0.0)
                                   (begin
                                     (vector-! vtmp (-> *phys-cbsp* cia) (-> *phys-cbsp* cib))
                                     (<= (vector-length vtmp)
                                         (+ (-> *phys-cbsr* cia) (-> *phys-cbsr* cib)
                                            PHYS-REACH-MARGIN))))
                          (+! (-> *phys-slot-ccpairs* slot) 1)
                          (dotimes (i la)
                            (when (>= i rla)
                              (dotimes (j lb)
                                (when (>= j rlb)
                                  (let ((pa (-> *phys-out* (+ sa i)))
                                        (pb (-> *phys-out* (+ sb j)))
                                        (rr (+ (-> *phys-lrad* (+ sa i)) (-> *phys-lrad* (+ sb j)))))
                                    (vector-! xdir pa pb)
                                    (let ((d (vector-length xdir)))
                                      (when (and (< d (- rr PHYS-PEN-TOL)) (> d 0.0001))
                                        (let ((half (* 0.5 (- rr d))))
                                          (vector-float*! xdir xdir (/ half d))
                                          ;; veto: never deeper into the character's own body
                                          (vector+! xcand pa xdir)
                                          (let ((p0 (phys-body-pen slot cbase jbase a (+ sa i) tier pa draw))
                                                (p1 (phys-body-pen slot cbase jbase a (+ sa i) tier xcand draw)))
                                            (cond
                                              ((> p1 (+ p0 PHYS-PEN-TOL))
                                               (+! (-> *phys-slot-xveto* slot) 1))
                                              (else
                                               (vector-copy! pa xcand)
                                               (+! (-> *phys-slot-ccc* slot) 1)
                                               (when (> (- rr d) (-> *phys-slot-cccmax* slot))
                                                 (set! (-> *phys-slot-cccmax* slot) (- rr d))))))
                                          (vector-! xcand pb xdir)
                                          (let ((p0 (phys-body-pen slot cbase jbase b (+ sb j) tier pb draw))
                                                (p1 (phys-body-pen slot cbase jbase b (+ sb j) tier xcand draw)))
                                            (cond
                                              ((> p1 (+ p0 PHYS-PEN-TOL))
                                               (+! (-> *phys-slot-xveto* slot) 1))
                                              (else (vector-copy! pb xcand)))))))))))))))))))
            ;; commit the strand pass to the bones (translation row only: the swing was
            ;; already written and a contact displacement of a few units does not re-aim it)
            (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
              (let* ((ci (+ cbase c))
                     (len (-> *phys-clen* ci))
                     (start (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci)))
                     (rl (max 0 (min (+ len -1) (-> *phys-crootlock* ci)))))
                (when (and (> len 0) (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* ci) classmask)))
                  (dotimes (i len)
                    (when (>= i rl)
                      (let ((k (-> *phys-jk* (+ start i))))
                        (when (< (+ k 1) nbones)
                          (vector-copy! (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform vector 3)
                                        (-> *phys-out* (+ start i)))
                          (set! (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform vector 3 w) 1.0))))))))

            ;; ---- RIGID DESCENDANTS: a joint below a moved bone must follow it ------------
            ;; Otherwise the mesh tears at the boundary. Iterated so a chain of descendants
            ;; propagates in one frame.
            (dotimes (k (min PHYS-MAXJ rig))
              (set! (-> moved k) 0))
            (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
              (let* ((ci (+ cbase c))
                     (len (-> *phys-clen* ci))
                     (start (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci)))
                     (rl (max 0 (min (+ len -1) (-> *phys-crootlock* ci)))))
                (when (and (> len 0) (zero? (-> *phys-cnodesc* ci))
                           (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* ci) classmask)))
                  (dotimes (i len)
                    (when (>= i rl)
                      (let ((k (-> *phys-jk* (+ start i))))
                        (when (< k PHYS-MAXJ) (set! (-> moved k) 1))))))))
            (let ((more 1))
              (dotimes (dp 4)
                (when (nonzero? more)
                  (set! more 0)
                  (dotimes (k (min PHYS-MAXJ rig))
                    (when (and (zero? (-> moved k)) (< (+ k 1) nbones))
                      (let ((p (the int (-> *phys-par* (+ pbase k)))))
                        (when (and (!= p #xff) (< p PHYS-MAXJ) (< (+ p 1) nbones) (nonzero? (-> moved p)))
                          (matrix-4x4-inverse! hbind (-> hd-jgeo data k bind-pose))
                          (matrix*! lkm hbind (-> hd-jgeo data p bind-pose))
                          (matrix*! (-> skel bones (+ k 1) transform) lkm
                                    (the-as matrix (-> skel bones (+ p 1) transform)))
                          (set! (-> moved k) 1)
                          (set! more 1)
                          (+! frame-ndesc 1))))))))
            ;; ---------------- windowed proof counters ----------------
            ;; (C14-D) resolution jerk: the worst single-frame NET resolution displacement any
            ;; link took, across every pass that moved one (the length of the frame's summed
            ;; correction vectors — see the *phys-lresv* declaration for why net, not path).
            ;; This is the number behind "des trucs bizarres plus genants qu'un simple clipping" —
            ;; a resolution the eye can see as a jump is a resolution worse than the clip it
            ;; replaced, and what the eye sees is where the bone ended the frame.
            ;; (C14c) THE LEDGER ABOVE CANNOT BE THIS NUMBER, AND THE DEVICE PROVED IT ARITHMETICALLY.
            ;; The declaration of *phys-lresv* already states the right definition — "what the eye
            ;; reads as a snap is where the bone ENDED the frame relative to where resolution found
            ;; it" — but summing correction VECTORS does not compute it, for a reason the first fix
            ;; (magnitude-sum -> vector-sum, after a still link read 100853) did not reach: the force
            ;; that undoes a correction is the SPRING, and the spring never writes to the ledger. So
            ;; the sum only ever sees one side of the argument and grows monotonically while the bone
            ;; goes nowhere. On the 09:46 device run, jak-hd's worst window read
            ;;     resjerk = 66389.27   while   maxdev = 1031.47
            ;; — a claimed 16-metre single-frame jump by a bone that never left a 25 cm neighbourhood
            ;; of its own authored pose all window. That is not a strict instrument, it is an
            ;; impossible reading, and it was hiding the two real defects it sat next to.
            ;;
            ;; What the eye actually sees is the link's offset FROM ITS AUTHORED POSE, frame over
            ;; frame: the authored pose travels with the character, so differencing against it
            ;; divides out the body carry (an actor crossing 4032 units in a frame carries his hair
            ;; with him; that is not a snap) and leaves exactly the artifact — the physics offset
            ;; changing discontinuously. A settled link holds its offset and reads ~0; an honest
            ;; swing reads its own per-frame travel (maxvel, ~117 on that same window); a real
            ;; one-frame snap reads its full visible size. It also sees EVERY pass, including the
            ;; model-pose ladder, the escape pass and the length restore, which write out/pos/prev
            ;; and never touched the ledger at all — so the correction is strictly more complete,
            ;; not laxer, and it cannot be satisfied by killing the sim because the locomotion
            ;; FLOORS (hairrun/chestrun) are graded on this same run.
            ;; The old ledger is still computed and still printed, as respath=, so the swap is
            ;; auditable rather than silent.
            (dotimes (k PHYS-JPS)
              (let ((nj (vector-length (-> *phys-lresv* (+ jbase k)))))
                (when (> nj (-> *phys-slot-respath* slot))
                  (set! (-> *phys-slot-respath* slot) nj))))
            (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
              (let* ((ci (+ cbase c))
                     (len (-> *phys-clen* ci))
                     (start (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci))))
                (when (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* ci) classmask))
                  ;; (C16) THE DENOMINATOR for the three suppressor shares. Taken here because this
                  ;; fold is the one place that runs exactly once per ACTIVE chain per frame.
                  (+! (-> *phys-slot-simcf* slot) 1)
                  (let ((fvar 0.0)   ;; this frame's worst per-link offset CHANGE on this chain
                        (fdev 0.0)   ;; this frame's worst per-link offset MAGNITUDE
                        (fsamp 0))   ;; 1 = at least one link produced a differenced sample
                  (dotimes (i len)
                    (let ((jj (+ start i))
                          (tmv 0.0)
                          (dn (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector))
                          (dd (new 'stack-no-clear 'vector)))
                      (vector-! dn (-> *phys-out* jj) (-> *phys-targ* jj))
                      (vector-! dd (-> *phys-targ* jj) (-> *phys-ltarg* jj))
                      (set! tmv (vector-length dd))
                      ;; frames=0 is this slot's first frame (it is incremented below), so there is
                      ;; no previous deviation to difference against; csettle>0 is the spawn ramp,
                      ;; where the chain is deliberately being moved onto its pose; and a frame on
                      ;; which the AUTHORED pose moved more than PHYS-CUT-DELTA is a cut, where the
                      ;; delta measures the animation rather than the resolution.
                      (when (and (> (-> *phys-slot-frames* slot) 0)
                                 (<= (-> *phys-csettle* ci) 0)
                                 (< tmv PHYS-CUT-DELTA))
                        ;; (cycle-15) ATTRIBUTION. resjerk is a magnitude and magnitudes do not say
                        ;; which way; three cycles were spent guessing at this number's sign. The
                        ;; signed change in |offset| separates a link being FLUNG (rjup) from a
                        ;; link whose whole deviation was collapsed onto the authored pose in one
                        ;; frame (rjdn) — they have different causes and different fixes — and
                        ;; rjtm records how far the AUTHORED pose itself travelled on the frame
                        ;; that set the maximum, which is the share of the "jump" that is inertia
                        ;; lagging a fast animation rather than the solver moving anything.
                        (let ((gd (- (vector-length dn) (vector-length (-> *phys-ldev* jj)))))
                          (when (> gd (-> *phys-slot-rjup* slot))
                            (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjup* slot) gd))
                          (when (> (- gd) (-> *phys-slot-rjdn* slot))
                            (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjdn* slot) (- gd))))
                        (vector-! dd dn (-> *phys-ldev* jj))
                        (let ((nj (vector-length dd))
                              (dvl (vector-length dn)))
                          (when (> nj (-> *phys-slot-resjerk* slot))
                            (set! (-> *phys-slot-resjerk* slot) nj)
                            (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjtm* slot) tmv))
                          ;; (C16) the honest floor's per-frame sample, under the SAME guard as
                          ;; resjerk on purpose: frame 0 has no predecessor, a settle ramp is being
                          ;; deliberately moved onto its pose, and a cut frame measures the
                          ;; animation rather than the physics.
                          (set! fsamp 1)
                          (when (> nj fvar) (set! fvar nj))
                          (when (> dvl fdev) (set! fdev dvl))))
                      (vector-copy! (-> *phys-ldev* jj) dn)
                      (vector-copy! (-> *phys-ltarg* jj) (-> *phys-targ* jj))
                      (when (> tmv frame-tmove) (set! frame-tmove tmv))))
                  ;; (C16) THE INERTNESS DETECTOR. Armed on any frame this chain's own anchor
                  ;; actually moved — a jolt, a step, a turn — not only on locomotion, because
                  ;; a standing villager whose head snaps round drives his hair without ever
                  ;; travelling 60 units in a frame. `civ/cish` is the MEAN written motion over
                  ;; those frames, and a chain that stays under PHYS-INERT-BAR across
                  ;; PHYS-INERT-N of them is INERT and fails the phase by name.
                  (when (and (> fsamp 0)
                             (<= (-> *phys-csettle* ci) 0)
                             (< (-> *phys-cauth* ci) 0.5)
                             (> (-> *phys-canchd* ci) PHYS-IDLE-ANCH))
                    (set! (-> *phys-civ* ci) (+ (-> *phys-civ* ci) fvar))
                    (+! (-> *phys-cish* ci) 1))
                  ;; (C16) fold this frame into the chain's window — LOCOMOTION frames only, the
                  ;; identical gate `crun` uses, so the honest floor and the retired magnitude one
                  ;; are graded on exactly the same frames and can be compared side by side.
                  (when (and (> fsamp 0)
                             (<= (-> *phys-csettle* ci) 0)
                             (> (-> *phys-canchd* ci) PHYS-RUN-ANCH))
                    ;; (C16) THE MOTION FLOOR ITSELF. `crun` is now the PATH LENGTH the written
                    ;; joint travelled in the authored frame over the window's locomotion frames
                    ;; — the sum of |dev(t) - dev(t-1)| — and no longer |dev|, the magnitude of
                    ;; the offset. A chain welded 352 units off its rest pose scored 352 on the
                    ;; retired form while visually static; on this one it scores ~0, which is the
                    ;; whole point (SPEC 16).
                    (set! (-> *phys-crun* ci) (+ (-> *phys-crun* ci) fvar))
                    (set! (-> *phys-cvsum* ci) (+ (-> *phys-cvsum* ci) fvar))
                    (+! (-> *phys-cvn* ci) 1)
                    (when (> fvar (-> *phys-cvmax* ci)) (set! (-> *phys-cvmax* ci) fvar))
                    (when (> fdev (-> *phys-cdmax* ci)) (set! (-> *phys-cdmax* ci) fdev))
                    ;; cvn was just incremented, so ==1 is this window's first sample: it seeds the
                    ;; minimum without needing a sentinel value that a real reading could collide with.
                    (when (or (= (-> *phys-cvn* ci) 1) (< fdev (-> *phys-cdmin* ci)))
                      (set! (-> *phys-cdmin* ci) fdev)))))))
            (when (> frame-maxdev (-> *phys-slot-maxdev* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxdev* slot) frame-maxdev))
            (when (> frame-maxvel (-> *phys-slot-maxvel* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxvel* slot) frame-maxvel))
            ;; (FAM) window MAXIMA, not last-frame values: a companion whose look changes mid-window
            ;; binds a different chain set, and the number the report needs is "how many were ever
            ;; simulating", not "how many happened to be simulating on the frame the window closed".
            (when (> frame-fama (-> *phys-slot-fama* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-fama* slot) frame-fama))
            (when (> frame-famb (-> *phys-slot-famb* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-famb* slot) frame-famb))
            (when (> frame-unclass (-> *phys-slot-unclass* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-unclass* slot) frame-unclass))
            ;; ---- (S) IDLE DRIFT, judged once the whole actor has been polled -----------------
            ;; NO anchor on this actor moved this frame, no chain is settling in from a spawn and
            ;; none is owned by the authored animation. There is no input. Whatever moved, moved by
            ;; itself — and that is the defect the owner described as "ca se balade meme sans
            ;; mouvement et ca FLOTTE". Owner bar: ~0.
            ;; INPUT-FREE = every anchor still AND every target still. The second half is the
            ;; cycle-4 correction: without it a turning NPC books its driven swing as drift.
            ;; ...and only once the actor has ALREADY been input-free for half a second. A chain
            ;; still settling out of the motion that just stopped is doing exactly what it should —
            ;; that transient is what settletime grades. What the owner described is a chain that
            ;; keeps wandering long after everything stopped, so drift is sampled only there.
            (when (and (< frame-anchd PHYS-IDLE-ANCH)
                       (< frame-tmove PHYS-IDLE-TARG)
                       (>= (-> *phys-slot-idleframes* slot) PHYS-IDLE-SETTLED))
              (+! (-> *phys-slot-idleobs* slot) 1)
              (when (> frame-self (-> *phys-slot-idle* slot))
                (set! (-> *phys-slot-idle* slot) frame-self))
              ;; the same verdict, attributed. Taken here and not in the chain loop because
              ;; "was this frame input-free" is a property of the whole actor and is only known
              ;; once every chain has been polled.
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (let ((ci (+ cbase c)))
                  (when (> (-> *phys-cself* ci) (-> *phys-cidr* ci))
                    (set! (-> *phys-cidr* ci) (-> *phys-cself* ci))))))
            ;; ---- (S) SETTLE TIME — decay, not the absence of contact -------------------------
            ;; The owner's instruction after cycle 3 was explicit: measure the DECAY to rest after
            ;; the driving motion stops, not whether anything is touching. So: the moment the anchor
            ;; goes still, start counting; the moment the fastest link drops under the rest speed,
            ;; that count IS the settle time, and the window keeps the WORST one. A stretch that is
            ;; still moving a whole second later is counted as a failure to settle instead of
            ;; silently never producing a number — an instrument that only reports successes is the
            ;; mistake that cost this phase a cycle.
            (cond
              ((or (> frame-anchd PHYS-IDLE-ANCH) (> frame-tmove PHYS-IDLE-TARG))
               (set! (-> *phys-slot-idleframes* slot) 0)
               (set! (-> *phys-slot-settled* slot) 0))
              (else
               (+! (-> *phys-slot-idleframes* slot) 1)
               (cond
                 ((nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-settled* slot)))
                 ((< frame-maxvel PHYS-REST-VEL)
                  (set! (-> *phys-slot-settled* slot) 1)
                  (when (> (-> *phys-slot-idleframes* slot) (-> *phys-slot-settletime* slot))
                    (set! (-> *phys-slot-settletime* slot) (-> *phys-slot-idleframes* slot))))
                 ((= (-> *phys-slot-idleframes* slot) PHYS-SETTLE-BAR)
                  (+! (-> *phys-slot-unsettled* slot) 1)))))
            (when (> frame-nreglue (-> *phys-slot-reglue* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-reglue* slot) frame-nreglue))
            (when (> frame-ndesc (-> *phys-slot-desc* slot))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-desc* slot) frame-ndesc))
            (+! (-> *phys-slot-nopose* slot) frame-nopose)
            ;; rest convergence: 30 consecutive calm frames -> the spring has settled back
            (cond
              ((< frame-maxvel 2.0)
               (+! (-> *phys-slot-calm* slot) 1)
               (when (= (-> *phys-slot-calm* slot) 30)
                 (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S rest-converged: restdev=~f (chain returned to rest)~%"
                         ag frame-maxdev)))
              (else
               (set! (-> *phys-slot-calm* slot) 0)))
            (+! (-> *phys-slot-frames* slot) 1)
            (when (>= (-> *phys-slot-frames* slot) 300)
              ;; A GOAL call carries at most 8 parameters, so the window needs several format calls —
              ;; but each `format 0` is routed to Android's log as its OWN logcat line, which split
              ;; the window across three lines on device and made every line-based device gate read
              ;; push=/maxpen= as ABSENT (cycle-5 measurement bug: the x86 stdout stream concatenated
              ;; them, the device stream did not). Build the whole window in a string buffer first
              ;; (format to a string APPENDS; clear starts it) and emit it with ONE call, so the
              ;; window is exactly ONE line on BOTH targets.
              ;; ---- (D) FROZEN AUDIT — must run BEFORE the per-chain deviations are cleared ------
              ;; Owner: Keira's short back hair "a l'air de ne pas etre dans le rayon d'influence et
              ;; donc est completement stiff". A chain that is DECLARED, class-live and simulated,
              ;; yet never moved 1.5 mm in a window where its actor demonstrably did, is that defect
              ;; — and it is invisible to every aggregate counter, which is why it survived a cycle.
              ;; Chains the authored animation currently owns are excluded: they are supposed to sit
              ;; still relative to their (authored) target. Owner bar: frozen=0.
              ;; CYCLE 10: armed on THIS CHAIN'S OWN anchor travel (see *phys-canchmv*), not on the
              ;; actor-wide maximum. Strictly sharper in both directions — a chain whose own anchor
              ;; was driven and did not respond is still caught, which is the Keira-back-hair defect
              ;; this counter was built for, and a chain nobody drove is no longer reported as
              ;; inert for resting. The old form was in direct contradiction with idledrift, which
              ;; fails a chain for moving when its own input is still: between them, a quiet chain
              ;; on a busy actor could not satisfy both.
              ;; CYCLE 16 — AND IT NOW MEASURES MOTION INSTEAD OF MAGNITUDE. The retired form
              ;; asked `is |dev| small?`, which is the identical mistake `crun` was making at the
              ;; other end of the scale: a chain WELDED at a large constant offset passed this
              ;; audit for six days while the owner watched it not move ("les meches sont
              ;; ANCREES", "la poitrine de Keira est COMPLETEMENT STATIQUE"). The verdict is now
              ;; the MEAN FRAME-TO-FRAME motion of the written joint over the frames this
              ;; chain's own anchor was really driven, and cish is printed next to it so a
              ;; not-inert verdict can never be the empty kind — cish=0 means UNJUDGED, not
              ;; healthy, and it is reported as unjudged.
              (let ((nfrozen 0))
                (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                  (let ((ci (+ cbase c)))
                    (when (and (> (-> *phys-clen* ci) 0)
                               (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* ci) classmask))
                               (< (-> *phys-cauth* ci) 0.5)
                               (>= (-> *phys-cish* ci) PHYS-INERT-N)
                               (< (/ (-> *phys-civ* ci) (the float (-> *phys-cish* ci)))
                                  PHYS-INERT-BAR))
                      (+! nfrozen 1))))
                (set! (-> *phys-slot-frozen* slot) nfrozen))
              (format (clear *phys-line-buf*)
                      "[HD-PHYS] ag=~S lvl=~D window: chains=~D joints=~D act=~D cm=~D"
                      ag
                      level
                      (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-njoints* slot)
                      frame-nact
                      classmask)
              (format *phys-line-buf*
                      " maxdev=~f maxvel=~f anchmove=~f nan-resets=~D (verlet state dump bounded)"
                      (-> *phys-slot-maxdev* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-maxvel* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-anchmove* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-resets* slot))
              ;; FIELD NAMING IS LOAD-BEARING: every device gate is a line-based grep, so no field
              ;; name may CONTAIN another's. `freeroot=` (not freerootdev=) and `residmax=` (not
              ;; maxresid=) exist precisely so `grep -v 'rootdev=0.0000 '` and `grep -v 'resid=0 '`
              ;; cannot match the wrong field and report a drifting root / residual penetration as
              ;; clean. Rename one of these and you silently disarm its gate.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " push=~D maxpen=~f resid=~D residmax=~f"
                      (-> *phys-slot-pushouts* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-maxpen* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-resid* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-maxresid* slot))
              ;; GOAL caps a call at 8 parameters (format + dest + fmt-string + 7 args = 9 = too
              ;; many), so this is two calls — which is FINE and is exactly why the whole window is
              ;; assembled in a string buffer: appending to a string does not split the line, only
              ;; `format 0` does.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " tier=~D cols=~D reglue=~D desc=~D nopose=~D"
                      tier
                      (-> *phys-slot-ncols* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-reglue* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-desc* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-nopose* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " rootdev=~f freeroot=~f"
                      (-> *phys-slot-rootdev* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-freeroot* slot))
              ;; per-chain window deviation — the whole list, never a top-N (a silent cap would read
              ;; as "every chain covered"). Same line, so line-based device gates still match.
              ;; The INPUT side of the per-chain question, chain by chain: how far this chain's own
              ;; anchor travelled in the window. Printed rather than merely used, because it is what
              ;; the frozen verdict is now armed on — a `0=0.0000` in cdev sitting next to a
              ;; `0=0.0000` here says "nobody drove it", and next to a large one says "it was driven
              ;; and did not answer", which is the defect.
              ;; DELIBERATELY AHEAD OF cdev: every existing parser of this line — the device leg's
              ;; chest-amplitude awk, its never-moved count, physics_c4_harvest — anchors on
              ;; `cdev:` and reads to END OF LINE. A list appended after it would silently join the
              ;; cdev population and, in the never-moved counter, be read as inert chains.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " canch:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c (-> *phys-canchmv* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-canchmv* (+ cbase c)) 0.0))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cdev:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c (-> *phys-cdev* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-cdev* (+ cbase c)) 0.0))
              (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*)
              ;; ---- CYCLE-3 SECOND WINDOW LINE ---------------------------------------------------
              ;; A SEPARATE line, not more fields on the first: the cycle-2 line is already the
              ;; longest thing this file prints and every device gate greps it by field name. Tag
              ;; `[HD-PHYS2]` so `grep '\[HD-PHYS\]'` — which every existing gate uses — cannot match
              ;; it, and it carries NO field name the first line owns (no maxdev=, no resid=, no
              ;; anchmove=), so no gate can read one line's number off the other.
              ;; Same one-call rule as line 1: assembled in the buffer, emitted with a single
              ;; `format 0`, because on Android every `format 0` is its own logcat line.
              (format (clear *phys-line-buf*)
                      "[HD-PHYS2] ag=~S authhold=~D autheng=~D authrel=~D authmax=~f"
                      ag
                      (-> *phys-slot-authhold* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-autheng* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-authrel* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-authmax* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " jitter=~D stickmax=~D rested=~D clamped=~D"
                      (-> *phys-slot-jitter* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-stickmax* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-rested* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-clamped* slot))
              ;; (P) the profile's worst adjacent step and its lowest root weight, recomputed from
              ;; the live table rather than restated from the config: the gate has to grade what the
              ;; solver BUILT, not what the data asked for.
              (let ((mstep 0.0) (rmin 1.0))
                (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                  (let* ((ci (+ cbase c))
                         (ln (-> *phys-clen* ci))
                         (st (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci))))
                    (when (> ln 0)
                      (when (< (-> *phys-infl* st) rmin)
                        (set! rmin (-> *phys-infl* st)))
                      (dotimes (i (+ ln -1))
                        (let ((d (fabs (- (-> *phys-infl* (+ st i 1)) (-> *phys-infl* (+ st i))))))
                          (when (> d mstep) (set! mstep d)))))))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " inflstep=~f rootinfl=~f" mstep rmin))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " reseed=~D burst=~D frozen=~D holdmax=~D"
                      (-> *phys-slot-reseed* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-burst* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-frozen* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-holdmax* slot))
              ;; the authored DETECTOR's raw reading per chain, whether or not it ever engaged: this
              ;; is what separates "ND never drives this bone" from "the threshold is mis-set".
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cres:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~D" c (-> *phys-cres* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-cres* (+ cbase c)) 0))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " aratio:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c (-> *phys-cauthmax* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-cauthmax* (+ cbase c)) 0.0))
              ;; per-LINK window spans, grouped by chain (`c<idx>:root:...:tip`). The whole list,
              ;; never a top-N: this is the instrument that answers "only the bout du bout moves".
              (format *phys-line-buf* " jdev:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (let ((ci (+ cbase c)))
                  (when (> (-> *phys-clen* ci) 0)
                    (format *phys-line-buf* " c~D" c)
                    (dotimes (i (-> *phys-clen* ci))
                      (let ((jj (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* ci) i)))
                        (format *phys-line-buf* ":~f" (-> *phys-jdev* jj))
                        (set! (-> *phys-jdev* jj) 0.0))))))
              (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*)
              ;; ---- CYCLE-4 THIRD WINDOW LINE ----------------------------------------------------
              ;; Its own line for the same reason [HD-PHYS2] is: every device gate is a line-based
              ;; grep, [HD-PHYS] is already the longest thing this file prints, and no field name here
              ;; is a substring of any field on the other two lines (a nested name silently disarms
              ;; the gate that greps the shorter one). These are the counters that replace a metric
              ;; the owner correctly called out as measuring the wrong thing.
              ;; (U) counted here rather than per frame: both are properties of the BINDING, so a
              ;; frame loop would only multiply them by 300 and say nothing new.
              (let ((noncol 0)
                    (nomask 0))
                (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                  (let ((ci (+ cbase c)))
                    (when (and (> (-> *phys-clen* ci) 0)
                               (nonzero? (logand (-> *phys-cflags* ci) classmask)))
                      (when (or (zero? tier) (<= (-> *phys-cradius* ci) 0.0))
                        (+! noncol 1))
                      (when (zero? (-> *phys-cncol* ci))
                        (+! nomask 1)))))
                (set! (-> *phys-slot-noncol* slot) noncol)
                (set! (-> *phys-slot-nomask* slot) nomask))
              (format (clear *phys-line-buf*)
                      "[HD-PHYS3] ag=~S idledrift=~f settletime=~D unsettled=~D freering=~D"
                      ag
                      (-> *phys-slot-idle* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-settletime* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-unsettled* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-freering* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " noncol=~D nomask=~D"
                      (-> *phys-slot-noncol* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-nomask* slot))
              ;; idlewin = the frames this window actually scored as input-free, slept = the
              ;; chain-frames the sleep rule zeroed. idledrift=0 with idlewin=0 is an EMPTY zero and
              ;; must be read as "not measured" — the same trap resid=0/push=0 was in cycle 3.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " idlewin=~D slept=~D arrn=~D"
                      (-> *phys-slot-idleobs* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-slept* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-arrn* slot))
              ;; (R) the gravity the integrator really applied, in WORLD axes and then in the anchor
              ;; bone's axes. gdir must read (0.0000, -1.0000, 0.0000) on every actor at every
              ;; orientation; gloc must NOT, or gravity would be turning with the bone.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " gsamp=~D" (-> *phys-slot-gsamp* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " gdir=(~f, ~f, ~f)"
                      (-> *phys-slot-gdir* slot x)
                      (-> *phys-slot-gdir* slot y)
                      (-> *phys-slot-gdir* slot z))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " gloc=(~f, ~f, ~f)"
                      (-> *phys-slot-gloc* slot x)
                      (-> *phys-slot-gloc* slot y)
                      (-> *phys-slot-gloc* slot z))
              ;; (U) per-chain minimum CLEARANCE to the body volumes that apply to it. Negative =
              ;; ended a frame inside the body. A large positive number on a chain the owner watches
              ;; go through a character means the volumes are not where the chain travels — which is
              ;; the difference between a solver bug and a collider bug, and it is exactly what
              ;; push=0 with resid=0 could not tell anybody.
              ;; (S/cycle-10) per-chain attribution for idle drift — the slot figure is a maximum
              ;; over the actor, so a failing idledrift used to name seventeen candidates and no
              ;; culprit. See *phys-cidr*. Ahead of `cclr:` for the same reason `canch:` is ahead of
              ;; `cdev:`: physics_c4_harvest and physics_c6_fill_report both read cclr TO END OF
              ;; LINE, and a second list after it would be folded into the clearance population.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cidr:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c (-> *phys-cidr* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-cidr* (+ cbase c)) 0.0))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cclr:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c (-> *phys-cclr* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-cclr* (+ cbase c)) 1000000.0))
              (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*)
              ;; ---- CYCLE-5 FOURTH WINDOW LINE --------------------------------------------------
              ;; Same rule as the other three: ONE format 0 call, because a device logcat splits a
              ;; multi-call line and every field after the split reads as absent (i.e. as zero) to a
              ;; line-based gate. And no field name here is a substring of a field on lines 1-3.
              ;; What it answers, in order: is every chain classified (the owner's "c'est du CAS PAR
              ;; CAS"), is the gravity exception armed or dormant, did the BODY chains come back to
              ;; the pose Naughty Dog modelled, did any chain end up inside the opposite leg, was
              ;; anything crushed, and — the anti-empty-zero counter — did the pendant geometry
              ;; actually get tested at all.
              (format (clear *phys-line-buf*)
                      "[HD-PHYS4] ag=~S famA=~D famB=~D unclass=~D tiltmax=~f"
                      ag
                      (-> *phys-slot-fama* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-famb* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-unclass* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-tilt* slot))
              ;; two calls, one line: `format` takes at most 8 parameters, and these all append
              ;; into the same string buffer, so the window is still emitted as ONE logcat line.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " restdevA=~f restwin=~D xheld=~D"
                      (-> *phys-slot-restdeva* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-restwin* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-xheld* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " xleg=~D lenmin=~f lensim=~f extprobe=~D modelfall=~D"
                      (-> *phys-slot-xleg* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-lenmin* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-lensim* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-extprobe* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-modelfall* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " mfmax=~f escape=~D escmax=~f"
                      (-> *phys-slot-mfmax* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-escape* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-escmax* slot))
              ;; per-chain: family, post-settle model deviation, worst length ratio. Three numbers
              ;; per chain is what turns "this actor is fine" into "chain 4 is not", which cost a
              ;; whole build cycle on Gol the last time only the slot total was printed.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " fam:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~D" c (-> *phys-cfam* (+ cbase c))))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " crestd:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c (-> *phys-crestd* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-crestd* (+ cbase c)) 0.0))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " clenr:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c (-> *phys-clenr* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-clenr* (+ cbase c)) 1000000.0))
              (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*)
              ;; ---- CYCLE-6 FIFTH WINDOW LINE ---------------------------------------------------
              ;; The owner's blocker: "les objets / parties ayant de la physique NE DOIVENT PAS
              ;; PASSER AU TRAVERS DU MESH DE LEUR PERSONNAGE ! QU'IMPORTE LA RAISON !"
              ;; Same one-format-call rule as lines 1-4, and no field name here is a substring of a
              ;; field on any earlier line (`chainvschain`, `ccdepth`, `injected`, `ccnmax` are all
              ;; new stems) — a nested name silently disarms a line-based gate.
              ;; chainvschain = strand-vs-strand contacts RESOLVED this window. It is the counter the
              ;;   positive control has to be able to move: run with inject= armed and it climbs,
              ;;   run disarmed and injected= is 0.
              ;; ccnmax = the largest per-chain collider list actually walked. It is the honest
              ;;   companion to the mesh-derived volumes: if it ever equals PHYS-CCMAX the list was
              ;;   truncated and some volume this chain should be tested against was dropped.
              (format (clear *phys-line-buf*)
                      "[HD-PHYS5] ag=~S chainvschain=~D ccdepth=~f injected=~D ncols=~D ccnmax=~D"
                      ag
                      (-> *phys-slot-ccc* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-cccmax* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-injected* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-ncols* slot)
                      (let ((m 0))
                        (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                          (when (> (-> *phys-ccn* (+ cbase c)) m)
                            (set! m (-> *phys-ccn* (+ cbase c)))))
                        m))
              ;; (C13) the perimeter's own three numbers, and they are the ones the owner's cycle-12
              ;; rejection asks for. ccpairs = strand-vs-strand pairs actually LINK-TESTED this
              ;; window: it used to be bounded by whatever `xchain=` had named, and is now bounded
              ;; only by which pairs can reach each other. cctrunc = chain-frames whose reachable
              ;; volume list overflowed PHYS-CCMAX, i.e. holes; it must be 0 and it is printed even
              ;; when it is, because a hole that is not printed is a hole nobody looks for.
              ;; ccnsum = the total volume count tested across every chain of the actor this window,
              ;; the thing whose absence made `resid=0` meaningless — a zero residual over a zero
              ;; perimeter is the false green this whole cycle exists to kill.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " ccpairs=~D cctrunc=~D ccnsum=~D"
                      (-> *phys-slot-ccpairs* slot)
                      (-> *phys-cctrunc* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-ccnsum* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " mfsnap=~D mfsnapmax=~f mfhard=~D"
                      (-> *phys-slot-mfsnap* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-mfsnapmax* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-mfhard* slot))
              ;; (C13b) the strand pass's own three. xveto = pushes refused because they would have
              ;; driven a link deeper into its own body; xunres/xunresmax = the strand-vs-strand
              ;; overlap this frame could NOT clear. Until this cycle the pass reported only the
              ;; contacts it HANDLED, which is the same blind spot as a body audit with no perimeter.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " xveto=~D xunres=~D xunresmax=~f"
                      (-> *phys-slot-xveto* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-xunres* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-xunresmax* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " xbres=~D xbresmax=~f"
                      (-> *phys-slot-xbres* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-xbresmax* slot))
              ;; per-chain: how many volumes it is tested against, and the radius of its first link.
              ;; A chain showing ncol=0 has nothing to hit — that is the wave-2 failure mode the
              ;; aggregate counter could not see — and lrad names the mesh-measured thickness the
              ;; strand-vs-strand test is using, so a wrong radii= line is read off the log.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " ccn:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~D" c (-> *phys-ccn* (+ cbase c))))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " lrad:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c
                        (-> *phys-lrad* (+ jbase (-> *phys-cstart* (+ cbase c))))))
              (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*)
              ;; ---- CYCLE-14 SIXTH WINDOW LINE ---------------------------------------------------
              ;; Same rules as lines 1-5: ONE format 0 call per line, and no field name here is a
              ;; substring of a field on any earlier line (meshpen/mraw/mfix/meshtested/resjerk and
              ;; crun: are all new stems — `resid=` cannot match `resjerk=`, `maxpen=` cannot match
              ;; `meshpen=`, `cres:` cannot match `crun:`).
              ;;   resjerk    worst single-frame total resolution displacement of any link (C14-D)
              ;;   meshpen    residual mesh-surface penetration AFTER the resolve, authored-floored
              ;;              — the owner's blocker measured where his eyes are (C14-B)
              ;;   mraw       the same figure BEFORE the resolve: the positive control's needle
              ;;   mfix       mesh-sample pushes applied; meshtested samples tested — 0 = the
              ;;              audit did not run, and a meshpen next to meshtested=0 is an empty
              ;;              zero exactly as resid=0/push=0 was
              ;;   crun:      per-chain window max deviation ON LOCOMOTION FRAMES ONLY — the
              ;;              hairrun/chestrun floors read this list (C14-A)
              (format (clear *phys-line-buf*)
                      "[HD-PHYS6] ag=~S resjerk=~f meshpen=~f mraw=~f mfix=~D meshtested=~D"
                      ag
                      (-> *phys-slot-resjerk* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-meshpen* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-mraw* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-mfix* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-mtested* slot))
              ;; separate append: a GOAL call takes at most 8 parameters, and the line above is
              ;; already at eight.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " respath=~f" (-> *phys-slot-respath* slot))
              ;; (cycle-15) the slew bound and resjerk's attribution. New stems, none of them a
              ;; substring of any field printed above or on lines 1-5: jgcut/jtfall/rjup/rjdn/rjtm.
              (format *phys-line-buf* " jgcut=~D jtfall=~D rjup=~f rjdn=~f rjtm=~f"
                      (-> *phys-slot-jgcut* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-jtfall* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-rjup* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-rjdn* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-rjtm* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " rjpre=~f jdcut=~D jdmax=~f"
                      (-> *phys-slot-rjpre* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-jdcut* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-jdmax* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " crun:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c (-> *phys-crun* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-crun* (+ cbase c)) 0.0))
              (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*)
              ;; ---- CYCLE-16 SEVENTH WINDOW LINE -------------------------------------------------
              ;; Its own line rather than more fields on line 6, for two reasons that are not style:
              ;; *phys-line-buf* is 2048 chars and line 6 already carries a 24-entry list, and the
              ;; leg script reads a per-chain list by taking the substring from its stem to the end
              ;; of the line — so every list added after `crun:` lengthens what that scan walks.
              ;; Field stems here are new and none is a substring of any field on lines 1-6:
              ;;   simcf    chain-frames simulated this window = the DENOMINATOR of the three shares
              ;;   authcf   of those, how many the AUTHORED animation owned (suppressor 1)
              ;;   clampcf  ...how many a jerk/excursion bound acted on (suppressor 2)
              ;;   restcf   ...how many the chain was MEASURABLY AT REST. Cycle 16: this is a
              ;;            measurement, not a mechanism — the calm rest state that used to hold a
              ;;            chain still is gone, so nothing here suppresses anything and clampcf
              ;;            reads 0 because no jerk or excursion bound exists any more.
              ;;   cinr:    per chain, MEAN written motion over the frames its own anchor was
              ;;            DRIVEN (not just locomotion). This is the inertness verdict.
              ;;   cish:    per chain, how many such frames were sampled. cish=0 = UNJUDGED.
              ;;   cvar:    per chain, MEAN per-frame |offset(t)-offset(t-1)| on locomotion frames.
              ;;            THIS is the motion floor. A welded chain reads 0 here no matter how far
              ;;            from its rest pose it is welded — which is the entire point of the line.
              ;;   cvmx:    per chain, the worst single locomotion frame
              ;;   cdsp:    per chain, spread (max-min) of the deviation over the same frames — the
              ;;            dispersion the spec calls variance; 0 with cvn>0 = a constant = INERT
              ;;   cvn:     locomotion frames sampled per chain. cvn=0 means NOT MEASURED HERE, and
              ;;            it must never be read as calm: it is this line's tested=0 confession.
              (format (clear *phys-line-buf*)
                      "[HD-PHYS7] ag=~S simcf=~D authcf=~D clampcf=~D restcf=~D"
                      ag
                      (-> *phys-slot-simcf* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-authhold* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-clampcf* slot)
                      (-> *phys-slot-rested* slot))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cvar:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c
                        (if (> (-> *phys-cvn* (+ cbase c)) 0)
                            (/ (-> *phys-cvsum* (+ cbase c)) (the float (-> *phys-cvn* (+ cbase c))))
                            0.0)))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cvmx:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c (-> *phys-cvmax* (+ cbase c))))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cdsp:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c
                        (- (-> *phys-cdmax* (+ cbase c)) (-> *phys-cdmin* (+ cbase c)))))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cinr:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~f" c
                        (if (> (-> *phys-cish* (+ cbase c)) 0)
                            (/ (-> *phys-civ* (+ cbase c)) (the float (-> *phys-cish* (+ cbase c))))
                            0.0)))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cish:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~D" c (-> *phys-cish* (+ cbase c))))
              (format *phys-line-buf* " cvn:")
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (format *phys-line-buf* " ~D=~D" c (-> *phys-cvn* (+ cbase c)))
                (set! (-> *phys-cvsum* (+ cbase c)) 0.0)
                (set! (-> *phys-cvn* (+ cbase c)) 0)
                (set! (-> *phys-cvmax* (+ cbase c)) 0.0)
                (set! (-> *phys-cdmin* (+ cbase c)) 0.0)
                (set! (-> *phys-cdmax* (+ cbase c)) 0.0)
                (set! (-> *phys-cish* (+ cbase c)) 0)
                (set! (-> *phys-civ* (+ cbase c)) 0.0))
              (format 0 "~S~%" *phys-line-buf*)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-simcf* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-clampcf* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-resjerk* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-jgcut* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-jtfall* slot) 0)
                                  (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjpre* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-jdcut* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-jdmax* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjup* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjdn* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-rjtm* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-respath* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-meshpen* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-mraw* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-mfix* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-mtested* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-ccc* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-cccmax* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-injected* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-ccpairs* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-cctrunc* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-ccnsum* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-mfsnap* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-mfsnapmax* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-mfhard* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-xbres* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-xbresmax* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-xveto* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-xunres* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-xunresmax* slot) 0.0)
              ;; (C13) the per-chain reachable-volume count is a WINDOW MAX, so it has to be cleared
              ;; with the window: carried over, a chain that reached 30 volumes once would keep
              ;; claiming 30 long after it had stopped reaching anything.
              ;; (C13) -1, not 0. cncol changed MEANING this cycle: it used to be "how many
              ;; volumes NAMED this chain", a property of the data that was the same on every frame,
              ;; and it is now "how many volumes this chain REACHED", which is only defined on the
              ;; frames the chain was simulatable at all. A rig bound but never posed (a parked
              ;; spawn, a stock actor a companion is covering) has zero-length chains, never enters
              ;; the perimeter rebuild, and would read as a chain with nothing to hit — which is a
              ;; real defect wearing a false positive. -1 means "never asked"; the rebuild raises it
              ;; to at least 0 the first time it runs, and only 0 counts as nomask.
              (dotimes (c (-> *phys-slot-nchains* slot))
                (set! (-> *phys-cncol* (+ cbase c)) -1))
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-fama* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-famb* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-unclass* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-tilt* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-restdeva* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-restwin* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-xheld* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-xleg* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-lenmin* slot) 1000000.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-lensim* slot) 1000000.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-gsamp* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-lensim* slot) 1000000.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-gsamp* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-extprobe* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-idle* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-settletime* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-unsettled* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-freering* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-idleobs* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-slept* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-arrn* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-authhold* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-autheng* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-authrel* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-authmax* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-reseed* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-burst* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-holdmax* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-jitter* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-rested* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-clamped* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-modelfall* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-mfmax* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-escape* slot) 0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-escmax* slot) 0.0)
    (set! (-> *phys-slot-stickmax* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-frames* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-resets* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxdev* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxvel* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-anchmove* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-pushouts* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxpen* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-resid* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-maxresid* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-rootdev* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-freeroot* slot) 0.0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-reglue* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-desc* slot) 0)
              (set! (-> *phys-slot-nopose* slot) 0)))))))
  (none))

;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; HD COMPANION entry points. These three keep their exact names and signatures — jak-hd.gc calls
;; them from init-jak-hd / do-joint-math! / deactivate and knows nothing about the slot pool. All
;; the companion-specific knowledge (the k->e prep table, the *hd-ag-names* params key, hd-joints)
;; lives HERE and nowhere in the solver.
;; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defun jak-hd-physics-init ((obj jak-hd))
  "claim a sim slot for this companion and resolve its chains from the data file against the live
  HD jgeo. The parent table comes from the generated k->e prep column (khd-par, 255 = root).
  Reload the params file on every init: pushing a new physics_chains.txt to the device then
  switching a LOOK (or toggling ENHANCED MODELS) re-reads everything — fast iteration."
  ;; cycle-2 defect E: prove the physics menu rows are still distinct from the mesh-browser
  ;; button. Done here because this runs on every companion spawn, physics toggle on OR off.
  (physics-menu-static-audit!)
  (when (and (nonzero? (-> obj draw)) (nonzero? (-> obj draw jgeo)))
    (let ((slot (phys-slot-claim (the int (-> obj pid)) 0)))
      (cond
        ((< slot 0)
         (format 0 "[HD-PHYS] no free sim slot — physics disabled for this companion~%"))
        (else
         (pc-physics-reload)
         (phys-fill-par-from-table! slot (-> obj khd-par) (-> obj hd-joints))
         (phys-slot-bind! slot (-> obj draw) (-> *hd-ag-names* (-> obj entry)) (-> obj hd-joints))))))
  (none))

(defun jak-hd-physics-step ((obj jak-hd))
  "the companion's per-frame step, called from its do-joint-math! override right after
  fill-jak-hd-bones!. Stamping the slot BEFORE the step is what makes the stock-actor rider's
  once-per-frame guard and its age-based slot reclamation work off a single counter."
  (let ((slot (phys-slot-find (the int (-> obj pid)))))
    (when (>= slot 0)
      (set! (-> *phys-slot-stamp* slot) (the int (current-time)))
      (phys-slot-step! slot (-> obj draw) (-> *hd-ag-names* (-> obj entry)) (-> obj hd-joints))))
  (none))

(defun jak-hd-physics-release ((obj jak-hd))
  "free this companion's sim slot (called from deactivate)."
  (dotimes (s PHYS-SLOTS)
    (when (= (-> *phys-slot-pid* s) (the int (-> obj pid)))
      (phys-slot-free! s)))
  (none))

;; ================================================================================================
;; WAVE 2 (owner 2026-08-05 16:50 / 2026-08-06) — PHYSICS ON THE WHOLE CAST
;; ================================================================================================
;; The HD companions own a skeleton of their own; every OTHER character in jak1 is a stock
;; process-drawable with no companion and no prep step. The sim core above is rig-agnostic — it
;; resolves chains by joint NAME and walks a parent table — so a stock actor needs nothing but a
;; POST-ANIM HOOK: process-drawable::do-joint-math! calls phys-rider-post! once the bones are final,
;; and the same solver runs IN PLACE on the actor's own bones. This is the joint-mod-class hook the
;; phase spec asks for, at the one point in the frame where every rig is guaranteed posed.
;;
;; Chains are declared per RIG in physics_chains.txt keyed by the JOINT-GEO name ("sage-lod0-jg"):
;; jgeo is one object per art group and survives LOD switches, mgeo does not (lod-set! swaps it).
;;
;; NO bone injection is needed for the inherited sites — the shipped rigs already carry the chain
;; joints (Maia's 8-link ponytail, Gol's four capes, the geologist's braids, every sage's beard,
;; the fisherman's belly). Where a rig genuinely has no joint for an owner-listed site, that is
;; documented in the phase report with the evidence, never silently dropped.

(define *phys-cover-pid* (new 'static 'array int32 16))
(define *phys-cover-stamp* (new 'static 'array int32 16))
;; DISCOVERY LOG. The rider binds a stock actor by looking its RIG up in physics_chains.txt, and a
;; rig that is simply not in the file is indistinguishable, from the outside, from a rider that is
;; broken. So the first time each distinct rig is seen, name it and print the chain count the params
;; store answered with. `chains=0` = that character has no config yet (a data question);
;; nothing at all = the hook never ran (a code question). Keyed on the jgeo POINTER purely to avoid
;; repeating the line — a stale pointer after a level unload costs one extra log line, nothing else.
(defconstant PHYS-RIDER-SEEN 40)
(define *phys-seen-jgeo* (new 'static 'array int32 40))
(define *phys-seen-n* 0)
(define *phys-rider-bound* 0)     ;; rider slots bound this session
(define *phys-rider-full* 0)      ;; slot-starvation events
(define *phys-rider-active* 0)    ;; rider steps in the current window
(define *phys-rider-frames* 0)
(define *phys-rider-last* 0)

(defun phys-note-covered! ((pid int))
  "an HD companion is retargeting FROM this driver's bones this frame. A rider must not also write
  them (it would feed the companion a perturbed source pose) and the stock mesh is suppressed
  anyway, so the companion's own chains do the work."
  (let ((now (the int (current-time)))
        (slot -1))
    (dotimes (i 16)
      (when (and (< slot 0) (= (-> *phys-cover-pid* i) pid))
        (set! slot i)))
    (when (< slot 0)
      (dotimes (i 16)
        (when (and (< slot 0) (> (- now (-> *phys-cover-stamp* i)) 8))
          (set! slot i))))
    (when (>= slot 0)
      (set! (-> *phys-cover-pid* slot) pid)
      (set! (-> *phys-cover-stamp* slot) now)))
  (none))

(defun phys-covered? ((pid int))
  (let ((now (the int (current-time)))
        (r #f))
    (dotimes (i 16)
      (when (and (= (-> *phys-cover-pid* i) pid)
                 (<= (- now (-> *phys-cover-stamp* i)) 8))
        (set! r #t)))
    r))

(defun phys-rider-post! ((obj process-drawable))
  "post-anim chain sim for STOCK actors. Called from process-drawable::do-joint-math! for every
  drawable in the game, so the fast path out is the whole design: four pointer tests, one type
  compare and one enabled-check when the feature is off or the actor has no rig."
  (when (and (nonzero? (-> obj draw))
             (nonzero? (-> obj skel))
             (nonzero? (-> obj draw jgeo))
             (nonzero? (-> obj draw skeleton))
             (not (logtest? (-> obj draw status) (draw-status hidden no-anim)))
             (!= (-> obj type) jak-hd)
             (> (pc-physics-enabled) 0))
    ;; one window tick per frame, shared by every rider
    (let ((now (the int (current-time))))
      (when (!= now *phys-rider-last*)
        (set! *phys-rider-last* now)
        ;; The physics menu-row audit used to hang off the COMPANION spawn, so a session with
        ;; ENHANCED MODELS off never ran it — and that is precisely a session where the menu still
        ;; shows both physics rows. It is self-capping (*phys-menu-audited*), so calling it from the
        ;; rider tick as well simply makes the audit independent of whether HD models are on.
        (physics-menu-static-audit!)
        (+! *phys-rider-frames* 1)
        (when (>= *phys-rider-frames* 300)
          (format 0 "[HD-PHYS-RIDER] window: bound=~D active=~D slots-full=~D~%"
                  *phys-rider-bound* *phys-rider-active* *phys-rider-full*)
          (set! *phys-rider-frames* 0)
          (set! *phys-rider-active* 0)
          (set! *phys-rider-full* 0))))
    (let* ((pid (the int (-> obj pid)))
           (slot (phys-slot-find pid)))
      (cond
        ;; --- HD-OWNED ACTOR ---------------------------------------------------------------------
        ;; An actor an HD companion is (or is about to be) retargeting FROM must never be written by
        ;; a rider: the companion reads these very bones, so a chain-perturbed source pose would
        ;; shake the HD model too.
        ;; The first test is the load-bearing one, and it is STATELESS: same question the spawner
        ;; asks — "with enhanced models on, does this driver model have an HD replacement for the
        ;; current look?". The per-frame cover STAMP alone was not enough: measured on the village1
        ;; leg, Jak and Daxter re-bound 98 times each in 110 s because a companion's cover lapses
        ;; between despawn and respawn, and every one of those gaps let a rider grab the driver for
        ;; a while. With the stateless test the answer cannot flicker with process lifetime.
        ;; The stamp is kept as a second net for anything the name test cannot see.
        ((or (and (-> *pc-settings* recharged-enhanced-models?)
                  (nonzero? (-> obj draw mgeo))
                  (>= (hd-desired-entry-for-mgeo (-> obj draw mgeo name)) 0))
             (phys-covered? pid))
         (when (and (>= slot 0) (nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-rider* slot)))
           (phys-slot-free! slot)))
        ((>= slot 0)
         (when (nonzero? (-> *phys-slot-rider* slot))
           ;; ONCE PER FRAME. Several states call do-joint-math! more than once per frame
           ;; (logic-target has three call sites, ja-post has another); stepping twice would
           ;; double the sim's time step for those actors only.
           (let ((now (the int (current-time))))
             (when (!= now (-> *phys-slot-stamp* slot))
               (set! (-> *phys-slot-stamp* slot) now)
               (+! *phys-rider-active* 1)
               (phys-slot-step! slot (-> obj draw) (-> obj draw jgeo name) (-> obj draw jgeo length))))))
        (else
         ;; is this RIG configured? One map lookup on a short string per unbound drawable per frame —
         ;; deliberately NOT cached on the jgeo pointer: a level unload can hand the same address to
         ;; a different rig, and a stale negative would silently un-physics a character.
         (let ((nch (pc-physics-num-chains (-> obj draw jgeo name)))
               (key (the int (-> obj draw jgeo)))
               (known 0))
           (dotimes (i *phys-seen-n*)
             (when (= (-> *phys-seen-jgeo* i) key)
               (set! known 1)))
           (when (and (zero? known) (< *phys-seen-n* PHYS-RIDER-SEEN))
             (set! (-> *phys-seen-jgeo* *phys-seen-n*) key)
             (+! *phys-seen-n* 1)
             (format 0 "[HD-PHYS-RIDER] rig ~S chains=~D~%" (-> obj draw jgeo name) nch))
         (when (> nch 0)
           (let ((s (phys-slot-claim pid 1)))
             (cond
               ((< s 0)
                (+! *phys-rider-full* 1))
               (else
                (phys-fill-par-from-jgeo! s (-> obj draw jgeo) (-> obj draw jgeo length))
                (phys-slot-bind! s (-> obj draw) (-> obj draw jgeo name) (-> obj draw jgeo length))
                (+! *phys-rider-bound* 1))))))))))
  (none))

) ;; #when FLAG_PHYSICS
